PVD("cambodia_ndp_2009-2013",{"docs":["","CMB NDP 2009 2013"],"s":{"1":[[1,"14","1","Rectangular Strategy Phase II Implementation","the Rectangular Strategy Phase II was revealed as an updated and fine-tuned version of the earlier Rectangular Strategy to develop systematic, coherent, interrelated, complimentary, and simplified priority packages within key sectors, which outlines in detail the policy priorities for the implementation of the RGC's reform programs to re-build institutional capacity, strengthen socio-economic infrastructure, and to create an enabling environment to attract investments from both domestic and foreign sources in order to create employment opportunities for Cambodians, to reduce poverty, and to develop key sectors of the economy.",""],[1,"14","1","National Strategic Development Plan Implementation","This strategy will be implemented mainly through the National Strategic Development Plan",""],[1,"14","2","NSDP Update 2009-2013 Preparation","The NSDP Update, 2009-2013 is being prepared to accomplish two primary goals.",""],[1,"15","4","Development Expenditure Programming and Resource Allocation Framework","Programming or allocation of total development expenditures based on: (i) information complied through the bottom-up planning process that covers all aspects of social and economic development needs; (ii) information from the top-down planning process that establishes the parameters of overall resource availability from the national budget and information on \"capital\" investments that will be required to achieve the projected economic growth targets; and (iii) estimates of the total amount of resources, from all sources, that are likely to be available or would need to be mobilized to achieve the Plan targets.",""],[1,"15","5","NSDP Update Consultation and Input Preparation Guidelines","the Ministry of Planning provided detailed policy and technical guidelines to Ministries and Agencies on how to prepare their inputs for NSDP Update.","Ministry of Planning"],[1,"15","5","TWG-Based Technical and Logistical Support for NSDP Inputs","it tasked the Lead Donor Facilitators of the TWG to work with all development partners to ensure that they are ready and able to provide technical and logistic support, if needed, through the TWG mechanism to their concerned Ministry/Agency in the preparation of inputs for NSDP Update.","Ministry of Planning"],[1,"19","4","Annual Progress Reporting for NSDP Implementation","To ensure effective monitoring of the implementation of NSDP 2006-2010, regular Annual Progress Reports have been prepared and widely disseminated by the Ministry of Planning.","Ministry of Planning"],[1,"21","1","Strengthened Inter-Ministerial Coordination for Development Programme Delivery","there is an urgent need to strengthen communication, coordination and cooperation between relevant ministries/institutions to ensure that development programmes are more speedily and effectively designed and implemented",""],[1,"38","12","Review and Reorientation of Ongoing Programmes","Many TWGs are still to commence review of all ongoing programmes to align and reorient them to NSDP priorities as well as to PIPs",""],[1,"108","2","Rectangular Strategy Implementation Acceleration and Policy Refinement","the Royal Government to improve and refine, its prioritized policies and to accelerate the implementation of this policy agenda during this legislature.",""],[1,"108","3","Continued Implementation of Rectangular Strategy Phase II","Continued implementation of the \"Rectangular Strategy-Phase II\" is a further step to achieve the \"Cambodian Millennium Development Goals\".",""]],"2":[[1,"29","1","Local Democratic Governance and Administration Reform","The Royal Government believes that establishing and promoting democratic development at provincial/municipal, district/Khan and commune/Sangkat levels can best achieve the expansion of democratic governance.",""],[1,"29","2","Decentralization and De-concentration Reform Implementation","To implement the D&D reforms an inter-agency committee that is Chaired by the Ministry of Interior (MOI), the National Committee for Sub- National Democratic Development (NCDD), has been established to provide overall direction and to coordinate the implementation of the D&D reforms.","Ministry of Interior (MOI)"],[1,"29","2","Regulatory Framework for Sub-national Law Implementation","The NCDD is now working on the formulation of a regulatory framework to implement these Laws, in particular on the regulations for the demarcation of administrative boundaries at sub-national levels and regulations on the composition of membership of Capital City Council, Provincial Councils, Municipal Councils, District and Khan Councils.",""],[1,"29","4","Technical Support for Commune/Sangkat Council Capacity Building","The NCDD is also coordinating technical support and assistance to improve the capacity of commune/sangkat council members to manage their respective commune/sangkat affairs effectively in accordance with the provisions of the law on the administration of Commune/Sangkat.",""],[1,"29","4","National Program for Sub-National Democratic Development","It is now working on formulating a National Program on the sub-national democratic development that will outlines the work plan for the enforcement of the Law on Administrative Management of the Capital, Provinces, Municipalities, Districts and Khans and the short-, medium-, and long-term D&D reform policies to be implemented from 2010 to 2019.",""],[1,"30","1","Decentralization and Deconcentration Reform Implementation","implementation of D&D reform policies and the enforcement of the Law on Administrative Management of Capital, Provinces, Municipalities, Districts and Khans.",""],[1,"30","2","Comprehensive Human Resources Management System for Sub-national Institutions","developing capacity of the newly created sub- national institutions to deliver programs and services under their mandate, is still a major challenge that will need to be dealt with within the framework of a new comprehensive human resources management system.",""],[1,"30","3","Sub-national Council Human Resource Development System","the long-term vision of the new human resource development (HRD) system for local administration is to have each sub-national council take full responsibility to train its civil servants under its own well-established HRD system.",""],[1,"32","2","Sub-National Public Administration Strengthening and Decentralization Reform Coordination","The Ministry of Interior (MOI) has been playing three major roles: (i) managing the sub-national public administration institutions; (ii) ensuring internal security of the nation, and public order through the National Police Forces (NFP); and (iii) leading and coordinating the implementation of RGC's Decentralization and De-concentration Reform Program (D&D), as the Chair of the National Committee for Sub-National Democratic Development (NCDD).","Ministry of Interior (MOI)"],[1,"47","8","Decentralisation and Deconcentration of Public Service Delivery","The decentralisation and deconcentration of public services delivery, support for participatory decentralised-based programmes, and the provision of credit to households and small businesses are some of the examples of Royal Government's efforts in this sector.",""],[1,"47","8","Participatory Decentralised Rural Development Programmes","The decentralisation and deconcentration of public services delivery, support for participatory decentralised-based programmes, and the provision of credit to households and small businesses are some of the examples of Royal Government's efforts in this sector.",""],[1,"91","9","Decentralization and De-concentration Support Measures","Supporting the RGC Strategic Framework for Decentralization and De-concentration.",""],[1,"114","3","Decentralization and De-concentration Policy Implementation","The Royal Government will further pursue the Decentralization and De-concentration policy by developing legal and regulatory framework and laying out new measures to ensure effective implementation of the \"Organic Law on the Administrative Management of the Capital, Provinces, Municipalities, Districts and Khans\"",""],[1,"114","3","Sub-National Action Plans for Delegation of Powers","Each ministry and agency will prepare concrete Action Plans for the delegation of power and functions to the sub- national levels.",""],[1,"114","3","Decentralized Financial Management Reform","Decentralized financial management will also be implemented in a phased and flexible manner over the medium term to allow for the capacity building at the sub national levels.",""],[1,"114","3","National Implementation Program for Sub-National Democratic Development","The National Committee on Sub-National Democratic Development is preparing a 10-year National Implementation Program.",""],[1,"117","18","Program for Sub-National Democratic Development","the National Committee for Sub- National Democratic Development (NCDD) is now developing a ten-year implementation program called the Program for Sub-National Democratic Development.",""],[1,"118","2","Sub-national Administration Capacity Strengthening","The second phase of also three year period, 2013 to 2015, will focus on consolidating and improving those structures and framework in order to guarantee that the sub-national administrations have the ability to set and implement the policies for their respective localities to improve the public service deliveries.",""],[1,"118","3","Program Component and Activity Adjustment","The third phase of four-year period, 2016 to 2019, will focus on the alteration of the components and activities of the program in order to ensure greater success and enhance the democratic development through lessons learnt and experiences drawn from the first and second phases.",""]],"3":[[1,"123","2","Cambodia Development Forum Coordination Mechanism","The Royal Government of the Fourth Legislature will continue to strengthen the mechanism of \"Cambodia Development Cooperation Forum -CDCF\" and \"Government- Private Sector Forum\" and consider the possibility to transform all these fora into the \"Cambodia Development Forum\"",""],[1,"123","2","Government-Development Partner Coordination Committee and Technical Working Groups Strengthening","The existing coordination mechanisms between the Royal Government and Development Partner Community (Government-Development Partner Coordination Committee- GDCC and the Technical Working Groups-TWGs) will be reviewed and further strengthened in order to enhance efficiency, especially on technical cooperation for development of human resources and institutional capacity and to strengthen cooperation among all relevant stakeholders.",""],[1,"123","3","Accra Agenda for Action Implementation","The Royal Government is committed to implement \"the Accra Agenda for Action\"",""],[1,"123","4","Comprehensive Cambodia Development Forum","The Royal Government envisages a comprehensive Cambodia Development Forum (CDF) which not only ensures that all development stakeholders, including the development partner community, the private sector, civil society organizations, and other concerned actors, are brought together to discuss issues related to both public and private sector development, but also that there is a close linkage between public and private sector investments, and more importantly, that public and private sector investments are mutually reinforcing and contribute to achieving the longer-term objective of socio-economic development of the country.",""],[1,"124","1","Cambodia Development Cooperation Forum Coordination and Joint Monitoring Mechanism","The Cambodia Development Cooperation Forum (CDCF) so far embodies the highest level partnerships between the Royal Government and the development partner community (including NGOs), where dialogue on strategic socio- economic development policies, guided by the Rectangular Strategy, takes place and the implementation of those policies is jointly monitored and associated with a financing framework that ensures development results and mutual accountability.",""],[1,"124","1","Review and Redesign of Dialogue and Participation Frameworks","This diversity of audience, and the associated different frameworks of dialogue and participation that have been established, will be critically reviewed and considered by the Royal Government to lay a foundation to move toward the CDF, and to ensure that the structures and formats of the CDF reflect the integrity of the diverse audience, coordination and effectiveness and efficiency.",""],[1,"124","2","Alignment of Development Assistance and Public Investment Budget with National Priorities","there is a need to closely link development assistance resources and the Royal Government's public investment budget with the priorities identified in the National Strategic Development Plan.",""],[1,"124","4","Government-Development Partner Coordination and Review Mechanism","The Government-Development Partner Coordination Committee (GDCC) and Technical Working Group (TWG) mechanisms will continue to provide the principal modes of dialogue between the Royal Government and its development partners.",""],[1,"125","1","Aid Effectiveness Partnership Mechanisms","The Royal Government believes that the effectiveness and efficiency of the partnership mechanisms are guided by, and consistent with, the Government's continued commitment to the Paris Declaration on Aid Effectiveness (2005) and the implementation of the commitments included in the Accra Agenda for Action (2008).",""],[1,"125","2","Technical Working Group Support for Partnership Dialogue","The Technical Working Groups will be appropriately supported to enable them to lead dialogue with development partners on key policies and strategies within their sector and reform areas.",""],[1,"125","3","Strengthening of Technical Working Group Monitoring Mechanism","The TWG mechanism will be strengthened to support the monitoring of the implementation of development cooperation activities in the sector or area that they support.",""],[1,"125","4","ODA Information Quality and Coordination Support","the Royal Government will continue to work with development partners and NGOs to ensure timely, accurate and complete ODA information provision, and to support line ministries and TWGs in their efforts to use this information to strengthen their own planning and coordination processes as well as meeting their obligations to report to the national level.",""],[1,"125","5","Strategic Framework for Development Cooperation Management Implementation","The Royal Government will continue to work with development partners to implement the Strategic Framework to ensure that complete and accurate information on external assistance is available to be incorporated into the national planning and budgeting processes.",""],[1,"126","3","Implementation of Accra Agenda for Action Commitments","The Royal Government's committed adaptation and implementation of the commitments in the AAA and the global commitments that will come out of the next High Level Forum in Seoul in 2011 will aim to ensure strengthened national ownership and leadership, more accountable partnership with all development partners and to enhance development results.",""],[1,"126","4","Aid Effectiveness Prioritization and Joint Monitoring Process","The Royal Government will continue to strengthen the joint process of identifying, agreeing, and monitoring jointly with development partners the implementation of the aid effectiveness priorities that are relevant to sector challenges and focused on achieving results.",""],[1,"126","5","Increase Net Resource Transfers for Development Programmes","The Royal Government will work to achieve this in context of a less fragmented aid environment and an increased use of government systems in delivery of development cooperation activities.",""],[1,"126","6","Capacity Development-Oriented Technical Cooperation Alignment","The Royal Government will ensure that all externally supported technical cooperation will be primarily directed to develop national human and institutional capacities and systems in a manner that is consistent with Royal Government's capacity development strategies and policies",""],[1,"127","1","Technical Cooperation Guideline Implementation","The Guideline on Technical Cooperation will be implemented and used to manage these resources at sectoral level as well as to guide support for implementing the core reform programmes of the Royal Government.",""],[1,"127","2","Programme-Based Aid Delivery Approach","The Royal Government encourages the use of programme-based approaches to effectively exercise ownership and leadership over the implementation of national policy priorities supported by development partners, promote stronger partnership and ensure development results and accountability.",""],[1,"127","3","Inclusive Results-Focused Development Partnership Dialogue","The Royal Government considers partnerships with all development partners an important policy priority critical for the successful implementation of the Rectangular Strategy Phase II, and is committed to an inclusive, robust and results-focused dialogue.",""],[1,"127","3","Strengthening Development Partnership Mechanisms","Further investments will be made to strengthen the partnership mechanisms, including working with all development partners to ensure that appropriate resources and competencies are in place to make effective use of these opportunities to review progress, identify challenges and respond in a partnership-based and results-focused manner.",""],[1,"184","1","Partnership Strengthening for Development Program Delivery","The RGC will further strengthen and broaden the nature and scope of partnerships within Royal Government's institutions, with external development cooperation partners, national and international Non-Government Organizations, and other civil society stakeholders to maximize the benefits for the people of Cambodia of the resources that will be available for development programs.",""],[1,"184","2","Public Financial Management Harmonization and Aid Coordination Strengthening","The Royal Government is taking concrete actions to further strengthen and refine the harmonization of planning, public investment expenditures and development cooperation financing among RGC institutions within the framework of RGC's Public Financial Management Reform Program.",""],[1,"187","7","Budget Support for Development Cooperation Financing","RGC would like to see its development cooperation partners take urgent actions to deliver their development cooperation financing resources through \"budget support\" linked to measurable qualitative and quantitative performance in each chosen sector.",""],[1,"187","8","Sector-Wide and Program-Based Development Cooperation Approaches","RGC urges its development cooperation partners to provide support to the development of sector-wide or program-based approaches for the key sectors of the economy and to deliver their assistance in a coordinated manner to implement the sector-wide programs to achieve cohesion and synergy and to avoid overlap and/or duplication.",""],[1,"187","8","Strengthening Sectoral Technical Working Groups","RGC recognizes that the operations of the sectoral TWGs need to be reviewed and strengthened to carry out this important task.",""],[1,"187","9","Strengthening of Technical Working Groups Mechanism","RGC will work with its development cooperation partners to strengthen the existing Technical Working Groups (TWGs) mechanism in order to enhance efficiency, especially on technical cooperation for the development of human resources and institutional capacity and to strengthen cooperation among all relevant stakeholders;",""],[1,"188","1","Restriction of TWG Membership to Financing Partners","Limiting the membership of external development cooperation partners in a TWG to those who are delivering financial support to the TWG sector.",""],[1,"188","2","Technical Working Group Participation Improvement","To improve the quality and level of discussion at the Technical Working Groups, RGC would like to see the participation of personnel who are technically qualified to provide advice and support in the sector of the TWG.",""],[1,"188","3","Development Cooperation Alignment and Aid Effectiveness Initiative","RGC will continue to urge its development cooperation partners to strive to ensure that their assistance is fully aligned to achieving NSDP Update's priority policies at a detailed operational level and not just at a broad thematic level.",""],[1,"188","3","Reallocation of Development Cooperation Resources to Priority Areas","RGC also urges development cooperation partners to speedily reallocate resources away from less priority areas now receiving funds, make a serious effort to significantly reduce various forms of \"free standing technical assistance\" and work towards achieving a greater \"net real transfer\" of development resources to the targeted vulnerable and poor beneficiaries, and to strengthen capacity of RGC institutions to deliver their programs and services efficiently to achieve CMDGs targets.",""],[1,"188","3","Institutional Capacity Strengthening for Service Delivery","RGC also urges development cooperation partners to speedily reallocate resources away from less priority areas now receiving funds, make a serious effort to significantly reduce various forms of \"free standing technical assistance\" and work towards achieving a greater \"net real transfer\" of development resources to the targeted vulnerable and poor beneficiaries, and to strengthen capacity of RGC institutions to deliver their programs and services efficiently to achieve CMDGs targets.",""],[1,"188","4","Planning and Development Cooperation Harmonization Measures","the Royal Government is taking concrete measures to strengthen and refine harmonization of planning, public investment expenditures planning, and allocation and utilization of development cooperation resources.",""],[1,"188","5","Review of Planning and Public Investment Coordination Mechanisms","Review the roles of RGC institutions and the mechanisms and approaches pertaining to the planning process, and the process for managing, coordinating and implementing public investment expenditures and development cooperation resources.",""],[1,"188","6","Public Investment and Development Cooperation Harmonization Measures","Propose measures to harmonize public investment expenditures and allocation and utilization of development cooperation resources to ensure consistency between these two processes in order to prepare a sound and inclusive National Budget expenditure plan that is consistent with the Rectangular Strategy II, the National Strategic Development Plan, and Sectoral Strategies as outlined in the Action Plan on Harmonization, Alignment and PFMRP.",""],[1,"189","2","Development Cooperation Disbursement Analysis and Feedback Mechanism","the data collected annually by RGC from development cooperation partners on actual and planned disbursements of their assistance will be analyzed by ministry/agency and each ministry/agency will be provided this information to: (i) review and verify that the information on disbursements are reported for their ministry/agency, and (ii) provide feedback on programs/projects financed that are aligned with NSDP priorities and those that are not.",""],[1,"194","3","Sub-Group of the TWG-PPR","the MOP had established a Sub-Group of the TWG-PPR, Chaired by MOP.","MOP"]],"4":[[1,"130","1","Land Reform Program","The Royal Government's land reform program is focused on measures to strengthen land management, land distribution and land use, to ensure the security of land ownership, to eradicate illegal land holding, and to prevent concentration of unused land in few hands.",""],[1,"130","2","Land Reform Legal and Regulatory Framework Development","During the Fourth Legislature, the Royal Government will continue implementing land reforms within the framework of the Land Law and the existing land policy by developing additional legal and regulatory framework such as the Law on Expropriation, the Law on Pre-emption and Land Development, the Law on Construction and Urbanization and the National Construction Standards.",""],[1,"130","3","State-Owned Land Management and Legal Enforcement Measures","The Royal Government will review and take necessary measures to increase the efficiency in the management and utilization of state-owned unused land and take legal actions with regard to illegal holding of state-owned land by private individuals.",""],[1,"130","3","State-Owned Asset Inventory Completion","The Royal Government will accelerate the completion of the inventory of the state-owned immoveable assets.",""],[1,"130","3","Single Window for Systematic Land Registration","It will further speed up the systematic land registration by establishing a Single Window to ensure transparency.",""],[1,"130","3","Priority Land Registration in Conflict-Free and Indigenous Areas","It will accord priority to the land conflict-free areas and areas inhabited by indigenous communities in order to reduce land conflict, ensure security of land ownership and eliminate illegal land holding.",""],[1,"130","3","Land Conflict Resolution Mechanisms","The Royal Government will continue to resolve land conflicts by using legal mechanisms to ensure justice coupled with the out-of- court conflict settlement mechanism.",""],[1,"130","3","Land Ownership Rights for Poor and Vulnerable Households","The Royal Government attaches priority to granting land ownership rights to poor households and vulnerable groups for housing, farming and small businesses.",""],[1,"131","1","Land Rights Registration and Dispute Resolution Programme","Continue the registration of ownership and other rights on all immovable properties (state and private property), transferring rights on those property, preventing and solving land disputes to enhance the security of land tenure and ensure an efficiently functioning land market.",""],[1,"131","2","Land Management Planning and Mapping Reform","Speed up the process of planning for all scales and levels of land management and mapping state land in all towns and districts",""],[1,"131","5","Land Administration and Land Law Reform","Continue fastening the development of policy and legal frameworks related to the reinforcement of undertaking land law and other relevant legislation to land administration task, land management and construction and land distribution performance.",""],[1,"131","6","Comprehensive Land Policy Paper Development","Developing the cuacnt Interim Paper of Strategic framework for Land Policy to a Comprehensive Land Policy Paper, (White paper)",""],[1,"131","7","Land Law and Regulatory Framework Strengthening","Developing and strengthening law practice and regulatory framework such as Law on Expropriation, Law on Demarcation and Mapping, Law on Construction, Code of Urbanization, Law on Pre- emption, Disaffecting Law, Law on Farming Land, and other additional regulatory frameworks concerning Land transfer, Land consolidation, Land sub-division, Land valuation, Land market, Construction standards, as well as amendments of some articles within Laws and some legal norms relevant to land law, taxation law, law on land management, urbanization and construction pursuant to the nation's progress.",""],[1,"132","2","Unified State Immovable Property Inventory System","Gradually establish a clear and complete inventory of State immovable properties (lands and buildings) in a unified database system in order to enhance the efficiency of State immovable properties management.",""],[1,"132","3","National Land Registration Programme","Conduct land registration throughout the country in a transparency and effective way for both State Land (public and private State lands), and individuals' private lands and Condominium.",""],[1,"132","4","Single Window Land Registration and Valuation System","Enhance the subsequent registration through a Single Window with a Land Valuation System created in form of participatory approach, transparency, public accessibility, reliability, and coordination with to Land Use Mapping, Registration and State Land Inventory, especially in urban and inhabited areas, forest and protected areas land demarcation for in complying with the existing legal and regulatory frameworks, in particular with Sub decree on State Land Management.",""],[1,"132","5","Single Window Land Registration and Land Information System","Strengthen the subsequent registration and proceed the up-to date land information by upholding a Single Window practice for an increase of national budget with transparency and public confidence.",""],[1,"132","6","Land Information System Development","Produce Land Information System (LIS) able to provide reliable information for customers and to be basis for structuring national geographic database and for multi- purpose of usage.",""],[1,"132","7","National Geospatial and Land Classification System","Create geometry system and land classification system according to land natural characteristic and geographical information system with uniformity throughout the country.",""],[1,"132","8","National Geodesy and Altitude Network Development","Keep preparing geodesy and altitude networks throughout the country and establish permanent GPS station.",""],[1,"132","9","Participatory Land Valuation and Property Assessment Framework","Prepare participatory, transparent and formal recognized system for assessing land price on the basis of land natural advantage equality with the inclusion of all land surface immovable properties for reference in purchasing and sale, rental, investment, lending, taxation (annual tax on the transference, rental, profit, unused land, cadastral definition, and compensation), and the creation of legal framework concerning the management of professional assessment on the price of immovable property.",""],[1,"132","10","Household Farming Land Tax Exemption Policy","Keep implementing the policy of disregarding tax on farming lands for household cultivation.",""],[1,"132","10","Study on Annual Property Tax Collection","it is important to initiate the study of annual tax collection for il1Ullovable property, except for household farming lands, in the purpose of preparing law concerning tax collection for land.",""],[1,"132","11","Administrative and Cadastral Land Dispute Resolution Mechanism","Proceed out court solving land dispute through the administrative and cadastral commissions of all levels (national, city/province, town/district and mobile group) and national authority for land dispute solution; particularly, for the case of multi party disputes.",""],[1,"132","12","State Land Inventory and Allocation Transparency Initiative","Encourage and compile inventory list for state lands in reservation for current and future land distribution and use with transparency, equity and accountability.",""]],"5":[[1,"17","7","Public Financial Management Reform Program","Through the \"Public Financial Management Reform Program\", budget credibility has been fundamentally achieved as reflected by substantial growth in government revenues and the rationalization of expenditure, especially to increase the current budget surplus, which contribute to expanding investments in the economic and social infrastructure aimed at enhancing public service and poverty reduction.",""],[1,"35","2","Public Financial Management Reform Program","Since 2004, the Royal Government has been implementing the PFM Reform Program (PFMRP).",""],[1,"35","7","Budget Preparation and Public Financial Management Reform","Budget is now more comprehensive, accurate and responsive to RGC policies.",""],[1,"35","9","Institutional Capacity Strengthening of the Ministry of Economy and Finance","Institutional capacity of the Ministry of Economy and Finance has been enhanced.","Ministry of Economy and Finance"],[1,"36","15","Strengthening Platform I Achievements","The Royal Government will continue to strengthen Platform I achievements.",""],[1,"36","15","Platform II Public Financial Management Action Plan","The detailed action plan to implement the Platform II was officially announced on 3rd December 2008.",""],[1,"92","6","Official Development Assistance Mobilization and Disbursement Reform","Proactive policy to mobilize and increase disbursement of ODA for capital/development spending.","Ministry of Economy and Finance"],[1,"92","7","Public Financial Management Reform Program Platform II","The Ministry of Economy and Finance is now implementing Platform II of RGC's Public Financial Management Reform Program that is focussed on \"Building on Improved Budget Credibility towards Achieving Financial Accountability\".","The Ministry of Economy and Finance"],[1,"93","1","Budget Entity and Manager Empowerment under Platform 2","It is envisaged that work that will be done under Platform 2 twill increase the empowerment of budget entities/managers.",""],[1,"93","1","Phased Rollout of Financial Control Reforms","progress will be closely monitored will be rolled out as lessons are learned, as confidence is build and trust is earned.",""],[1,"93","2","Financial Management Information Systems and Transparency Improvement","Both enhanced accountability and empowerment will be supported by measures to further improve information systems and transparency about how financial management obligations are being exercised in practice by budget entities/managers.",""],[1,"93","3","Detailed Implementation Proposals for Technical Financial Management Reforms","For MEF, to develop proposals for the detailed implementation of some of the key technical changes envisaged in Platform 2 such as the way that funds will reach service deliverers and be utilized, the implementation of improved financial information systems and methods for holding budget implementation agencies more accountable.","MEF"],[1,"93","6","Financial Information System Computer Systems Procurement","work on procuring the computer systems that will sit at the heart of the financial information system is now well advanced.",""],[1,"93","6","Strategic Resource Management Development","The development of a more strategic approach to resource management is being developed,",""],[1,"93","6","Internal Audit Framework Development","a framework for internal audit activity has been designed",""],[1,"93","6","Line Ministry Reform Cells and Capacity Development Programmes","all line ministries have participated in briefing seminars and the design of capacity development programs.","all line ministries"],[1,"93","8","Budget Entity Manager Empowerment and Control Framework Strengthening","To build on initial steps towards greater empowerment of budget entities managers to achieve improved results because there will be an improved control framework within which to exercise that empowerment and lessons will have been learned.",""],[1,"93","9","Expenditure Efficiency and Ongoing Spending Review","To challenge the efficiency of expenditure deployment and the continuing relevance of on-going expenditures because there will be an improved basis for engaging budget entities/managers in examining such questions based on improved information flows and visibility of what is happening with resources in practice.",""],[1,"94","1","Programme Coordination and Monitoring Mechanisms","The programme now needs to engage a much wider range of players within the public service and careful coordination and monitoring will be vital.",""],[1,"94","2","Alignment of Public Financial Management Reform with Civil Service and Decentralization Reforms","there is a need to align PFM reforms with other reform programs for civil service management and D&D reforms.",""],[1,"94","4","Review and Restructure Financial Management Organisational Structures","Functional reviews will be carried out and restructuring undertaken as necessary.",""],[1,"94","4","Introduce Computerised Financial Information Systems","the introduction of computerised financial information systems will have significant organisational and process implications that will need to be allowed for if those systems are to be sustainable.",""],[1,"94","7","Public Financial Management Reform","Continuing to further reform public financial management to enhance public confidence in the use of Riel.",""],[1,"101","9","Public Finance Management Reform Program","As part of the RGC's Public Finance Management Reform Program (PFMRP), the Ministry of Economy and Finance (MEF) has established two processes that provide important inputs in the preparation of Annual National Budget.","Ministry of Economy and Finance (MEF)"],[1,"101","9","Medium-Term Expenditure Framework","The \"Medium-term Expenditure Framework (MTEF)\" provides projections of the \"recurrent expenditures\" of RGC institutions for the next three years.","Ministry of Economy and Finance (MEF)"],[1,"101","9","Budget Strategic Framework","The second process is a three-year rolling \"Budget Strategic Framework\" that follows a bottom-up approach and is prepared by the Budget Department of the MEF.","Ministry of Economy and Finance (MEF)"],[1,"102","1","Strengthening Linkages for Annual Budget Formulation","the MEF will continue to further strengthen linkages between these two processes to further refine and streamline the process of Annual Budget formulation.","MEF | RGC institutions"],[1,"102","2","Capital Expenditure Budget Leveraging Strategy","So far, RGC has been leveraging its capital expenditure budget portion of the National Budget to attract external financing to meet its high priority capital expenditure needs.",""],[1,"102","6","Public Finance Management Reform Program Linkage Strengthening","As part of the implementation of the Public Finance Management Reform Program, the Royal Government is now in the process of strengthening linkages between the processes that: (i) identify high priority public investment requirements, which include the five-year National Strategic Development Plans (NSDP) and the three-year rolling Public Investment Program PIP; (ii) the mobilization of external resources from traditional and non- traditional development partners; and (iii) the preparation of the Budget Strategic Framework.",""],[1,"102","6","Public Investment Program Prioritization and Sequencing","projects included in PIP need to be prioritized, this will require RGC institutions to assign sequenced priority ranking of the proposed projects planned for implementation during the next three years, taking into account the overall macroeconomic environment and an awareness of the scope to mobilize external resources based on recent trends.",""],[1,"102","7","Public Investment Program Formulation Strengthening","It is a high priority of the RGC to further strengthen the PIP formulation process.",""],[1,"102","7","PIP-Aligned Resource Mobilization and Reporting","The CRDB/CDC will ensure that in its resource mobilization activities it will actively promote the funding of projects included in PIP, and prepare regular reports on PIP projects that are supported by external development cooperation partners (EDPs) as well as projects supported by EDPs that are not part of the PIP.","CRDB/CDC"],[1,"102","8","Indicative Recurrent Expenditure Allocation Projection","the MEF has prepared a preliminary/indicative projection of recurrent expenditure allocation for RGC institutions for the NSDP Update 2009-2013 period.","MEF"],[1,"114","1","Public Financial Management Reform","The Public Financial Management reform has enabled the Royal Government to achieve budget credibility through improved revenue management and expenditure rationalization.",""]],"6":[[1,"114","1","Single Window Public Service Mechanism","The \"Single Window\" mechanism has been launched to facilitate the public service users while the decentralized public services at commune/sangkat level and public service provision through information technology are also offered.",""],[1,"114","1","Decentralized Public Service Delivery at Commune/Sangkat Level","the decentralized public services at commune/sangkat level and public service provision through information technology are also offered.",""],[1,"114","1","Public Financial Management Reform","The Public Financial Management reform has enabled the Royal Government to achieve budget credibility through improved revenue management and expenditure rationalization.",""],[1,"114","2","Expansion of PMGs and MBPI Coverage","In the Fourth Legislature, the Royal Government will continue to expand the coverage of the PMGs and MBPI to a number of priority ministries and agencies, in order to deepen nationwide sectoral reform programs.",""],[1,"114","2","Public Sector Salary Increase","The Royal Government will pursue the increase in base salary of 20% per annum, compared to 10-15% in the third legislature.",""],[1,"114","2","Public Administration Modernization and Service Delivery Reform","The Royal Government will continue to enhance the efficient use of information technology; implement improved personnel management and the capacity building for government officials; increase roles and participation of women in public administration; enhance provision of basic public services, government sovereignty services, investment-related services, and support to small and medium businesses through the implementation of the \"Single Window\" mechanism; and to pursue the establishment of Ombudsman offices.",""],[1,"114","2","Ombudsman Office Establishment","The Royal Government will also set up new mechanisms in providing public services through the creation of the \"Special Operation Agency\" in a number of ministries and agencies, and will encourage the civil society and private sector to participate directly in providing public services.",""],[1,"114","4","Public Administration Reform Programme","Building on achievements to date, the Council for Administrative Reform is deepening and widening the reform.",""],[1,"114","5","Civil Service Capacity Development Policy","The CAR is developing a policy on developing capacity in consultation with ministries","CAR | ministries"],[1,"115","1","Capacity Development Policy and Coordination Framework","The purpose of the policy is to set parameters for capacity development and to facilitate the coordination of efforts.",""],[1,"115","2","Programme Deployment and Capacity Support Arrangements","Programs and implementation arrangements will be deployed to complement work already underway.",""],[1,"115","3","Public Service Delivery Improvement and Civil Service Reform","In particular, the focus will be to continue to improve the quality and delivery of public services in line with the Policy on Improving Public Service Delivery, to complete the policy framework to guide the reform particularly those parts relating to the management, development and deployment of civil servants (performance and merit based practices), to strengthen the management of capacity in the Civil Service (with an early focus on better using existing competencies, coordination mechanisms and immediate implementation needs), to continue to deploy performance and accountability instruments (SOAs, PMGs, MBPIs and PMAS) as wedges to changing practices and procedures; to continue to improve compensation in a fiscally responsible manner, and to significantly reinforce personnel management and control mechanisms (recruitment, promotion, retirement for example).",""],[1,"115","4","National Programme for Administrative Reforms 2009-2013","Following the National Seminar on the Administrative Reform held in February 2009, Samdech Akkak Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister approved a strategy for implementation of the \"National Programme for Administrative Reforms 2009-2013\" that is articulated around five thrusts.",""],[1,"115","6","Public Service Delivery Improvement Policy Implementation","Continuing the implementation of the Policy on Improving Public Service Delivery.",""],[1,"115","7","Governance Action Plan Update","Updating the Governance Action Plan to focus on how to improve public services and enhance coordination among the reforms.",""],[1,"115","8","Public Services Compendium Finalization and Dissemination","Finalizing the Compendium on public services and disseminate it broadly to enhance transparency and facilitate access to public services including: electronic access.",""],[1,"115","9","Service Delivery Simplification and Streamlining Initiative","Coordinating and collaborating with ministries and institutions to review targeted services by simplifying procedures and streamlining delivery processes.",""],[1,"115","11","Administrative Reform for Public Service Performance and Accountability","In order to achieve the priorities of the Royal Government and to improve public services to people, the Administrative Reform will focus on improving performance and accountability to enhance implementation of policy and operational priorities of the Royal Government by:",""],[1,"116","2","Performance and Accountability Instruments Deployment","Continuing the deployment of Performance and Accountability instruments: Special Operating Agencies, Merit Base Performance Incentives and Priority Mission Groups.",""],[1,"116","4","Demand-Driven Institutional and Human Capacity Development Policy Framework","A policy framework will guide implementation by ministries and institutions that will include:",""],[1,"116","7","Performance Management and Accountability System","The development and deployment of Performance Management and Accountability System.",""],[1,"116","11","Civil Servants Basic Salary Increase Policy","Continue the implementation of the 20% annual increase is basic salary policy of civil servants.",""],[1,"116","12","Human Resource Management Policy Finalization","Finalize the policy on human resource management and guidelines.",""],[1,"116","17","Civil Service Cadre Management Strengthening","Strengthening cadre management and maintaining the number of civil servant to an acceptable level.",""],[1,"116","20","Redeployment Policy Implementation","Finalizing and implement the policy on redeployment.",""],[1,"116","21","National Program for Administrative Reform","The National Program for Administrative Reform - Serving People Better for the present mandate to 2013 outlines a detailed Action Plan of sequenced actions.",""],[1,"116","21","Administrative Reform Partnership Arrangements","It is urgent that necessary partnership arrangements be put in place to implement the reform.",""],[1,"116","21","Administrative Reform Coordination and Monitoring Mechanism","it is urgent to strengthen mechanisms for coordination and monitoring.",""],[1,"117","3","Administrative Reform Policy Framework","a policy framework to guide administrative reform and a coherent set of programs and partnerships;",""],[1,"117","6","Performance and Accountability Enhancement Instruments","the continuing deployment of instruments to enhance performance and accountability (SOAs, PMGs, MBPIs and PMAS).",""],[1,"117","7","Support Systems for Ministry Reform Implementation","Involves the establishment of systems, processes and mechanisms to support ministries in their implementation of reform activities, including:",""],[1,"117","8","Human Resources Management Tools Deployment","deployment of instruments and tools to enhance the management and development of human resources;",""],[1,"117","9","Performance and Accountability Improvement Measures","gradual deployment of practices and processes to improve performance and accountability;",""],[1,"117","10","Public Service Capacity Development Initiatives","Implementation of a coherent set of capacity development initiatives to enhance the quality and delivery of public services and the implementation of policy priorities.",""],[1,"117","16","Governance Action Plan III Update","the Council for Administrative Reform, in close collaboration with ministries, is also updating the Governance Action Plan.","ministries"],[1,"117","17","Governance Action Plan for Public Service Delivery","GAPIII will, in effect, outline how ministries and institutions will implement their reforms to improve the quality and delivery of public services.",""],[1,"118","1","Institutionalization of Governance Structures","The first phase of three year period, 2010 to 2012, will focus on the establishment and institutionalization of structures and good governance framework at national and sub-national levels.",""]],"7":[[1,"191","1","Regular Monitoring and Evaluation Protocol","Regular monitoring and evaluation of the actions taken by ministries and agencies to achieve the goals and targets of RGC's priority policies for the Fourth Legislature is an integral part of the planning process.",""],[1,"191","2","Periodic Monitoring and Evaluation of Development Actions","The Royal Government would like all ministries and agencies and development cooperation partners who are financing any action/program/project to give a high priority to carrying out periodic monitoring and evaluation of the implementation of the action/program/project and to promptly provide copies of these reports to the Ministry of Planning after they have been finalized","Ministry of Planning"],[1,"192","1","CMDG Targets and Indicators Revision and Update","Also, based on revision of targets and indicators of global MDGs, that became effective as of 1 January 2008, the targets and indicators of relevant CMDGs will be updated to incorporate any changes in the global MDGs.",""],[1,"192","3","Indicator Monitoring Responsibility Assignment","A line Ministry/Agency that will be responsible for monitoring the indicator must be identified, and the willingness of the concerned Ministry/Agency to carry out this work must be secured.",""],[1,"192","8","Update of Core Monitoring Indicators and Targets","it is, however, a high priority of the Ministry of Planning to continue work on developing an update set of \"core monitoring indicators/targets\" for NSDP Update 2009-2013, and to complete this task before work on the first overall assessment of progress on the implementation of NSDP Update 2009-2013 is carried out.","Ministry of Planning"],[1,"192","9","Mid-Term Review Preparation of NSDP Update 2009-2013","the Ministry of Planning has decided to focus on preparing a more comprehensive mid-term review of NSDP Update 2009-2013.","Ministry of Planning"],[1,"192","9","Next Progress Assessment Report Preparation","The work on the preparation of the next progress assessment report will begin in September 2012 and completed by the end of December 2012.",""],[1,"192","9","Preparation of NSDP 2014-2018","The work on the preparation of NSDP 2014-2018 will begin in January 2013 with a target completion date of end of December 2013.",""],[1,"194","1","NSDP Update 2009-2013 Implementation Roadmap","The NSDP Update 2009-2013 presents a roadmap for the implementation of RGC's priority policies for the Fourth legislature that have been articulated in Rectangular Strategy Phase II.",""]],"8":[[1,"65","4","Population Policy Implementation","The last, but not the least, of the \"growth\" rectangles of RS covers predominantly social sectors, viz., (4) implementation of population policy.",""],[1,"83","5","Population Policy Mainstreaming and Capacity Strengthening","The National Committee for Population and Development (NCPD) has been working to strengthen its human resources to integrate population-related issues in the development planning processes at all levels for planners and policy makers.",""],[1,"166","2","National Population Policy Implementation","The four sides or sub-components of this component of the Rectangular Strategy Phase II deal with: and the (iv) implementation of national population policy.",""],[1,"182","31","Population Policy Integration into Socio-Economic Planning","the Royal Government will continue its efforts to integrate the population policy into socio-economic policy, plans and programs at all levels.",""],[1,"183","3","Capacity Building for Population and Poverty Policy Analysis","Enhancing the capacity of policy makers, parliamentarians, planners, and development program managers at the national and sub-national levels to take into account the data and analysis on key population and poverty issues.",""],[1,"183","4","Guidelines for Integrating Key Population and Poverty Variables","Formulating guidelines for integrating key population and poverty variables in the design of all development programs.",""],[1,"183","5","Capacity Building for Planning Officers on Population Integration","Strengthening capacity of planning officers at the national and sub-national levels to integrate population issues in planning processes.",""],[1,"183","6","Population Policy Monitoring and Update Mechanism","Strengthening institutional capacity to identify emerging population issues by periodically carrying out analysis and to monitor and update the population policy.",""],[1,"183","7","Disaggregated Population Data Development and Dissemination","Developing and widely disseminating disaggregated population data at the national and sub-national levels.",""],[1,"183","8","Household Survey Implementation","Continuing work on carrying out the CDHS 2010 survey, and the CIPS 2013 in a timely manner.",""]],"9":[[1,"40","13","Institutional, Legal Framework, and Human Resources Development Strengthening","Strengthen institution, legal framework and human resources development.",""]],"10":[[1,"37","7","NGO Law Reform","A law on NGOs will be passed after wide consultation with all stakeholders.",""],[1,"123","2","NGO and Association Engagement in Socio-economic Rehabilitation and Monitoring","The Royal Government will continue to encourage NGOs and Associations that have been legally established and operate based on good governance principles to engage in the process of socio-economic rehabilitation and development, to promote democracy and the respect for human rights and dignity as well as to participate with the Royal Government in monitoring the implementation of various policy strategies.",""],[1,"123","2","Law on Non-Government Organizations and Associations","The Royal Government will continue to pursue the adoption and implementation of a Law on Non-Government Organizations (NGOs) and Associations in close consultation with relevant agencies and organizations.",""],[1,"125","6","Civil Society Engagement and Monitoring Framework","The Royal Government will continue to encourage civil society organizations that have been legally formed and operate based on good governance principles to engage in the process of socio-economic development of the country, and in the promotion of democracy and human rights, and encourage their responsible participation in monitoring the implementation of national development strategies and policies.",""],[1,"126","1","Law on Non-Government Organizations and Associations","The Government will continue to pursue the adoption and implementation of the Law in close consultation with relevant agencies and organizations.",""],[1,"126","2","Civil Society Participation in Policy Dialogue Mechanisms","The Royal Government will continue to ensure rigorous participation of CSOs in the dialogue mechanisms.",""]],"11":[[1,"151","2","Telecommunications Law and Regulatory Framework Reform","speed up the adoption of the Law on Telecommunications and associated legal and regulatory framework",""],[1,"151","2","Postal and Telecommunication Competition Promotion","foster competition in the postal and telecommunication services to ensure efficiency of this sector",""],[1,"151","2","E-Government and IT System Efficiency Initiative","increase the efficient use of IT system and promote e- government",""],[1,"151","5","Development Project Implementation Management","Efficiently managing the implementation of development projects that are underway to ensure the completion of these projects on schedule.",""],[1,"151","9","Telecommunication Contract Compliance Monitoring and Enforcement","Continuing to monitor and to take legal actions against telecommunication operators who are in violation of their contracts.",""],[1,"151","10","Investment Company Regulatory Framework","Developing and promulgating regulations required to orient the investment companies about this sector.",""],[1,"151","11","Mobile Telecommunications Revenue Leakage Prevention","Continuing to give priority to stop leakages of revenues from the mobile telecommunication system.",""],[1,"151","15","Regulatory Framework Strengthening for Telecommunications Approvals","To strengthen the regulatory framework, the Ministry of Post and Telecommunications will develop of approval:","Ministry of Post and Telecommunications"],[1,"152","4","Approval of International Multilateral Partnership Against Cyber Terrorism","Approval of International Multilateral Partnership Against Cyber Terrorism (2010- 2011)",""],[1,"152","7","Radio Frequency Usage Management Commission Establishment","Declaration on establishing Radio Frequency Usage Management Commission (2010)",""]],"12":[[1,"56","5","National Fibre Optic Network Expansion","The Ministry of Post and Telecommunications is managing the implementation of several large projects worth around 536 million US$ to extend the fibre optics cable network infrastructure across the country to expand telecommunications services nationwide.","Ministry of Post and Telecommunications"],[1,"151","2","Post and Telecommunications System Development","The Royal Government of the Fourth Legislature will continue to develop the post and telecommunication system and promote the development of information and communication technology (ICT) to ensure high quality conforming to international standards, low price and reasonably nation-wide coverage.",""],[1,"151","2","Sector Capacity Building for Post and Telecommunications","build capacity of the sector",""],[1,"151","2","Equipment and Technology Modernization for Telecommunications","improve and modernize the equipment and technology to ensure effectiveness and a wider coverage of the services",""],[1,"151","2","ICT Backbone Infrastructure Development","build and enhance efficiency of the backbone infrastructure for the information and communication technology sector",""],[1,"151","3","Telecommunications Service Expansion and Fee Reduction","the Ministry of Post and Telecommunications will take actions to expand telecommunications services and reduce fees by:","Ministry of Post and Telecommunications"],[1,"151","4","Telecommunications Infrastructure Investment Promotion","Developing and providing information on investment opportunities to investors to build telecommunications infrastructure.",""],[1,"151","6","Submarine Fibre Optic Cable Rehabilitation","Rehabilitation of Submarine fibre optics cable.",""],[1,"151","7","Fibre Optic Telecommunications Network Construction","Construction of fibre optics telecommunications Network.",""],[1,"151","8","Greater Mekong Sub-region Fiber Optic Network Linkage Project","Projects in the Greater Mekong Sub-region to link fibre optics network from Siem Reap to Skun; Kampong Cham to Lao PDR boarder (Stung Treng);",""],[1,"151","8","Telecommunications Service Improvement in Urban and Rural Areas","improvement of telecommunications services in both urban and rural areas.",""],[1,"151","12","Fiber Optic Network Development","Continuing to promoting the development of fibre optics network using underground and undersea cables to improving communications services within the country and to improve communication to international destinations.",""],[1,"151","14","Telecommunication Office Construction Programme","Constructing telecommunication offices at Preah Vihear, Ratanakiri, Takeo, Stung Treng, and Kampong Thom.",""],[1,"152","1","Establishment of the Universal Telecommunication Union","Sub-decree on Establishing Universal Telecommunication Union (2009-2011)",""],[1,"153","9","Telecommunication Network Expansion and Modernization","to strengthen and expand the modern telecommunication network to make services available at a reasonably low rate;",""]],"13":[[1,"58","8","Electronic Market Communication System","To improve market information, in 2008, the Ministry developed an Electronic Market Communication System (EMCS) which is expected to provide better and faster information.","Ministry"]],"14":[[1,"151","13","Gender-Focused Research and Development Enhancement","Enhancing and improving research and development focusing on gender issues.",""],[1,"152","19","National Media Coverage Expansion and Quality Improvement","Expand coverage and improve the quality and effectiveness of the national media to provide services to 95 percent of the population across the country, to the region and other continents, including North America.",""],[1,"152","20","Provincial Radio and Television Station Expansion and Capacity Improvement","Continue construction of new provincial radio and television stations and improvement of their capacity to enable them to rely on live major events at the national level, and to be able to produce and broadcast programs to more areas, especially on issues facing women and children.",""],[1,"152","21","Institutional and Human Resources Capacity Building","Build institutional and human resources capacity, with an emphasis to increase the number of female staff, to improve delivery of services to the public and to effectively interact and cooperate within ASEAN, in the region and with development partners.",""],[1,"152","22","Press Law Enforcement","Enforce the Press Law in order to enhance the rule of law, and freedom of the press, of expression and of publications.",""],[1,"152","23","Media and Information Technology Regulatory Framework Development","Study, research and draft legal instruments in order to effectively regulate the media businesses and to support the development of information and audio filed and information technology.",""],[1,"153","1","Public Participation and Women’s Inclusion in Information and Audio Sector","Continue encouraging and opening up the participation of the public sector, civil society groups, and non-governmental organizations, and give priority to women to play their role in the information and audio field.",""]],"16":[[1,"23","5","Legal and Judicial Reform","These are: (i) fighting corruption; (ii) legal and judicial reforms; (iii) public administration reforms in all aspects (including decentralisation and de-concentration); and (iv) reform of the armed forces.",""],[1,"24","1","Ministry of Justice Legislative Drafting Function","The Ministry of Justice is responsible for drafting of all laws, including the anti-corruption law.","Ministry of Justice"],[1,"24","7","Legal and Judicial Reform Acceleration","The Royal Government is committed to accelerating the Legal and Judicial Reform process.",""],[1,"25","1","Legal and Judicial Reform Action Plan","Since mid 2005, the Council for Legal and Judicial Reform has been implementing its comprehensive action plan to implement RGC's Legal and Judicial Reform Strategy.",""],[1,"25","2","Fundamental Rights Protection and Awareness Measures","Improvement of the protection of fundamental rights and freedoms by developing and supporting measures to safeguard rights and raise awareness among the people and all institutions involved",""],[1,"25","3","Legislative Framework Modernization","Modernization of the legislative framework by developing a comprehensive framework of laws through an efficient, coherent and participatory law-making process, ensuring balanced legislation and a full implementation of the rule of law.",""],[1,"25","4","Legal and Judicial Information Access Improvement","Provision of better access to legal and judicial information by promoting dissemination of basic legal knowledge through official publications, electronic media and information folders and ensuring easy accessibility to all legal and judicial information for legal practitioners and any other interested party.",""],[1,"25","5","Legal Profession and Judicial Procedure Reform","Enhancement of the quality of legal processes and related services by strengthening the legal profession, enhancing access to legal assistance and streamlining judicial procedures in order to ensure fair justice and due process for the people.",""],[1,"25","6","Judicial Services Strengthening Reform","Strengthening of judicial services, i.e. the judicial power and the prosecutorial services by introducing the necessary educational, legislative, procedural ad structural measures to ensure access to justice within fair, credible and independent judicial institutions enjoying broad respect.",""],[1,"25","7","Alternative Dispute Resolution Mechanisms","Introduction of alternative dispute resolution mechanisms to enable quick, informal and easy dispute resolution to the benefit of involved parties and to ease the burden on the established judicial system.",""],[1,"25","8","Legal and Judicial Sector Institutional Strengthening","Strengthening of Legal and Judicial sector institutions to fulfil their mandates by strengthening management, planning and monitoring mechanisms and capacity in general in order to enable the full provision of public services and to ensure decision- making in accordance with principles of good governance and their efficient enforcement.",""],[1,"25","17","Draft Law on Court Organization and Prosecution","Draft Law on Court Organization and Prosecution.",""],[1,"26","4","Pilot Court Model for Provincial Courts","A Pilot Court Model for provincial courts has been established by the Council of Legal and Judicial Reform in cooperation with the Ministry of Justice.","Council of Legal and Judicial Reform | Ministry of Justice"],[1,"26","9","Out-of-Court Dispute Resolution Mechanisms","Mechanisms for dispute resolution outside the court system to reduce the backlog of cases at the provincial court and to expedite dispute resolution for the citizen and the poor have been put in place by the Ministry of Justice in cooperation with the Ministry of Interior.","Ministry of Justice | Ministry of Interior"],[1,"26","9","Legal Services Centers Expansion","Since 2007, the Ministry of Justice has established 20 Centers for Legal Services that proceeded.","Ministry of Justice"],[1,"26","9","Nationwide Expansion of Dispute Resolution Mechanisms","If these mechanisms work successfully then they will be expanded across the country.",""],[1,"26","13","Legal Awareness and Justice Sector Capacity-Building Programmes","Budget constraints to expand programs aimed at improving legal knowledge of communities and the vulnerable people and as well as the training programs to build capacity of the Judges and prosecutors.",""],[1,"111","4","Legal and Judicial Reform Strategy Implementation","The Royal Government will continue implementing the legal and judicial reform strategy in order to achieve its seven strategic objectives.",""],[1,"111","4","Adoption of Fundamental Justice and Anti-Corruption Laws","It will also focus more on the early adoption of major fundamental laws such as the Penal Code, the Anti-Corruption Law, the Law on the Statutes of Judges and Prosecutors, the Law on the Organization and Functioning of the Courts and the Law on the Amendment of the Law on the Organization and Functioning of the Supreme Council of the Magistracy.",""],[1,"111","4","Public Legal Awareness and Law Enforcement Training Programme","At the same time, the Royal Government will continue to organize programs to disseminate knowledge of laws and procedures to the public and provide legal training to law-enforcement officials with the aim of improving awareness and proper enforcement of the laws.",""],[1,"111","5","Judges and Prosecutors Competency and Accountability Strengthening","the Royal Government will continue to address the following priorities : (1) enhancement of the competency of Judges and Prosecutors through continued high quality training and initial professional training, and enhancing the accountability of judges and prosecutors by promulgating the statutes for Judges and Prosecutors, and by taking strict disciplinary actions in close cooperation with the Supreme Council of the Magistracy",""],[1,"111","5","Judicial Sector Support Mechanisms and Training Schools","development of the support mechanisms to serve the judicial sector- including the introduction of the statutes for the court clerks, the notaries and the bailiffs; and the operational functioning of professional training schools for the above officials in order to ensure their proper qualifications and professionalism",""],[1,"111","5","Legal Aid for Poor Citizens","provision of legal aid- especially through provision of lawyers to poor citizens to help protect their rights and interests at court",""],[1,"111","5","Alternative Dispute Resolution Promotion","further promotion of the mechanisms for dispute resolution outside of the court system in order to improve and strengthen the culture of harmonious co- existence of people in peace and solidarity",""],[1,"112","2","Legal Reform Promotion for Core Justice and Anti-Corruption Laws","Continue to promote the adoption of the major fundamental laws namely the Penal Code, the Anti-corruption Law, the Law on the Organization and Functioning of the Court, the Law on the Amendment to the Law on the Organization and Functioning of the Supreme Council of the Magistracy.",""],[1,"112","4","Legal Rights Awareness Dissemination Campaign","The Council for Legal and Judicial Reform, the Ministry of Justice, the Royal Academy for Judicial Professions, Lawyer Training Centre, the National Police Academy and other specialized institutions will actively engage in disseminating information on Laws and rights of citizens under the Laws in order to enhance their awareness of and ability to defend their rights in order to reduce offences against them.","Ministry of Justice"],[1,"112","5","Court Information Services Booths","Establish information services booth for citizens at the municipal and provincial courts.",""],[1,"112","23","Strengthening the SCM Disciplinary Council","Strengthening the Disciplinary Council of the SCM.",""],[1,"112","24","Model Court Reform and Expansion","Model Court implementation: Strengthening management and administration of courts, expansion to other courts and increasing funding support for court reform.",""],[1,"113","1","Court Decisions Collection and Publication System","Collecting, commenting, printing and publishing court decisions.",""],[1,"113","2","Justice Sector Institutional Support Mechanism","Building mechanism to assist the Justice Sector Institutions",""],[1,"113","3","Statutory Reform for Justice and Corrections Personnel","Enact and implement statutes for court clerks, notaries, bailiffs, police and corrections;",""],[1,"113","4","Training Schools for Court Clerks, Notaries and Bailiffs Strengthening","Strengthen the Training Schools for Court Clerks, Notaries and Bailiffs.",""],[1,"113","5","Strategic Plan for Legal Aid Recommendations","Prepare a Strategic Plan to implement key recommendations set forth by \"Legal aid national survey: December 2006\".",""],[1,"113","6","Legal Aid Activity Plan Implementation","Implement the Activity Plan for the provision of legal aid.",""],[1,"113","7","ADR Mechanism Promotion","Continue to promote ADR Mechanism",""],[1,"113","8","Maison de la Justice Project Strengthening","Strengthen the Maison de la justice project;",""],[1,"113","9","Expansion of Alternate Dispute Resolution Centres for Legal Services","Expand the implementation of the Alternate Dispute Resolution (ADR) mechanism outside the court system by establishing Centres for Legal Services in 20 districts, and expand these services in all districts and the capital in order to reduce the backlog of cases at the provincial court and facilitate the dispute resolution for the citizens, in particular the poor at the commune level.",""],[1,"113","10","ADR Legal Framework Development","Study and prepare legal framework for the integration of ADR.",""],[1,"113","11","Judiciary Services Expansion","Expand the Judiciary services by establishing:",""],[1,"113","12","Establishment of Special Courts and Tribunals","Special Courts as needed such as the Commercial Tribunal, the Labour Tribunal, the Juvenile Tribunal and the Administrative Tribunal.",""],[1,"113","13","Sub-national Court of Appeal Access Expansion","The Court of Appeal at sub-national levels to facilitate access to the judicial system for citizens, in particular those living in remote area citizen and to reduce the backlog at Phnom Penh court of Appeal.",""],[1,"113","15","International Cooperation in Law and Justice","Strengthening international cooperation in the law and judicial field especially with Asean countries.",""],[1,"113","16","Continuing Skill Training for GS-CLJR Staff","Continuing skill training for GS-CLJR staff;",""],[1,"113","17","Justice Sector Planning Guide Training and Reform Implementation Mechanism","Continuing delivery of training on the Planning Guide for the Justice Sector Institutions and prepare necessary mechanism for strengthening the implementation of the reform;",""],[1,"113","18","Legal and Judicial Reform Monitoring Indicators","Preparing indicators and monitor the implementation of the legal and judicial reform;",""],[1,"113","19","Legal and Judicial Reform Programme Communication","Continuing informing courts and local authorities of the legal and judicial reform programme.",""],[1,"119","5","Right to Obtain Justice Project","MOI will continue to implement the Right to Obtain Justice Project between MOI and Ministry of Justice.","MOI | Ministry of Justice"]],"17":[[1,"65","4","Education Quality Strengthening","The last, but not the least, of the \"growth\" rectangles of RS covers predominantly social sectors, viz., (1) strengthening the quality of education;",""],[1,"65","4","Education and Health Sector Coordination Mechanisms","Progress has been very impressive in both education and health sectors, where cooperation and coordination mechanisms among various stakeholders had started even before introduction of the TWG mechanism in late 2003.",""],[1,"65","4","Sectoral Strategy Implementation and Monitoring","Sectoral strategies in both of these critical sectors are now well developed and are being implemented, and progress is being monitored on a regular basis in a timely manner.",""],[1,"66","1","Education Sector Strategic Plan Implementation","The ESP 2006-2010 implementation has contributed to enhancing equitable access to education for all Cambodian children, assisting them to become good students, good children, and good citizens, who will be able to productively contribute to socio-economic development of Cambodia in the future.",""],[1,"66","2","Education Sector SWAp Coordination and Financing Mechanism","The SWAp in the education sector has made available to the Ministry of Education a mechanism for aligning development cooperation assistance with the education sector needs.","Ministry of Education | MOEYS"],[1,"66","2","Public Financial Management Reform Program for Education","The education sector is one of the priorities in Public Financial Management Reform (PFMR) program of the RGC.","RGC"],[1,"66","2","Education Budget Expansion and Timely Disbursement","The RGC remains committed to further strengthening of the quality of education and have continued to increase the recurrent expenditure allocations for the education sector in the National Budget and has ensured timely disbursements to the MOEYS of the allocated resources, which have increased from 183.2 billion CR in 2000 to 742.5 billion CR in 2009.","RGC | MOEYS"],[1,"68","3","Accessible Education Facilities for Disabled Children","The expansion of education services has included more accessible facilities for disabled children by way of ramps, toilets, etc.",""],[1,"68","10","Internal Regulation for Public Primary Schools","Issued a Prakas on Internal Regulation for pubic primary schools to increase promotion rate.",""],[1,"68","11","Child Friendly School Policy Endorsement","Endorsed the Child Friendly School (CFS) Policy and the Master Plan to improve quality of education.",""],[1,"68","12","Education Policies for Disabled Children","Endorsed Policies on Education for Disabled Children, implementing accelerated classes and piloting the CFS programs in the lower secondary schools.",""],[1,"68","13","New Curriculum Implementation Guidelines and Textbook Supply Framework","Issued guidelines on the implementation of the new curriculum for basic education including the learning standards and action plans for guiding teachers on the new curriculum policy and guidelines on preparing school subjects and guideline for students to select elective subjects to study in upper secondary schools.",""],[1,"69","1","Education Law and BMC Implementation and Legislative Improvement Plans","the MoEYS is now preparing action plans to improve other legislative instruments, so far, the actions it has taken have included:","MoEYS"],[1,"69","4","Program-Based Budgeting Guideline Issuance","The MoEYS has issued Guideline dated 05 February 2008 on the functions and duties, the preparation of documents, and legislative instruments for those institutions that are involved in managing and using the Program Based Budgeting (PB) at the central and provincial/municipal levels.","MoEYS"],[1,"69","7","Education Function Decentralization Strategic Plan","The MoEYS has drafted a Strategic Plan to decentralize the education function and it is waiting for the endorsement of the Organic Law.","MoEYS"],[1,"69","8","Education Monitoring System Strengthening","The MoEYS is now focusing its effort, in particular, on strengthening the monitoring system.","MoEYS"],[1,"69","17","Construction of Additional Lower Secondary Schools","After the ADB and World Bank projects are completed there will still be a need to construct an additional 400 lower secondary schools to secure full coverage.",""],[1,"69","19","Textbook Supply Assurance","Ensuring adequate supply of textbooks for all students.",""],[1,"166","2","Education Quality Strengthening","The four sides or sub-components of this component of the Rectangular Strategy Phase II deal with: (i) strengthening the quality of education;",""],[1,"166","5","Education Strategic Plan Implementation","In the Fourth Legislature, the Royal Government will continue to implement the Education Strategic Plan, putting emphasis on ensuring that all Cambodian children and youth should have equal opportunity for access to basic education, both formal and informal, without discrimination on grounds of race, skin colour, gender, languages, religion, political affiliations of parents, place of birth and social status.",""],[1,"166","5","Peace, Human Rights, and Anti-Violence Education Initiative","Equally, the implementation of the Strategic Plan is linked to imparting a culture of peace, respect for human rights and dignity, respect for the principles of freedom, democracy and justice, and instilling a culture against violence, drug use, child and women trafficking and social discrimination.",""],[1,"166","6","Education Quality Improvement Programme","The Royal Government will pay attention to improve the quality of education by: providing incentives to teachers; improving curriculum; encouraging outstanding students; training teachers and upgrading teaching methodologies; improving class room conditions and learning materials; and, establishing libraries and laboratories.",""],[1,"166","6","Student Dormitory Expansion and Rural School Construction","In order to ensure equitable opportunity, the government will continue to establish dormitories for students, especially female students; to build schools for all levels, particularly in rural and remote",""],[1,"167","1","Scholarship Expansion for Poor Students","to increase scholarship for poor students.",""],[1,"167","1","Teacher Training and Deployment Policy Implementation","the government will continue to train qualified teachers in adequate number and effectively implement teacher deployment policy.",""],[1,"167","1","Teacher Upgrading and Qualification Pathway","The government will encourage teachers who work at primary and lower secondary schools and who have obtained bachelor degree at any age to take an exam to become high school teachers; and allow primary teachers who have not completed high school take an exam to obtain equivalent certificate of high school graduation.",""],[1,"167","3","Education Budget Increase and Financing Mobilization","The government will increase budget allocation for education and mobilize more financing to support education to ensure higher and effective quality of education.",""],[1,"167","4","Updated Education Sector Plan Preparation","As a high priority, the MoEYS will begin the process of preparing an updated ESP 2009-2013 to ensure the harmonization of the education sector plan with the mandate of the Legislature and to bring a sharper focus on achieving the goals of RGC's policies for the education sector.","MoEYS"],[1,"167","5","Implementation of Priority Education Sector Measures","the MoEYS will continue to diligently implement appropriate measures in the three focus areas of ESP","MoEYS"],[1,"167","6","School Access and Primary Education Expansion","Ensuring equal access to education service by building schools close to student's home, reducing the number of incomplete primary schools, providing operational budgets to schools, increasing the supply of teachers, and building dormitories for students, especially girls.",""],[1,"167","7","Education Service Quality Improvement","Improving quality and effectiveness of education service by increasing provision of school instructional materials, libraries and laboratories, continuing to further reform the curriculum, increasing learning hours, providing scholarships to",""],[1,"168","1","Support for Poor Students and School Improvement","poor students, enhancing teaching and management capacity, strengthening teachers' morality, improving schools' environment (supply of clean water and latrines), and expanding functional literacy.",""],[1,"168","2","Education Officer Institutional Capacity Building for Decentralisation","Enhancing institutional development and capacity building of education officers for decentralisation by re-structuring working procedures, developing legislative instruments, and training education officers at all levels on technical skills.",""],[1,"168","3","Program-Based Budgeting Framework for MoEYS Services","To deliver its services, the MoEYS will follow the Program Based Budgeting approach as set out in Budget Strategic Plan 2010-2012.","MoEYS"],[1,"168","5","Early Childhood Education Expansion","Expansion of early childhood education.",""],[1,"168","16","Education Sector Monitoring and Evaluation and Inspection Program","This program is focused on monitoring and evaluation of education sector's performance and administrative and financial inspection.",""],[1,"169","2","Education Policy Decrees and Regulations Development","To support the implementation of the prioritized policies of RGC, the MoEYS will develop and submit for approval the following decrees/sub-decrees/regulations:","MoEYS"],[1,"169","4","School and Institution Organizational Restructuring Prakas","Prakas on establishment, closing, integration, inaction, separation, and transforming of school or institution.",""],[1,"169","20","Health Check Requirement for Students and Staff","xvi. Prakas on health check for student and staff.",""],[1,"169","39","Primary School Access Expansion","Provide access for school-age children to attend primary school.",""],[1,"170","1","Local Teacher Recruitment Initiative","Increase the number of teachers recruited from local areas, particularly disadvantaged areas.",""],[1,"170","2","Facility Development Plan Preparation","Prepare facility development plan in cooperation with DPs and NGOS.",""],[1,"170","4","Public Pre-School and Community School Strengthening and Expansion","Continue to strengthening public pre-school and class and existing pre-school community and expansion schools.",""],[1,"170","5","Child-Friendly School Strengthening and Expansion","Strengthening and expansion of child friendly school.",""],[1,"170","6","School Operational Budget Increase","Increase school operational budget in consistency with school development plan.",""],[1,"170","7","Female Student Councils in Schools","Establish female student councils in schools to deal with difficulties and encourage female students.",""],[1,"170","8","Teacher Training Curriculum Revision","Revise teacher training curriculum at all levels and all specialized subjects.",""],[1,"170","13","Higher Education Program Framework Revision","Revise framework of higher education programs to reflect national and market needs in accord with higher education vision and strategy 2020",""],[1,"170","13","Scholarship Budget Support for Essential Fields","ease government budget for scholarships in essential areas especially female students.",""],[1,"170","22","Timely Provision of Student and Teacher Books","Supply enough students' books and teachers' books on time.",""],[1,"170","23","School Library Strengthening and Expansion Programme","Strengthening the existing library at school and continue to expand over the country.",""],[1,"170","24","Grade-12 Examination Technology Upgrade","Revise standard and quality of grade-12 examination by seeking for new technology to control the exam.",""],[1,"170","30","Teacher Salary, Recruitment, Promotion and Replacement Policy Reform","Formulate accurate policies related to teachers' salary, recruitment, promotion and replacement.",""],[1,"171","4","Budget Resource Use Legislation","Prepare legislation on the use of budget resources on time and in accordance with the budget allocation schedule.",""],[1,"171","5","Implementation Guideline and Monitoring Mechanism Strengthening","Strengthening implementation guideline and monitoring mechanism.",""],[1,"177","2","Female Students Education Access Support Programme","The Royal Government of the Fourth Legislature will continue to implement its policy aiming at increasing education opportunity for female students through increased scholarships, additional training programs, providing accommodation and safe transportation, and increasing the number of female teachers.",""],[1,"178","4","Girls' Education Awareness and Expansion Initiative","Promote formal and informal education for women and girls by raising awareness among the public of the value and importance of girls' education; advocating for and monitoring the expansion of the program of early childhood education and community based preschools, especially in remote areas; raising awareness of education among parents and families; promoting expansion of informal education including programs on literacy, livelihood and vocational skills for adult women and girls who have dropped out of school; advocating for the expansion of scholarship programs at high school and higher education levels.",""]],"18":[[1,"62","5","Employment Placement Services for Job-Seekers","The Ministry of Labour and Vocational Training (MLVT) has been providing employment placement services to assist job-seekers in finding employment in private sector businesses and to work in foreign countries.","Ministry of Labour and Vocational Training (MLVT)"],[1,"63","1","Technical and Vocational Training Programs","The Ministry is also provided technical and vocational training programs through its 36 training centres.","The Ministry"],[1,"63","7","Labour Market Information System and Employment Placement Services Expansion","Developing a labour market information system, expanding the coverage of the Employment Placement services.",""],[1,"64","1","Technical Education and Vocational Training Expansion","Expanding the technical education and vocational training programs to meet the skilled labour needs, especially in rural areas to create skilled jobs and to support the development of agro-industries, improve agriculture sector productivity and diversification.",""],[1,"154","1","Employee and Skilled Labor Productivity Training","improve productivity through training for employees, technicians, and skilled labor",""],[1,"157","9","Vocational Training for Labour Market Demand","capacity building through vocational training in response to market demands by mainly focusing on drop-out young students at secondary and high schools, disabled people, women, marginalized groups and minorities;",""],[1,"158","15","Expansion of Technical and Vocational Training in Rural Areas","Expand technical and vocation training, in particular in rural areas, by:",""],[1,"158","16","Technical and Vocational Training Needs Analysis","Carrying out a comprehensive analysis of technical and vocational training required to meet the needs of employers in the urban areas as well as to support the development of rural communities.",""],[1,"158","17","National Qualifications and Accreditation Framework for TVET","Develop national qualifications, national competency standards, testing, and accreditation of technical and vocational training courses and programs.",""],[1,"158","18","Expansion of Technical and Vocational Training Institutes","Expand the scope and number of technical and vocational training institutes across the country and actively promote the participation of the private sector in providing the required technical and vocational training.",""],[1,"158","19","Gender Equity in Technical and Vocational Training Access","Ensure gender equity in access to technical and vocational training opportunities.",""],[1,"167","2","Education Quality Improvement and Skills Training Partnership","The Royal Government will continue to strengthen its partnership with private sector and the national and international communities to enhance and improve the quality of education services paying more attention to information and foreign language training at all levels of general education, technical and vocational training, and in higher education as well, consistent with international standards and the country's development needs.",""],[1,"167","2","Vocational Training Policy Linked to the Labour Market","the government will continue to implement the vocational training policy linking with labour market in close cooperation with relevant parties through the following measures: (1) provide basic skills training to people in rural areas to increase income; (2) provide training or skill improvement to factory workers in cooperation with employers; (3) continue to expand technical and vocational training to provinces/municipalities, including entrepreneurship training program; and (4) establish National Agency for Profession and Employment, and Employment Centres in provinces/municipalities as a mechanism for dissemination of labour market information.",""]],"19":[[1,"68","7","Higher Education Scholarship Award Scheme","Equity for admission to higher education has been improved through scholarship award scheme for outstanding students, poor students, students from remote areas, and female students.",""]],"20":[[1,"65","4","Enhanced Health Services Delivery","The last, but not the least, of the \"growth\" rectangles of RS covers predominantly social sectors, viz., (2) ensuring enhanced health services;",""],[1,"70","6","Health Sector-Wide Management Approach","From early on RGC had adopted a health sector-wide management (SWIM) approach to guide the development of this sector.",""],[1,"71","17","Demand-Side Service Utilization Interventions","Demand side interventions are important to increase utilization of improved services through provision of clearly defined Continuum of Care of services.",""],[1,"77","10","Health Service Delivery Contracting and Special Operating Agencies","Contracting for health services delivery has been scaled up and institutionalized within the Cambodian public sector institutional context through a stronger focus on internal contracting and managerial autonomy through Special Operating Agencies in accordance with the RGC Policy on Service Delivery.",""],[1,"80","3","Health Sector Sub-Decree Implementation","To improve governance of the health care delivery system, a number of sub-decrees covering various aspects of the health sector are being implemented by the MOH.","MOH"],[1,"80","18","Strengthening Cooperation with External Partners","The MoH recognizes the importance of strengthening its cooperation with external partners","MoH"],[1,"81","1","Health Sector Support Program Phase 2","through Health Sector Support Program phase 2 and its Joint Partnership Agreement aligning partner investments behind MoH strategic and operational planning.","MoH"],[1,"81","2","Decentralization and Deconcentration Health Governance Reform","The on-going D&D reforms program will further strengthen this responsiveness.",""],[1,"166","2","Health Services Enhancement","The four sides or sub-components of this component of the Rectangular Strategy Phase II deal with: (ii) enhancing health services;",""],[1,"171","14","Sector-Wide Health Services Delivery Management","To ensure systematic development of health services delivery to the population, RGC adopted a Sector Wide Management (SwiM)",""],[1,"172","1","Health Sector Strategic Plan Implementation","A new HSP for 2008-2015 has been developed. It is now being implemented in close cooperation with all EDPs; as well as, work on implementing the Minimum Package of Activities (MPA) is progressing well.",""],[1,"172","1","Minimum Package of Activities Implementation","work on implementing the Minimum Package of Activities (MPA) is progressing well.",""],[1,"172","1","Priority Health Budget Allocation and Timely Fund Release","Health is one of the four priority sector for PAP, which ensures adequate allocation and timely releases of budgetary funds both for current and capital expenditures.",""],[1,"172","2","Health Strategic Plan Implementation","the Royal Government will continue to implement the Health Strategic Plan to reduce maternal mortality rate and infant mortality rate, and improve other health indicators by enhancing and expanding health services, especially reproductive, maternal, and infant and children services.",""],[1,"172","3","Communicable Disease Prevention and Treatment Program","The Royal Government is focused on the implementation of the program for prevention and cure of communicable diseases; construction of referral hospitals and health centres throughout the country that could provide effective, equitable and sustainable basic health services; and enhancement of quality of health professionals.",""],[1,"172","3","Referral Hospital and Health Centre Construction Programme","The Royal Government is focused on the implementation of the program for prevention and cure of communicable diseases; construction of referral hospitals and health centres throughout the country that could provide effective, equitable and sustainable basic health services; and enhancement of quality of health professionals.",""],[1,"172","3","Health Workforce Distribution and Incentive Measures","The Royal Government will ensure better distribution of doctors, medical workers and midwives in the health system; increase allowances for health staff working in rural areas; and increase the number of doctors, medical workers and midwives.",""],[1,"172","3","Health and Sanitation Education and Information Dissemination","The Royal Government will continue to pay attention to health and sanitation education; widely disseminate health information especially in rural areas; and provide services to the poor through the Equity Fund and health insurance system.",""],[1,"172","3","Equity Fund and Health Insurance Support for the Poor","The Royal Government will continue to pay attention to health and sanitation education; widely disseminate health information especially in rural areas; and provide services to the poor through the Equity Fund and health insurance system.",""],[1,"172","4","Decentralized Health Service Delivery and Management Devolution","The Royal Government will continue to take measures to: make health services more responsive and be available closer to people through decentralized service provision and devolution of management authority to sub-national levels such as national hospitals, referral hospitals and health centres;",""],[1,"172","4","Health Infrastructure, Equipment, and Technology Investment","increase investment in physical infrastructure, medical equipment and technologies;",""],[1,"172","4","Sector-Wide Health Governance Approach","strengthen governance in the health sector by implementing the Sector-Wide Approach emphasizing national ownership and partnership with the international community.",""],[1,"172","4","Private Sector Participation in Health Investment","Also, the Royal Government will continue to promote private sector participation in order to increase investment in health sector and strengthen public health intervention.",""],[1,"173","3","Expansion of Minimum and Complimentary Packages of Activity","Expand coverage of the Minimum Packages of Activity (MPA) and the Complimentary Packages of Activity (CPA) based on Health Coverage Plan with a focus on meeting client needs.",""],[1,"173","4","Integrated Health Service Delivery Support Systems","Strengthen health Service delivery support systems in an integrated manner.",""],[1,"173","5","Needs-Based Public Health Services and Interventions","Target public health services provision and public health interventions according to need.",""],[1,"173","6","Health Sector Quality Standards Framework","Develop and apply consistent standards of quality across the entire health sector (public, private and non-profit).",""],[1,"173","7","Health Service Contracting Models","Develop contracting models as part of a comprehensive approach to health services delivery.",""],[1,"173","9","Health Sector Funding Mobilization and Resource Efficiency Improvement","Seek increased funding from National Budget and improve efficiency in utilizing government resources allocated for health.",""],[1,"173","10","Health Development Cooperation Alignment and Coordination","Align development cooperation funding with MOH strategies, plans and priorities and strengthen coordination of development cooperation funding for health.","MOH"],[1,"173","11","Financial Barriers Reduction and Social Health Protection Mechanisms","Reduce financial barriers at the point of care and develop social health protection mechanisms.",""],[1,"173","15","Health Workforce Technical Skills Improvement","Improve technical skills and competence of health workforce.",""],[1,"173","16","Staff Professionalism and Ethics Strengthening","Strengthen staff professionalism, ethical conduct, and quality of work.",""],[1,"173","17","Health Sector Staff Distribution and Retention Improvement","Improve staff distribution and retention, with priority to personnel essential to health sector priorities.",""],[1,"173","18","Staff Remuneration and Performance Incentive Reform","Improve staff remuneration, salaries, and performance incentives.",""],[1,"174","24","Social Health Protection for Poor and Vulnerable Groups","Ensure social health protection, especially for the poor and vulnerable groups.",""],[1,"175","8","Pro-Poor Health Financing Systems","Implement pro-poor health financing systems.",""],[1,"175","16","Public Health Intervention Strengthening","Strengthen public health interventions to deal with cross-cutting challenges.",""],[1,"175","17","Public-Private Partnerships in Service Provision","Promote effective public and private partnerships in service provision.",""],[1,"175","18","Community Engagement in Health Service Delivery and Quality Improvement","Encourage community engagement in health services delivery and quality improvement.",""]],"21":[[1,"172","4","Health Research and Performance Monitoring Support","enhance support services and health research for policymaking, planning, performance monitoring and evaluation;",""],[1,"173","13","Health Sector Financing Policy Data and Monitoring System","Collect data and information required to develop and monitor health sector financing policy.",""],[1,"173","20","Health Information System Strengthening","Increase the availability of accurate, timely, and complete health data of high quality from public and private sources, together with enhanced coordination, and resources for the Health Information System (HIS).",""],[1,"173","21","Health Data Sharing and Management Improvement","Improve data sharing, management, analysis, dissemination and use across all levels of the health system, including population and socio-demographic data.",""],[1,"173","22","National Disease Surveillance and Non-Communicable Disease Response Strengthening","Improve the national disease surveillance system, public facility patient medical record system, and strengthen the case reporting, monitoring and response to non communicable diseases.",""],[1,"173","23","Private Sector Participation in the National Health Information System","Expand participation in the national HIS by the private sector, and facilitate data use for planning, resource allocation and management of human resources, infrastructure, and supplies.",""],[1,"174","1","Health Sector Harmonization and Alignment","Harmonize and align all activities within MoH and across the Health Sector to achieve HSP2 goals.","MoH"],[1,"174","2","Public-Private Partnership Development","Build public Private Partnerships.",""],[1,"174","3","Research, Policy Analysis, and Legislative Drafting Capacity Enhancement","Enhance capacity to conduct research, Policy analysis, and to draft Regulations and Legislation.",""],[1,"174","4","Institutional Capacity Strengthening for the Ministry of Health","Strengthen institutional capacity as part of MoH's institutional development efforts.","MoH"],[1,"174","5","Health Sector Stewardship Decentralization and Deconcentration","Strengthen MoH health sector stewardship through decentralization and de- concentration.","MoH"],[1,"174","6","Multi-Sector Health System Accountability Initiative","Mobilize multi-sector responses to enhance national health system accountability for access to quality health services for all.",""],[1,"175","5","Decentralized Service Delivery and Management Reform","Implement decentralized service delivery and management functions.",""],[1,"175","9","Health Legislation and Regulatory Strengthening","Reinforce health legislation, professional ethics and code of conduct, and strengthen regulatory mechanisms.",""],[1,"175","12","Health Information System and Health Research Strengthening","Strengthen and invest in health information system and health research.",""],[1,"175","19","Institutional Strengthening at All Levels","Systematically strengthen institutions at all levels.",""],[1,"175","20","Ministry of Health Operational Planning and Monitoring Framework","The MoH's operational framework, and its monitoring and evaluation functions are important tools to monitor and evaluate the overall health sector performance on a regular basis, to prepare information required for policy decision-making and to realign program services delivery, if necessary, to achieve the targeted goals and objectives of the programs; as well as to provide inputs for the preparation of Annual Progress Reports on the implementation of NSDP Update 2009-2013.","MoH"]],"22":[[1,"179","5","Reproductive Health Information Access Support","Support improved access to information and knowledge on reproductive health in communities, especially among disabled and pregnant women.",""],[1,"179","6","Women and Girls Nutrition Awareness Campaign","Promote nutrition of women and girls especially women of child bearing age by raising awareness on food security and nutrition among communities through information education communication materials and media.",""],[1,"179","7","Community Malaria Prevention Awareness Campaigns","Raise awareness among women at the community of the prevention and combating transmission disease through the implementation of information campaigns, training and the provision of basic information on malaria to target volunteers and communities.",""],[1,"179","8","HIV/AIDS Transmission Prevention for Women and Girls","Support prevention of HIV/Aids transmission in women and girls by facilitating the implementation of the strategic plan on women, girls and HIV/AIDS and increasing knowledge and support among communities to fight against immediate risk to women and the girl child.",""],[1,"180","8","Women's Health Care and Reproductive Health Access Improvement","Health sector by advocating for and monitoring improved access of women to health care and reproductive health services, especially focusing on addressing maternal mortality, and also increasing access to modern birth spacing methods and services; and increased water supply and sanitation facilities; supporting educational",""],[1,"181","1","HIV/AIDS Prevention Information and Awareness Campaigns","information campaigns; advocacy and monitoring and supporting information and awareness campaign for preventing HIV/AIDS transmission.",""]],"23":[[1,"78","6","Expansion of Social Protection and Health Safety Nets","RGC has and will continue to expand social-protection measures and other social safety nets to address this problem.",""],[1,"78","7","Community-Based Health Insurance Schemes","Currently, 12 CBHI schemes are being implemented in 11 ODs in 7 provinces and Phnom Penh Municipality, covering 81 HCS and 11 Referral Hospitals, and 73,828 beneficiaries.",""],[1,"79","1","PMG29 Program Implementation","The implementation of the PMG29 program of the RGC in the MOH started in 2006.","MOH"],[1,"79","1","MBPI Program Implementation","The implementation of MBPI program of the RGC has begun in 2009 in 6 provinces and 2 Central institutions30 covering 190 posts.",""],[1,"79","1","Midwifery Incentives for Safe Facility Deliveries","The provision of Midwifery Incentives to promote safe delivery at health facilities nation-wide has substantially increased deliveries at HCs and RHs attended by a skilled birth attendant from 39% in 2006 to 58% in 2008.",""],[1,"79","2","Midwife Recruitment and Training Capacity Expansion","A priority of the MOH is to increase recruitment and training capacity over the next five years, as well as to improve quality of the training.","MOH"],[1,"79","3","Performance-Based Pay System for Health Workers","MOH is looking at options to implement performance based pay system to improve management and delivery of health care services, as well as providing special incentives for those working in 'hard to reach' areas, together with improved national human resource planning and a more effective in-service training system.","MOH"],[1,"79","3","Special Incentives for Health Workers in Hard-to-Reach Areas","MOH is looking at options to implement performance based pay system to improve management and delivery of health care services, as well as providing special incentives for those working in 'hard to reach' areas, together with improved national human resource planning and a more effective in-service training system.","MOH"],[1,"79","3","National Health Workforce Planning and In-Service Training Reform","MOH is looking at options to implement performance based pay system to improve management and delivery of health care services, as well as providing special incentives for those working in 'hard to reach' areas, together with improved national human resource planning and a more effective in-service training system.","MOH"],[1,"79","3","Fast Track Interventions to Improve RMNCH Access and Quality","As a first step, the \"Fast Track Interventions to Improve Access and Quality of RMNCH\" is now being implemented.",""]],"24":[[1,"72","2","Tuberculosis DOTS Expansion and TB/HIV Collaboration","The coverage of the basic Directly Observed Treatments (DOTS) for tuberculosis (TB) has reached 100% of health center, while Community DOTS has been expanded to 506 health centers.",""],[1,"72","2","Public-Private DOTS Expansion","Public-private DOTS have also been expanded to 11 provinces and TB/HIV collaborative activities to 57 ODs.",""],[1,"72","2","Multi-Drug Resistant Tuberculosis Pilot Project","Multi-Drug Resistant TB project is being piloted.",""],[1,"72","5","Rapid Response Teams for Outbreak Detection and Response","Rapid Response Teams (RRT) have been established from National level down to Health Center Level.",""]],"25":[[1,"75","13","National Monitoring and Evaluation System Strengthening","The national M&E system needs further strengthening to better capture progress and results achieved by the national response28.",""],[1,"76","9","Expansion of Mental Health Services","Mental health services have been expanded gradually.",""],[1,"77","1","Cross-Sector Non-Communicable Disease Prevention and Monitoring","Dealing with non-communicable disease needs to be prevention, and to energize and monitor preventive measures across all sectors.",""],[1,"80","2","Health Information System Strengthening","A focus area for strengthening HIS is the provision of relevant and timely high quality health information for evidence-based policy formulation, decision making, program implementation, performance monitoring and evaluation by using appropriate communications and technology.",""]],"26":[[1,"186","8","Social Sector Services Expansion","It includes: resources to expand social sectors services to achieve CMDGs targets (2,050.0 billion CR or 500 million US$);",""]],"27":[[1,"65","4","Gender Policy Implementation","The last, but not the least, of the \"growth\" rectangles of RS covers predominantly social sectors, viz., (3) implementation of gender policy;",""],[1,"81","11","Women's Development Centres Vocational Training and Entrepreneurship Support","Eleven Women's Development Centres are now in place in provinces.",""],[1,"83","3","Finalization of Gender Mainstreaming Action Plans","Five other line ministries are in the process of finalising their GMAPs (Ministry of Justice; Ministry of Environment; Ministry of Public Works and Transport; and Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, and Ministry of Post and Telecommunications).","Ministry of Justice | Ministry of Environment | Ministry of Public Works and Transport | Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation | Ministry of Post and Telecommunications"],[1,"83","3","Financing and Technical Support for Gender Mainstreaming Action Plans","Ten line ministries have been provided resources from the National Budget or are receiving assistance from development partners to implement their GMAPs.","MLMUC | MRD | MoT | MLVT | MAFF | MoEYS | MoH | DOLA/MOI | MOP | MOC"],[1,"83","4","Strengthening National Gender Analysis and Advocacy Capacity","The national capacity for gender analysis, research and advocacy needs strengthening.",""],[1,"83","4","Harmonization of Gender Mainstreaming and Monitoring Frameworks","The harmonization of gender mainstreaming plans, sectoral strategic plans and monitoring machinery together with appropriate resource mobilization to implement sectoral GMAPS effectively is still a challenge.",""],[1,"181","4","Gender Equality Partnership and Coordination Mechanism","promote enhanced partnerships and coordination around gender equality and women's empowerment, including the development of a programme based approach.","MOWA"]],"28":[[1,"162","1","Employment Support and Social Safety Net Strengthening","The government has cooperated with national and international organizations and all relevant institutions to provide employment opportunities for, and reduce vulnerability of, the poor.",""],[1,"162","3","Coordinated Social Protection and Safety Net Strengthening","These developments have increased the level of urgency for RGC institutions to deal with social protection issues through a more coordinated approach in order to protect the significant gains that have been made in reducing poverty over the last decade; and to ensure that social safety nets are in place for workers (who make a contribution to the national economy) both in their working life and when they retire after reaching the legal retirement age.",""],[1,"162","4","Comprehensive Social Safety Net System","The Royal Government remains committed to developing and implementing a comprehensive and sustainable social safety net system aimed at protecting the livelihoods of the poor and most vulnerable segments of the population.",""],[1,"162","4","Social Safety Net Policy Development Consensus-Building","The Council for Agriculture and Rural Development (CARD) has taken some important steps to build consensus on the key concepts and broad direction for policy development on social safety nets for the poor and vulnerable segments of the population in collaboration with implementing line ministries.","Council for Agriculture and Rural Development (CARD)"],[1,"162","4","Social Protection Planning and Implementation Principles","Moving ahead on this important task, CARD will ensure that in planning for and implementation of social protection measures the following principles are adhered to:","Council for Agriculture and Rural Development (CARD)"],[1,"162","5","Social Protection Measures for Immediate Relief and Capacity Building","give preference to social protection measures that provide not only immediate relief but also contribute to building the beneficiary population's ability/capacity to contribute to the economic development of their communities.",""],[1,"162","5","Food for Work Rural Road Infrastructure Programme","Food for work programs to build rural road infrastructure that enables beneficiary populations' greater access to education and health services, and access to markets for their products;",""],[1,"162","5","Health Equity Fund and Agricultural Input Support Package","Health Equity Fund providing relief through health fee waivers, scholarships for education to build the skills base, and targeted distribution of agriculture inputs to smallholder farmers to improve productivity of their holdings and to generate income (seeds, fertilizer, extension services etc) are some good",""],[1,"163","2","Expansion of the ID Poor National Identification System","the program will be expanded to cover the whole country and periodically updated to remain a reliable source of data for targeting social safety net measures aimed at poor households.","Ministry of Planning"],[1,"163","3","Cross-Sectoral Social Protection Coordination with Decentralized Planning","Enhance cross-sectoral coordination and integration of social protection measures with decentralized development planning processes at the sub-national levels.",""],[1,"163","4","Social Safety Net Overhead Reduction","Minimize the planning and delivery costs (overheads) of social safety net programs to achieve a maximum net transfer of resources to the beneficiary populations.",""],[1,"163","5","Social Protection and Safety Net Delivery Programs","A number of RGC institutions are currently delivering social protection and safety net programs to assist individuals, households, and communities to better manage risks, shocks and extreme poverty.","Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation | Ministry of Labour and Vocational Training | Ministry of Women's Affairs | Ministries of Health, Education, Rural Development, and Economy and Finance"],[1,"163","5","Inter-Ministerial Safety Net Coordination and M&E Mechanism","RGC has now mandated CARD to setup an inter-ministerial coordination mechanism to monitor and evaluate the implementation of safety net interventions to strengthen food security and nutrition status of the vulnerable and the poor.","CARD"],[1,"163","6","Social Protection and Safety Nets Strengthening Programme","To implement RGC's priority policies to strengthen social protection and safety nets the Ministry's work will be concentrate on the following six areas:","Ministry of Social affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation"],[1,"163","7","Emergency Assistance Program Expansion","Continue to expand emergency programs to provide assistance to the victims and the vulnerable",""],[1,"165","3","National Social Safety Nets","Research and establish national security nets for general people",""]],"29":[[1,"64","4","Social Security Fund Management and Benefit Provision","The Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation (MoSAVY) is responsible for developing and managing the Social Security Fund and the National Social Security Fund for civil servants.","Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation (MoSAVY)"],[1,"64","4","Pension and Disability Payment Adjustment Mechanism","The pension of retirees and payments for work disabilities have been adjusted constantly in response to national economic growth.",""],[1,"64","5","Veterans Welfare Payment Scheme","A total of 87,875 families (families of dead veterans, disabled veterans; retired veterans and veterans losing their ability to work) have received regular payments from the government.","MoSAVY"],[1,"64","5","Cambodian Veterans' Association","The Cambodian Veterans' Association has been established to promote the interests of veterans and their families, protect their rights, raise their living standard and create a sense of solidarity and mutual help.",""],[1,"64","5","Veteran Sector Reform","Reforms of the veteran sector have improved the living conditions of veterans.",""],[1,"158","20","Social Security Law Enforcement and Contribution Collection Strengthening","Strengthen the enforcement of the provisions of the Law on Social Security, collection of contributions, the management of risk related to occupational safety, health care and pension benefits provisions of the social security system.",""],[1,"162","1","Pension and Benefit Enhancement for Civil Servants and Veterans","Also, the Royal Government has improved and strengthened social safety nets for retired civil servants and veterans by increasing pensions and other benefits.",""],[1,"162","2","Social Safety and Pension System Strengthening","To continue to implement social safety policies, the Royal Government of the Fourth Legislature will: give priority to improve working conditions for workers and employees, enforcement of Social Security Law, implementation of the principle of benefit and pension scheme for people with disabilities and their dependents; ensure protection of those covered by the Labour Law; and make available to all employees insurance coverage against workplace accidents.",""],[1,"162","2","Support for Persons with Disabilities and Veterans' Families","The Royal Government will continue to strengthen support to people with disabilities and families of veterans who sacrificed their lives for the nation.",""],[1,"162","2","Comprehensive Pension System for Retired Civil Servants and Veterans","Furthermore, the Royal Government will continue to support retired civil servants and veterans through implementing a comprehensive pension system under the National Social Security Fund.",""],[1,"162","2","National Social Security Fund Legislation","In this context, the government will work towards promulgation of a \"Law on the Comprehensive National Social Security Fund\" and a \"Law on the Establishment of National Pension for Veterans\".",""],[1,"165","1","Civil Servant Pension Expansion","Strengthen pension provision for retired civil servants and expand the pension scheme in terms of the availability the national budget",""],[1,"165","2","Strengthen Social National Security Fund Implementation for Civil Servants","Strengthen the implementation of the social national security fund for civil servants",""],[1,"165","4","Social Security Fund Bill for the General Population","Prepare a comprehensive bill on the social security fund for general people",""],[1,"165","6","Veterans Policy Implementation","Continue to implement national policies for veterans to recognize the good deeds of veterans who have made sacrifices for the country",""],[1,"165","7","Veterans Salary Management Reform","Continue to promote reforms in the management and provision of salary for veterans more effectively",""],[1,"165","8","Social Security Fund Bill and Veterans National Fund Sub-Decree","Prepare a bill on the social security fund and a sub-decree on the national fund for veterans",""],[1,"165","9","Veterans' Villages Construction Programme","Construct veterans' villages using the model of disabled solders' villages of Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen",""],[1,"165","10","Strengthening the Cambodian Veterans' Association","Strengthen the operations of the Cambodian Veterans' Association",""],[1,"166","1","National Social Safety Fund Expansion","The MoLVT will continue to further strengthen and broaden the scope of implementation of these three components.","Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training (MoLVT)"]],"30":[[1,"64","6","Social Services and Emergency Relief for Vulnerable Groups","The MoSAVY, also provides services to homeless and destitute people, emergency relief to people effected by natural and other disasters, victims of sex trafficking and inter- country human trafficking, protecting the four basic rights of children, promoting family values, and caring for orphan infants, orphan children, disable children, and children with HIV/AIDS.","MoSAVY"],[1,"64","7","Homelessness Support and Reintegration Programme","The six-point strategy of providing temporary shelters in social affairs' centers, psychology education services, health care services, and short-term vocational training services; and reintegrating vulnerable people into communities through the provision of support capital at the first stage and follow-up by local officials of the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation is being implemented.","Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation"],[1,"163","8","Homelessness Support Strategy Implementation","Strengthen the activities to address the problems of homeless people by continuing to implement the nine-point strategy and the existing mechanism effectively",""],[1,"163","9","Human Trafficking Victim Rehabilitation and Reintegration Support","Continue to combat human trafficking and; promote rehabilitation and reintegration of victims into communities by providing better follow-up support",""],[1,"163","9","Law Protecting the Rights of Human Trafficking Victims","making a law protecting the rights of the victims of human trafficking",""],[1,"163","9","Strengthening Social Affairs Centers for Victim Services","strengthen social affairs centers to ensure the provision of good services for the victims",""],[1,"163","10","Family Development and International Family Day Promotion","Strengthen and expand the building of good families, promote the roles of families and people in social development, and continue the annual organizing of International Family Day May 15",""],[1,"164","1","Social Services Support for Families Affected by HIV/AIDS","Increase efforts to provide social services to the families of women and children affected by HIV/AIDS.",""],[1,"164","2","Child Rights Implementation and Vulnerable Children Support Programme","Strengthen and expand the implementation of the four basic rights of children; mobilize forces to address the problems of orphan children, disabled children and children from poor families",""],[1,"164","3","Alternative Child-Care Policy Implementation","Keep implementing the policy on alternative child-care and a minimum standard for center-based child-care; strengthen orphanages of the government and those of NGOs and increase the effectiveness of child-care",""],[1,"164","4","Adoption Affairs Strengthening","Strengthen domestic and inter-country adoption-related affaires",""],[1,"164","5","Inter-country Adoption and Child Rights Legislation","Push for the passage of the law on inter-country adoption and law on child rights",""],[1,"164","6","Strengthen and Expand Child Protection Networks","Strengthen and expand the activities of the Cambodian National Council for Children and community-based child protection networks",""],[1,"164","7","Children's Values Promotion and International Children's Day Event","Promote three-model behavior of children-good child, good student and good friend-and organize International Children's Day June 1 annually",""],[1,"164","8","Morality and Decency Education Programs","Strengthen and expand education programs on morality and decency to prevent violence, crimes and substance abuse among children and youths",""],[1,"164","9","Youth Rehabilitation Center Expansion","Strengthen and expand youth rehabilitation centers",""],[1,"164","10","Protection of Children's Rights in the Justice System","Promote the protection of minor's rights in accordance with the convention on child rights within the justice and judicial system",""],[1,"164","11","Youth Sports, Camping, and Study Tour Promotion","Encourage sports activities, camping, study tours for children and young people",""],[1,"164","12","Advocacy for Inclusion of Children and Youth Needs in Development Plans","Support the advocacy of the inclusion of the needs of children and young people into national development plans at all levels",""],[1,"164","14","Multi-Sector Strategy for Orphans and Vulnerable Children Coordination","Coordinate the multi-sector strategy for orphans and vulnerable children",""],[1,"165","5","Support for Elderly Associations and Services","Support the establishment of retired civil servants' associations and elderly associations in communities; encourage families and communities to support the elderly without whom they can depend on for assistance; provide support services to the elderly; and organize Elderly International Day October 1",""]],"31":[[1,"9","26","Social Safety Nets for Civil Servants, Employees and Workers","Establishment of Social Safety Nets for Civil Servants, Employees and Workers",""],[1,"19","3","Fiscal Measures and Social Protection Safety Net Programs","RGC is now implementing a mix of fiscal measures and social protection and safety net programs to ensure that this does not happen.",""],[1,"19","3","Direct Action Programs to Uplift the Poor","Bold innovative programs of direct action to uplift the poor are urgently needed, which would also help accelerate the much needed \"transfer of net resources\" to the poor.",""],[1,"21","4","Expansion of Social Safety Nets for Vulnerable Groups","The RGC is therefore taking urgent measures to expand social safety nets for the most vulnerable through subsidies and targeted labour intensive work -- like food for work programs.",""],[1,"57","2","Social Safety Nets for Workers and Civil Servants","The four aspects of this rectangle are: (iv) establishment of social safety nets for civil servants, employees and workers.",""]],"32":[[1,"164","15","Disability Rights Policy and Law Implementation","Implement policies for the disabled; push for the implementation of the law on the protection and promotion of disabled people's rights; and promote the implementation of the international convention on the rights of people with disabilities",""],[1,"164","16","Disability Rehabilitation Services","Continue to sustain rehabilitation services for people with disabilities",""],[1,"164","17","Braille and Sign Language Training Services Expansion","Keep expanding Braille and sign language training services for disabled people and promote these services through IT systems",""],[1,"164","18","Vocational Training, Employment and Community Services for Persons with Disabilities","Promote vocational training, create jobs and provide community services as well as encourage a movement self-help for people with disabilities",""],[1,"164","19","Disabled People's Sports Promotion and Inclusion in Development Planning","Strengthen and expand disabled people's sports movement; organize sports, international events for people with disabilities; and include the needs of the disabled into development plans at all levels",""],[1,"164","20","Disability Inclusion and Anti-Discrimination Initiative","Continue to improve the understanding of disabilities among families, communities, employers and responsible agents in order to reduce the discrimination against disabled people; and continue to create more favorable environments for the disabled at all levels in order to ensure quality services and cut down physical, social, economic and politic obstacles",""]],"33":[[1,"18","1","Provincial and Rural Roads Improvement","attention is now being paid to accelerate improvement of provincial and rural roads.",""],[1,"48","14","Road Network Repair, Maintenance and Upgrading","RGC's key physical infrastructure priorities include repair, maintenance and upgrading of the road network from national to rural levels",""],[1,"48","14","Transport Network Rehabilitation and Construction","This rectangle of the Rectangular Strategy addresses issues dealing with: (i) further rehabilitation and construction of transport network",""],[1,"139","2","Multimodal Transport Network Rehabilitation and Reconstruction","The Royal Government of the Fourth Legislature will continue to give high priority to the rehabilitation and reconstruction of multimodal transport network connecting all parts of the country, and with neighbouring countries.",""],[1,"139","3","National Roads and Transport Infrastructure Rehabilitation Programme","The Royal Government will continue to accord high priority to the maintenance of national roads, the reconstruction of provincial and rural roads, the expansion of ports and the rehabilitation of railways, also in order to connect to the rail network of the neighbouring countries within the Greater Mekong Sub-region (GMS) framework.",""],[1,"139","4","Private Sector Road Maintenance Participation","The Royal Government will seek increasing private sector participation, through bidding processes, in routine and periodic road maintenance.",""],[1,"139","4","Provincial Public Works and Rural Development Capacity Strengthening","It will further strengthen the management and technical supervision and audit capacity of the Provincial Departments of Public Works and Transport and the Provincial Departments of Rural Development.",""],[1,"140","11","Public Works and Transport Policy Development","Formulating policies on development of Public Works and Transport, especially roads.",""],[1,"140","12","Road Development Strategy and Master Plan Revision","Formulating and updating (revise) strategies and Master Plans on the development of roads.",""],[1,"140","13","Road Management Legal Framework Reform","Formulating legal papers for strengthening of road management: Sub-Decree on the right of way and Road Law, etc ..",""],[1,"140","14","Road Numbering System Development","Preparing Road Numbering System managed by the Ministry of Public Works and Transport.","Ministry of Public Works and Transport"],[1,"140","15","Urban Sewage System Construction Along National Roads","Constructing of sewage systems in towns that are situated along National Roads.",""],[1,"140","17","Construction of Main National Roads","Continue the Construction of Main National Roads for the Integration in the Country and the Region by:",""],[1,"140","18","National Roads Rehabilitation Programme","Continuing the rehabilitation of remaining National Roads in order to connect provincial towns to the Capital and neighbouring countries.",""],[1,"141","1","Road Network Expansion and Ring Road Construction","Continuing to seek for funding for the enlargement of roads around Phnom Penh to have 4 lanes, and construction of ring roads around major city towns, widening RN1, RN4, and RN5 to 4 lanes.",""],[1,"142","22","Updated Road Network Development Master Plan Approval","Continue to revised and enhance the approval on the updated Road Network Development Master Plan in the Kingdom of Cambodia.",""]],"34":[[1,"32","4","Road Traffic Law Enforcement Promotion","In cooperation with relevant ministries, the MOI has promoted the enforcement of Law on Land Traffic to reduce road accidents.","relevant ministries"],[1,"49","13","National Safety Plan Information Dissemination","Preparing and disseminating information on National Safety Plan.",""],[1,"49","14","Road Safety Seminars and Workshops","Organizing seminars/workshops to promote road safety.",""],[1,"49","15","Road Safety Education Materials Dissemination","Producing educational material on road safety, and disseminating this material widely on Radios and TVs.",""],[1,"49","16","Road Safety Audit and Information Publication Training","Conducting trainings on auditing and publishing information on road safety.",""],[1,"49","17","National Road Safety Week","Organizing National Week of Road Safety, to be held from 7th to 14th April, every year.",""],[1,"49","18","Road Safety Training for Motorcycle License Applicants","Conducting trainings on road safety for the public as a part of the tests to get Motorcycle Driving License through the Provincial/Municipal Departments of Public Works and Transports.",""],[1,"50","1","On-site Road Safety Training for Motorcycle License Applicants","Preparing and implementing on-site training programs on road safety in low-income communities in the remote districts/areas as part of the testing to get the Motorcycle Driving License.",""],[1,"50","2","Motorcycle Driving Test Training Program","Conducting training programs as part of the Motorcycle Driving Test for adult youth in schools in Provinces and Cities countrywide.",""],[1,"50","3","Traffic Safety Action Plan and Helmet Campaign","Organizing a series of Seminars to formulate the Traffic Safety Action Plan, and promote the \"Helmet Campaign\".",""],[1,"50","4","Permanent Weighbridge and Mobile Scale Expansion","Work on 7 permanent weighbridge stations and 20 mobile scales is underway that is scheduled to be completed in 2009.",""],[1,"139","5","Roads Law and Transport Infrastructure Regulatory Reform","The Royal Government will speed up the adoption of the Law on Roads as well as supporting legal and regulatory framework for efficient management of transport infrastructure.",""],[1,"139","5","Traffic Safety and Transport Offences Enforcement Measures","The Royal Government will place emphasis on traffic safety and stricter measures against transportation offences, including overloaded carriers.",""],[1,"140","16","Road Signage and Lane Marking Installation","Installing road signs, lane markings and Kilometre Signs.",""],[1,"141","7","Vehicle Registration and Licensing Process Streamlining","Shorten the timing for registration of vehicles, making number plates, process for getting driving license, etc ..",""],[1,"141","8","Road Traffic Safety Strengthening","ii. Strengthen road traffic safety.",""],[1,"142","1","Road Traffic Law Enforcement Strengthening","Strengthen the enforcement of Road Traffic Law (promulgate on February 8th, 2007) and the Sub-decree on the Management of Garages that Repair and Transform Vehicles.",""],[1,"142","10","Join-Inspection Committee on Road Traffic Violation","Sub-Decree on the Establishment of Join-Inspection Committee on Road Traffic Violation;",""],[1,"142","12","Prakas on Sale and Bidding of Vehicle Registration Services","Draft a Prakas on Sale and Bidding of Vehicle Registration Services;",""],[1,"142","13","Driving License Scoring Procedures","Formulate Procedures on Scoring of Driving License;",""]],"35":[[1,"49","1","Private Sector Concession for Railway Network Development and Maintenance","To speed up the development of the railway network, RGC has decided to give the concession to the private sector for the development, operations and maintenance of the railway network.",""],[1,"49","1","Railway Network Rehabilitation and Expansion Programme","The rehabilitation, construction and development of the railway network that connects Phnom Penh to provinces and to the railway networks of the neighbouring countries, as part of the Asian Railway Network, is also a high priority of the RGC.",""],[1,"49","1","Transport Network Maintenance and Private Sector Participation","RGC has also given a high priority to ensuring that the transportation network is properly maintained and has encouraged and promoted the participation of the private sector in the operations and maintenance of the transportation network.",""],[1,"50","6","Railway Rehabilitation and Expansion Programme","Plans are now being prepared to rehabilitate and expand this important mode of transportation and its integration with the regional railways.",""],[1,"50","6","Railways Restructuring and Rehabilitation Committees","The Committee for Railways Restructuring and Rehabilitation and the Committee for the Management of Railways Concessions are now in place.",""],[1,"50","6","Railway Concession Implementation","Work is now underway to implement the concession agreement.",""],[1,"50","6","Railway Infrastructure Rehabilitation Project","To rehabilitate the railways infrastructure, a rehabilitation project funded by a loan agreement with the Asian Development Bank (ADB) is now being implemented.",""],[1,"50","6","Railway Network Rehabilitation Works","Through this project the following sections of the railways network will be rehabilitated: the missing link from Sisophon - Poipet 48 km (to connect to Thai railways); the line between Phnom Penh and Sihanouk Ville Port of 264 Km; and from Phnom Penh to Sisophon of 337 Km.",""],[1,"50","6","Supplementary Railway Financing and Upgrading Package","The Royal Government is also considering a supplementary financing agreement with ADB and a grant from AusAID (total about US$ 72 million) which will provide funding for a new station construction in Samrong (9 km from Phnom Penh) and additional upgrading of the railway, including branch line to Green Trade Warehouse (6 m from Phnom Penh) and Northern Line.",""],[1,"50","6","Batdeoung-Trapeang Sre Railway Link Feasibility Study","To construct the missing link from Batdeoung to Trapeang Sre (the railways connecting point on Cambodia-Viet Nam border) a engineering feasibility study is being carried out.",""],[1,"50","6","Cambodia-Thailand Railway Cross-Border Agreement Negotiations","The Royal Government has now assigned the Ministry of Public Works and Transport to carry forward these negotiations.","Ministry of Public Works and Transport"],[1,"139","3","Royal Cambodian Railway Privatization and Private Sector Participation Initiative","The Royal Government will make every effort to privatize the operations of Royal Cambodian Railway, and will encourage private sector participation in the rehabilitation of infrastructure and in transportation services.",""],[1,"141","21","Railway Rehabilitation and Thai Rail Connection","Speed up the rehabilitation of railways in both directions, and connection with Thai railway system.",""],[1,"141","22","Bak Deung to Lok Ninh Railway Project Study","Prepare study of a railway project from Bak Deung to Lok Ninh, Viet Nam in the scope of ASEAN Railway (Singapore-Kun Minh Railway Link \"SKRL\").",""],[1,"141","23","Railway Concession Agreement Implementation Enhancement","Enhance the implementation of the concession agreement by private sector (Toll Cambodia Co., Ltd) , on the management and operation of Cambodia railway.",""],[1,"142","8","Establishment of Railway Department in the Ministry of Public Works and Transport","Decree on the conclusion of Royal Railway of Cambodia (State enterprise) and establishment of Railway Department in Ministry of Public Works and Transport.","Ministry of Public Works and Transport"]],"36":[[1,"22","8","Aviation Infrastructure and Flight Safety Improvement","Further development of aviation infrastructure, including continuous improvement of flight safety, still continues to be a key priority to ensure the tourism development and absorption of increasing number of tourists to Cambodia.",""],[1,"50","7","Open Sea Port Strategy","RGC has been implementing its \"Open Sea\" Strategy.",""],[1,"51","3","Open Sky Airport Infrastructure Improvement Strategy","RGC has been implementing its \"Open Sky\" strategy.",""],[1,"51","3","International Airport Infrastructure Upgrading","the infrastructure of the 3 international airports has been significantly improved fostering the development of tourism.",""],[1,"51","3","Local Airport Repair and Preservation Programme","All of the 8 local airports are being repaired and preserved, rehabilitating runways and establishing airports boundaries.",""],[1,"51","3","Civil Aviation Human Resource Development","Development of human resources in civil aviation sector is a RGC priority to ensure further improvement of this sector in the future.",""],[1,"139","4","Open Sky Policy and Aviation Service Improvement","The Royal Government will continue to pursue the open sky policy, strengthen flight safety and enhance airport services.",""]],"37":[[1,"51","4","GMS Cross Border Transport Agreement Implementation","To implement this agreement, RGC has entered into bi-lateral MOU's with Thailand, Viet Nam, and Lao-PDR.",""],[1,"51","6","Cross-Border Transport Agreement Implementation at Poi Pet-Aranyaprathet Checkpoint","Two MOU's have been signed for implementing CBTA at Poi Pet- Ararnyaprathet check point.",""],[1,"51","7","CCA Construction and Additional Checkpoint Identification","Work is now underway to identify and construct the CCA, and the identification of additional Check-points.",""],[1,"51","8","Implementation of Traffic Rights Exchange MOU at Poipet-Arangpathed Border Checkpoint","Both side have agreed to de-link the 2 MOUs in order to allow the implementation of the MOU on the exchange of traffic rights (quota 40) at Poipet-Arangpathed border check point.",""],[1,"51","10","Cross-Border Customs Control Area Development","Work is now underway to identify and construct the CCA, and to establish Customs Procedures for inspection of goods and vehicles crossing the border, etc.",""],[1,"51","11","Implementation of GMS Cross-Border Transport Agreement Customs Procedures","Custom authorities from both sides have agreed and signed a MOU on custom procedures to implement of The Initiative in Implementation of GMS Cross Border Transport Agreement ( IICBTA ) at Bavet-Mockbai border check point.",""],[1,"52","5","Passenger Traffic Partnership Agreement Preparation","A separate Partnership Agreement on passenger traffic is under preparation that will require the approval of the Ministries of Public Works and Transport from both sides.","Ministries of Public Works and Transport"],[1,"52","8","Trilateral Cross-Border Transport Agreement Task Force","The three countries have agreed to set up a Task force for preparing a Trilateral Agreement between Cambodia, Lao PDR and Viet Nam on cross- border transport that will start in 2010.",""],[1,"121","4","Participation in Great Mekong Sub-Region and ACMECS Implementation","Actively participate in implementing the Great Mekong Sub-Region, Ayeyawada- Chao Phraya Mekong Economic Cooperation Strategy (ACMECS) focusing on the cross-border investment development, cross-border transportation, and investment along the borders.",""],[1,"121","5","Economic Corridors Forum Participation and Transport Infrastructure Rehabilitation","Actively participate in the development of the economic corridor through the Economic Corridors Forum of the Great Mekong Sub-Region with the active involvement of Provincial Governors Forum, and ensure the rehabilitation and construction of transport infrastructure needed to support the development of the GMS economic corridors to promote the development of the remote areas.",""]],"38":[[1,"141","15","Mekong River Transportation Focus","Continue to focus on transportation along the Mekong River from Phnom Penh to the Sea in Viet Nam.",""],[1,"141","16","Waterway Transport Agreement Formulation","Continue and finalize the formulation of the Waterway Transport Agreement between Cambodia and Viet Nam.",""],[1,"141","17","Waterways Master Plan Finalization and Implementation Preparation","Finalize the Waterways Master Plan and prepare for implementation.",""],[1,"141","18","Sihanouk Ville Port Second Project Implementation","Continue the implementation of the 2nd Project at Sihanouk Ville Port, funded by JBIC:",""],[1,"141","19","Special Economic Zone Infrastructure Construction","Construction of infrastructure for the settlement of a Special Economic Zone covering 70 hectares of port territory.",""],[1,"141","20","Multi-purpose Port and Special Cargo Berth Construction Project","A Construction Project of a Multi-purpose Port for serving logistical supports to the crude oil exploration at the open sea, and a Berth for special cargo in bulk.",""],[1,"142","11","Multimodal Transport Law Drafting","Draft a Law on the Multimodal Transport ;",""],[1,"142","14","Waterway Transportation Sub-Decree","Draft a Sub-Decree on Waterway Transportation;",""],[1,"142","15","Waterway Transportation Agreement Review and Maritime Draft Review","Continue to check the Agreement on Waterway Transportation with Viet Nam; Review the Draft on Kram on Maritime Transportation;",""],[1,"142","17","Authorization Prakas for Vessel Port Entry","Foster the endorsement of Draft Prakas on the Authorization for Vessels' Entrance Through Ports of the Kingdom of Cambodia;",""],[1,"142","18","Adoption of Draft Prakas on Security Within Port Zones","Foster the endorsement of Draft Prakas on the Security Within the Port Zones of the Kingdom of Cambodia;",""],[1,"142","20","Maritime Transportation and Ports Master Plan Endorsement","Foster the endorsement of a Master Plan on Maritime Transportation and Ports by the Royal Government;",""],[1,"142","21","Master Plan on Waterway Transportation Endorsement","Foster the endorsement of a Master Plan on Waterway Transportation in the Mekong River System of Cambodia.",""]],"39":[[1,"14","2","Systematic Measures to Mitigate the Global Financial Crisis Impact","The Royal Government is taking systematic and sequenced measures to mitigate the negative impact of the international financial cataclysm and global economic recession on our financial and economic system, and to protect our hard earned achievements.",""],[1,"21","2","Regional Cooperation and Integration Expansion","the Royal Government ... [will] strengthen and expand cooperation and regional integration in order to maximize benefits from our great economic potentials through expanding the scale of regional markets as well as trade and investment promotion in the region.",""],[1,"21","3","Economic Response Mechanism","The RGC response mechanism has adopted a two pronged approach, focusing on short-term and long-term actions.",""],[1,"21","3","Competitiveness Improvement and Economic Diversification Strategy","In order to build resiliency against the current global economic down turn and to sustain economic growth, Cambodia will be looking at ways to improve its competitiveness in the regional and international arena, as well as actively look for opportunities to diversify and expand the economic base.",""],[1,"21","3","Sector Diversification and Technology Development Support","Cambodia will continue to diligently explore new economic frontiers while nurturing existing and emerging sectors such as telecommunications and Information Communication Technology (ICT), light manufacturing, financial and securities market; and potential sectors such as alternative energy sources, oil exploration, mining; and processing technology to sustain productivity and competitiveness.",""],[1,"59","5","Cambodia-Vietnam Cross Border Market Committee","a Cambodia-Vietnam Cross Border Market Committee has been organized to develop the blue print for cross border market construction along Cambodia-Vietnam border in Memot and to prepare agreement on tariff free exports of Cambodia agricultural products to Vietnam.",""],[1,"60","2","Investment Promotion Environment","The Royal Government remains committed to creating an environment that encourage and promotes investments by both domestic and foreign investors in all priority sectors to broaden and diversify the economic base.",""],[1,"90","4","Economic Diversification and Competitiveness Policy Agenda","through a vigorous implementation of its socio-economic policy agenda for the Fourth Legislature articulated in Rectangular Strategy Phase II, in particular the implementation of policies to diversify and broaden the economic base and to improve competitiveness in the regional and international markets",""],[1,"105","1","Competitiveness Improvement and Economic Diversification Measures","As long-term measures, the RGC priority is to continue to address long term issues through improved competitiveness.",""],[1,"105","1","Economic Base Diversification and Expansion Initiative","RGC will be looking at ways to improve its competitiveness in the regional and international arena, as well as actively look for opportunities to diversify and expand the economic base.",""],[1,"105","4","Economic Competitiveness and Diversification Initiative","RGC will be looking at ways to improve its competitiveness in the regional and international arena, as well as actively look for opportunities to diversify and expand the economic base.",""],[1,"105","4","Regional Market Integration Strategy","RGC will strengthen integration of the Cambodian economy in the dynamic regional markets.",""],[1,"106","4","Trade Facilitation and Regional Economic Integration Strengthening","Further strengthening trade facilitation and integration of the Cambodian economy in the dynamic regional markets, in particular with the ASEAN, Greater Mekong sub-region (GMS) groups, and \"CLV\" discussions (Cambodia- Lao PDR-Viet Nam), will require RGC institutions with responsibilities for areas -- such as transportation infrastructure (roads, railways, ports, and airports), private sector development (especially the planning and development of Special Economic Zones), trade facilitation, and industrial development (in",""],[1,"121","7","Prudent Monetary and Budgetary Stabilization Measures","The Royal Government will pursue prudent monetary and budgetary policies in order to consolidate macroeconomic and financial stability by focusing on packaged measures to check inflation and/or influence its effects on the prices of basic goods such as food and fuel by implementing austerity measures and rationalizing consumption.",""],[1,"121","7","Physical Infrastructure Investment Programme","The Royal Government will continue to invest in physical infrastructure such as roads, irrigation systems, and electricity supply system, which can cut down costs and enhance productivity and economic efficiency as well as increase investment to promote agricultural productivity to be able to respond to the increasing food prices and to avail of the opportunity of higher demand for food in the world, thus promoting agricultural development in Cambodia.",""],[1,"122","1","Economic Diversification and Competitiveness Promotion","the Royal Government will continue to foster the diversification and strengthen the competitiveness of the Cambodian economy by assuring a highly conducive climate for both public and private (domestic and foreign) investments",""]],"40":[[1,"20","4","Export Market Diversification Initiative","To diversify the markets for our garments and other manufactured goods market to East Asia, the Middle East and Africa etc.",""],[1,"58","2","Bilateral Investment Promotion and Protection Agreements","To promote private sector investments, the Royal Government has signed bi-lateral agreements on the promotion and protection of investments with 7 neighbouring countries, and 17 agreements with other countries in the Middle East, East Asia, and Europe.",""],[1,"58","9","Product Association Organization and Market Integration Support","The MOC has also provided assistance in organizing product associations to improve production capacity and to integrate products into local markets, nich markets, and world markets.","MOC"],[1,"59","1","Trade Fairs and Foreign Trade Partner Business Meetings","It has organized \"Trade fairs\" to promote local products and organized several business meetings with foreign trade partners for individual products to solve the problem of product congestion and to facilitate the flow of products to the world market.",""],[1,"120","3","Trade Liberalization and Market Access Expansion","the Royal Government will make further strides on the path of trade liberalization aimed at free movement of goods and services within the country and between Cambodia and her trade partners.",""],[1,"120","3","Export Market Access Support for Cambodian Products","The Royal Government will continue to create access for Cambodian products, without barriers and obstacles, to extensive regional and world markets.",""],[1,"120","4","APEC Membership Pursuit and ASEAN Community Participation","the Royal Government of the Fourth Legislature will pay priority attention to the further integration of Cambodia into the region and the international community by pursuing membership of Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation (APEC) forum and participating in the building of the ASEAN Community.",""],[1,"120","4","WTO Compliance Legislation and Enforcement","it is necessary for all ministries/agencies to pay attention to and fulfil the duties of Cambodia's membership in the WTO by adopting laws and regulations and ensure their effective enforcement to meet the requirements of the WTO.",""],[1,"120","5","Inter-Ministerial Coordination Strengthening","the Royal Government will continue to further strengthen inter-ministerial coordination",""],[1,"120","5","Legal and Regulatory Alignment for Membership Obligations","adopt laws and regulations required to meet the obligations of membership in international and regional organizations",""],[1,"120","5","Institutional Capacity Building for Law Enforcement","strengthen capacity of the concerned RGC institutions to manage and effectively enforce the adopted laws and regulations",""],[1,"121","2","APEC Membership Negotiation and Regional Integration Participation","Engage in discussions/negotiations to become a member of Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation (APEC) forum, and continue to participate in building the ASEAN community and Network of East Asia.",""],[1,"121","3","ASEAN Plus Partnership Promotion and Center Establishment","Actively promote the creation of ASEAN + China, ASEAN + Korea, ASEAN + Australia-New Zealand as well as establishing ASEAN + China and ASEAN + Korea Centers.",""]],"41":[[1,"154","2","Agro-processing and Assembly Industry Promotion","the Royal Government will promote a favourable climate for developing the agro-processing industry, and assembling industry including electronic and machinery assembly.",""],[1,"154","2","Special Economic Zones Legal Framework Reform","the Royal Government will continue enhancing necessary legal framework, especially creating the law for the efficient operations of Special Economic Zones.",""],[1,"154","3","Public-Private Partnership Promotion for Infrastructure Investment","The Royal Government will continue promoting the public and private sector partnership for investment especially for physical infrastructure projects.",""],[1,"154","4","Private Sector Enabling Environment and Investment Promotion Measures","To implement RGC priority policies for the Fourth Legislature the highest priority of all concerned RGC institutions is to support the creation of an enabling environment that fosters private sector development by taking measures to alleviate major bottlenecks to private sector development.",""],[1,"154","5","Investor Single Window Service Strengthening","The Cambodian Investment Board of the Council for the Development of Cambodia (CIB/CDC) has operated a \"single window service\" for investors for many years in order to reduce the administrative burden of seeking approval for new investment projects.","The Cambodian Investment Board of the Council for the Development of Cambodia (CIB/CDC)"],[1,"154","5","Investor Aftercare and Tracking System","During the Fourth Legislature, this mechanism will be further strengthened and streamlined and a new \"Investor Aftercare\" mechanism, as well as, an \"Investor Tracking System\" will be developed and implemented.","The Cambodian Investment Board of the Council for the Development of Cambodia (CIB/CDC)"],[1,"154","5","Investment Promotion and Coordination for Priority Sectors","The CIB/CDC and the Ministry of Commerce will continue to actively promote new investments in the priority economic sectors to diversify and broaden the economic base, develop and widely disseminate information on investment opportunities in priority sectors to potential private sector investors, and strengthen coordination among concerned RGC institutions to promote a sense of joint responsibility for enhancing the competitiveness of private sector businesses.","The Cambodian Investment Board of the Council for the Development of Cambodia (CIB/CDC) | the Ministry of Commerce"],[1,"154","6","Special Economic Zones Implementation Strengthening","The Council for the Development of Cambodia will further strengthen the implementation of the Special Economic Zones (SEZ) and will ensure that the locations of the SEZ's are suitable for maximizing the integration of Cambodia's economy into the region.","The Council for the Development of Cambodia"],[1,"154","7","Government-Private Sector Forum Coordination Mechanism","The Royal Government will continue to",""],[1,"155","1","Government-Private Sector Coordination and Public-Private Partnership Strengthening","explore new ways to further strengthen this Government-Private Sector coordination mechanism and to build public-private partnerships.",""]],"42":[[1,"154","1","Private Sector Legal and Regulatory Support Reform","the Royal Government will continue to: strengthen the supportive legal framework for the private sector including laws and regulations, and administrative procedures",""],[1,"154","1","Fair Competition Promotion Measures","ensure fair competition",""],[1,"155","28","Draft Commercial Legislation Submission","At the end of 2009, the Ministry of Commerce will submit the following 3 draft laws to the Office of the Council of the Minister for review and approval:","Ministry of Commerce | Office of the Council of the Minister"],[1,"156","2","Commercial Law Reform Package","the Ministry of Commerce will submit the following draft laws for review and adoption: (1) the Competition Law (already developed); (2) the E-Commerce Law (already developed); (2) the Consumer Protection Law (being developed); and (4) he Trade Remedy Law (being developed).","Ministry of Commerce"],[1,"156","3","Commercial Agents Law Review and Adoption","At the end of 2011, the law on Commercial Agents will be submitted for review and adoption.",""]],"43":[[1,"37","8","Government-Private Sector Forum Cooperation Mechanism","Already, the cooperation efforts such as through the Government Private Sector Forum are much appreciated by the private sector and are bearing fruit as manifest in the robust growth of private sector investments.",""],[1,"38","1","Private Sector Partnership Strengthening","deepen the harmonious and symbiotic relationships with the private sector, based on strict adherence to the laws and regulations and focused on development priorities.",""],[1,"124","1","Government Private Sector Forum for Investment and Business Environment Reform","The Government Private Sector Forum has provided a regular forum for the Royal Government to address issues on foreign investment promotion and improvement of the business and trade environment.",""],[1,"124","3","Private Sector Engagement and Dialogue Enhancement","Built on the success so far of the mechanism of dialogue between the Royal Government and the private sector in the Government Private Sector Forum, the Royal Government will make effort to further enhance participation of the private sector in the discussions to ensure not only the development of the sector itself but also its strategic importance and contribution to the wider socio-economic development of the country.",""]],"44":[[1,"57","2","Private Sector Strengthening and Investment Promotion","The four aspects of this rectangle are: (i) strengthening private sector and attracting investments (including garment and tourism sectors);",""],[1,"57","2","Small and Medium Enterprise Promotion","The four aspects of this rectangle are: (ii) promotion of small and medium enterprises;",""],[1,"57","2","Job Creation and Improved Working Conditions","The four aspects of this rectangle are: (iii) Job creation and ensuring better working conditions for workers and employees; improved work conditions; and (iv) establishment of social safety nets for civil servants, employees and workers.",""],[1,"57","2","Business Cost Reduction and Market Access Expansion","RGC has brought down the costs of doing business and expanded market access, reduced in-country transportation costs and improved safety through improved basic infrastructure that also promotes integration of urban and rural economies.",""],[1,"57","5","Single Window Investment Approval Mechanism","the Royal Government has created a \"Single Window\" mechanism through which investors can complete all paper requirements to seek approval of their proposed investment projects.","Cambodian Investment Board of the Council for the Development of Cambodia (CIB/CDC)"],[1,"57","5","Decentralized Approval of Small Investment Projects","To reduce further the administrative burden of seeking approvals of investment projects of less than 2 million US$, the RGC has decentralized the authority to review and approve these projects to provincial authorities.",""],[1,"58","1","Investor Aftercare and Investor Tracing System","The CIB/CDC has also established an \"Investor Aftercare\" mechanism and an \"Investor Tracing System\" to provide support to investors in getting their approved projects underway and to monitor progress on the implementation of the approved investment projects.",""],[1,"58","1","Streamlining and Improvement of Investor Services","A high priority of the Royal Government is to continue to streamline and improve the delivery of investor services by strengthening the technical capabilities of officials, in particular at the mid levels, at the national and sub- national levels.",""],[1,"58","3","Business Registration and Trade Facilitation Measures","The Ministry of Commerce (MOC) has been working on streamlining the procedures for new business registration, provding market information, organizing product associations, implementing \"better factories\" program, trade facilitation and promotion, and enforcement of intellectual property laws.","Ministry of Commerce (MOC)"],[1,"58","7","Electronic Business Registration System","In 2013, the Ministry of Commerce will develop an electronic system for business registration.","Ministry of Commerce"],[1,"59","2","Phnom Penh Chamber of Commerce Training and Support","Phnom Penh Chamber of Commerce that was established in 1995, has been providing training for trainers, as well as support to the Provincial Chambers of Commerce.",""]],"45":[[1,"159","2","SME Business Climate Improvement Measures","The Royal Government of the Fourth Legislature will continue to improve the business climate for small and medium enterprises development focusing on four main aspects: (1) legal and regulatory framework - facilitating registration particularly via internet system, defining procedures and principles for inspection and certificate of origin for import and export, and adoption of a sub-decree on trade facilitation through risk management; (2) financing - creation of financial leasing companies, and strengthening governance and financial reports; (3) supportive actions for small and medium enterprises - promoting innovation and technology as well as financing for small and medium enterprises, and strengthening and widening other supportive services, (4) integrating small and medium enterprises into a global value chain and preventing all kinds of smuggling.",""],[1,"159","3","National Productivity Center Establishment","the Royal Government will promote implementation of new measures including: establishing of the National Productivity Center in order to improve productivity and reduce production costs",""],[1,"159","3","National Standards Institute Establishment","establishing a National Standards Institute to ensure product quality conforming with regional and international standards",""],[1,"159","3","National Testing Laboratories Establishment","establishing national testing laboratories for physics, chemistry, micro-biology, and mechanics in order to evaluate quality and set prerequisite criteria for products",""],[1,"159","3","Industrial Property Rights Protection Mechanism Strengthening","strengthening industrial property rights protection mechanism in order to promote innovation, adoption of new techniques and new technology",""],[1,"159","3","Skills Improvement Training Programme","imparting training to improve skills",""],[1,"159","3","Legal Framework Strengthening for Industry","strengthening the relevant legal framework",""],[1,"159","4","One Village-One Product Movement","The Royal Government continues to promote the \"one village-one product\" movement by encouraging inventions, entrepreneurship, and self-confidence in rural areas.",""],[1,"159","4","Regional Technical Training for Special Products","The Royal Government will promote technical training for special products within some regions in the context of strengthening quality and expanding markets which are critical for further support to and participation in this movement.",""],[1,"160","3","Industrial and SME Support Policy Development","Formulate policies to support industry and SMEs.",""],[1,"160","5","Industrial Property Rights Policy Reform","Formulate and implement policies for industrial property rights issues.",""],[1,"160","6","Metrological Capacity Strengthening Policy","Formulate and implement policies to strengthen capacity to deal with metrological issues.",""],[1,"161","1","Fiscal and Non-Fiscal Support Measures for Prioritized Industries","Taking appropriate actions to improve fiscal and non- fiscal measures to support prioritized industries.",""],[1,"161","4","Technology and Technique Improvement Policy Development","Formulating policies and strategies to improve techniques and technologies.",""],[1,"161","6","Producer Productivity and Technique Training Programme","Providing trainings on productivity- and technique-related subjects to producers.",""],[1,"161","7","Productivity and Technique Advisory Services","Establishing advisory services for productivity- and technique-related issues.",""],[1,"161","8","Expansion of R&D Centre Internet Connectivity","Enhancing and expanding the use of R&D centres through internet.",""],[1,"161","10","Industrial Property Rights Protection Services","Strengthening and providing protection services for industrial property rights.",""],[1,"161","11","Industrial Property Rights Awareness and Training Programme","Raising awareness and providing training on industrial property rights.",""],[1,"161","12","Centre for Creative Initiatives and Innovations","Establishing centre for creative initiatives and innovations and strengthening its operations.",""],[1,"161","14","Intellectual Property Rights Stakeholder Engagement and Registration Support","Strengthening relationship with intellectual property right agents and applicants for certification and registration.",""],[1,"161","15","Industrial Property Rights Advisory Services","Establishing advisory services for industrial property rights.",""],[1,"161","17","Industrial Property Rights Policy Formulation and Implementation","In Program area #7, Formulate and implement policies for industrial property rights issues, the MIME will take the following actions:","MIME"],[1,"161","18","National Metrology Legal and Regulatory Framework","Putting in place legal and regulatory framework and technical regulations for the management of national metrological32 processes.",""],[1,"161","19","Metrology Management Infrastructure Development","Establishing metrology management infrastructure including national metrology centre and control and verification centre in 5 regions.",""],[1,"161","20","Metrology Training and Dissemination Programme","Disseminating and providing training on metrology- related subjects.",""]],"46":[[1,"150","25","Phnom Penh-Vealrinh 230KV Transmission Line Completion","230KV transmission line connecting Phnom Penh-Vealrinh substation to be completed in 2013.",""],[1,"153","9","Physical Infrastructure Investment for Private Sector Development","To facilitate private sector development, the Royal Government of the Fourth Legislature will continue to accord priority to improve physical infrastructure through increased public investment in transportation networks, including roads, railways, waterways (river, sea), and air routes;",""],[1,"153","9","Electricity Generation and Distribution Expansion","to increase the electricity generating capacity and expand the distribution network in urban and rural areas to provide energy at a reasonable rate;",""],[1,"153","9","Clean Water Supply Network Expansion","to enhance and widen the clean water supply network;",""],[1,"153","9","Cultural and Natural Tourism Infrastructure Development","and to enhance and expand infrastructure system for cultural and natural tourism sector.",""]],"47":[[1,"37","2","Banking Prudential Regulation Strengthening","to increase confidence in the banking system and to mitigate any potential effects the National Bank of Cambodia took proactive measures to strengthen prudential regulation of the banking system, increased the reserve requirement rate from 8% to 16% in the banking system, placed a 15% credit ceiling on the real estate sector, improved credit rating system of the banking sector, and strengthened the credit information sharing system.","National Bank of Cambodia"],[1,"37","2","Modern Enterprise Banking Systems and Risk Management Guidance","The National Bank of Cambodia has also required banks to develop a modern enterprise system based transaction mechanism by improving the code of conduct, encouraging good corporate governance, and provided guidance to banks on risk management.","National Bank of Cambodia"],[1,"37","4","Amendment of the Banking and Financial Institutions Law","the NBC is working on amending the scope of the Law on Banking and Financial Institutions to keep the legal framework up-to-date with market changes.","National Bank of Cambodia (NBC)"],[1,"37","4","Financial Intelligence Unit for Anti-Money Laundering and Counter-Terrorism Financing","The NBC has established a Financial Intelligence Unit to implement the Law on Anti-Money Laundering and Combat the Financing of Terrorism, passed in 2007.","National Bank of Cambodia (NBC)"],[1,"37","5","Financial Sector Development Strategy Implementation","The RGC has continued to vigorously implement the Financial Sector Development Strategy 2006-2015.",""],[1,"90","4","Accommodative Monetary Policy and Financial Sector Support","the National Bank of Cambodia's rapid response has included a dramatic easing of and accommodative monetary policy and implementing wide-ranging measures to support and strengthen the financial and banking system.","National Bank of Cambodia"],[1,"90","6","Financial Sector Strengthening and Bank Recapitalization","to further strengthen the financial sector in order to rebuild market confidence and to attract new private capital.",""],[1,"94","5","Financial Sector Development Strategy Implementation","The National Bank of Cambodia (NBC), the monetary authority, will continue to vigorously implement RGC's \"Financial Sector Development Strategy 2006-2015\"","National Bank of Cambodia (NBC)"],[1,"94","5","Financial Crisis Mitigation Policies","The National Bank of Cambodia will continue to aggressively pursue policies needed to mitigate the potential adverse effects of the global financial crisis and the economic downturn on the Cambodian economy, the financial sector, and the vulnerable and poor segments of the population.","National Bank of Cambodia"],[1,"94","6","Monetary Policy Toolkit Enhancement and Market-Based Monetary Framework Development","The NBC will continue to enhance its monetary tools kit and to further develop a market- based monetary framework by:",""],[1,"95","1","Monetary Policy and Liquidity Management Mechanism","Encouraging a money supply and liquidity monitoring mechanism, strengthening the reserve requirement system, setting up an efficient overdraft system, preparing to issue central bank paper, and enhancing the lender of last resource mechanism.",""],[1,"95","4","Microfinance and Banking Sector Improvement","Improving the microfinance and banking sectors.",""],[1,"95","5","Promotion of Non-Banking Financial Institutions","Encouraging non-banking financial institutions.",""],[1,"95","8","Legal and Banking Supervision Framework Reform","Enhance the legal infrastructure: to continue to improve the legal framework, regulations and banking supervision entities, in particular, prepare a draft to amend the Law on Banking and Financial Institutions to govern uniformly the economic and financial sector.",""],[1,"95","9","Banking Supervision and Internal Audit Capacity Strengthening","Develop human resource: to further improve the implementation of laws and regulations, and strengthen banking supervision capacity and NBC's internal audit functions.",""],[1,"95","10","Financial Sector Liberalization and Competition Promotion","Liberalize and promote competition: by strengthening the licensing regulations and putting in place infrastructure required to support new innovations in the financial sector and the diversification of the financial sector.",""],[1,"95","11","Bank Problem-Solving System Upgrade and Exit Strategy","Upgrade reliability and validity: of the problem solving system and insolvency of banks in order to formulate and implement an exit strategy to systematically withdraw the special measures put in place to deal with the effects of the global financial crisis and the economic downturn.",""],[1,"96","1","Non-Bank Financial Sector Regulatory Review and Supervisory Delegation","Reviewing the laws and regulations that govern the non-bank financial sector.",""],[1,"96","4","Foreign Exchange Market Monitoring and Regulation Upgrade","Enhancing the monitoring of exchange market: by upgrading and regulating the foreign exchange market business.",""],[1,"105","3","Accommodative Monetary Policy and Financial Sector Support Measures","the National Bank of Cambodia's has responded rapidly by adopting a easing and accommodative monetary policy and implementing wide-ranging measures to support and strengthen the financial and banking system.","National Bank of Cambodia"]],"48":[[1,"37","4","Support for Microfinance Linkages to Rural Banking Services","The National Bank of Cambodia (NBC) has actively supported microfinance institutions, both domestic and overseas partners, to link banking services to rural areas.","National Bank of Cambodia (NBC)"]],"49":[[1,"95","12","Microfinance Services Expansion","The NBC will take action required to expand the scope of the microfinance services that are urgently needed to meet the requirements of small businesses and rural communities, in particular small land holder farmers.",""],[1,"95","12","Comprehensive National Microfinance System","The main objective is to put in place a comprehensive and efficient microfinance system that covers all parts of the country.",""],[1,"95","13","Microfinance Regulatory Framework Strengthening","Enhance the regulatory framework: by continuing to build NBC's capacity to strengthen the regulatory framework and the effectiveness of microfinance supervision, including any prudential regulations to build public confidence in using microfinance services.",""],[1,"95","14","Microfinance Institution Licensing and Regulation Reform","Strengthen microfinance institutions: encouraging unregistered NGOs to become licensed, law-abiding microfinance institutions enjoying the right to collect deposits.",""],[1,"95","15","Microfinance Network Expansion","Expand microfinance network: by fostering growth through the granting of licenses to microfinance institutions to reinforce management, expand operational networks, increase capacity and efficiency, and produce more profits in order to satisfy the borrowing requirements of people living in remote areas.",""],[1,"95","16","Microfinance Literacy and Basic Training Programme","Build Capacity: by providing basic training to people, in particular, poor people, to understand microfinance services such as savings and the proper use of loans to generate income and improve their living standards.",""],[1,"95","17","Expansion of Credit Information System to Microfinance Institutions","Strengthen Information infrastructure: by enhancing the expansion of the credit information system to microfinance institutions and reinforce the financial linkages between microfinance institutions and commercial banks.",""],[1,"95","17","Strengthening Financial Linkages Between Microfinance Institutions and Commercial Banks","Strengthen Information infrastructure: by enhancing the expansion of the credit information system to microfinance institutions and reinforce the financial linkages between microfinance institutions and commercial banks.",""],[1,"95","18","Development of Non-Bank Financial Institutions","The National Bank of Cambodia will continue to develop non-bank financial institutions, in order to deepen the financial sector by:","The National Bank of Cambodia"]],"50":[[1,"20","6","Agricultural Sector Diversification and Agro-processing Support","To prioritize the use of resources and expertise of the government, and donors to broaden and diversify our agricultural sector, in order to attract more quality investments in agri-business and improve agricultural trade linkages, land reform, agricultural diversification and agro-processing.",""],[1,"41","3","Post-Harvest Management and Agro-Industry Promotion","Improve post-harvest management; promote export and domestic markets for agricultural products (including rice - not merely paddy, fruits and vegetables); promote agro-industry including post-harvest processing; improve quality of standard of agricultural products; organise farmers' organisations for better bargaining power; aim for optimum use of land and other resources; and, encourage and increase private sector investments and participation.",""],[1,"41","3","Private Sector Investment Promotion in Agriculture","encourage and increase private sector investments and participation.",""]],"51":[[1,"40","4","Agricultural Research and Extension System Strengthening","Improve and strengthen agricultural research and extension systems",""],[1,"40","12","Agricultural Market Access Promotion","Promote market access of agriculture products.",""],[1,"41","1","Agricultural Productivity and Farmer Support Programme","Increase productivity in rice and other crops; increase and improve access to extension services, credit and inputs; increase irrigation; ensuring better benefits for farmers through marketing;",""],[1,"41","3","Agricultural Producer Organization and Bargaining Power Support","organise farmers' organisations for better bargaining power;",""],[1,"41","4","Local Agricultural Extension and Farmer Partnership Mechanisms","Establish mechanisms at local level that can provide techniques and services to the farmers; promote program of agricultural extension at local level; and promote the formation of farmer to be effective and partner with private sector.",""]],"52":[[1,"127","4","Agricultural Productivity and Diversification Reform Package","To this end, the Royal Government's policies main goal is to promote agriculture productivity and diversification as well as land, fisheries and forestry reforms by addressing in package issues of agriculture technology, rural infrastructure such as roads, irrigation system and electricity and credits, markets and processing-technology, especially for exports.",""],[1,"127","4","Agricultural Institutional Coordination Mechanism","This requires institutional mechanisms and highly effective coordination for sector-wide progress and qualitative changes.",""],[1,"127","5","Agriculture Productivity and Diversification Improvement","The Enhancement of the Agriculture Sector Rectangle consists of four elements: (i) improving agriculture productivity and diversification; (ii) land reform and clearing of mines; (iii) fisheries reform; and (iv) forestry reform.",""],[1,"128","2","Agricultural Productivity and Diversification Programme","The Royal Government of the Fourth Legislature will continues to place priority on increasing agricultural productivity and diversification as well as promoting agro-industries.",""],[1,"128","2","Integrated Agricultural Intensification and Rural Support Package","This will be achieved through an integrated approach including increased proper use of improved agricultural inputs, agricultural extension, research and development, construction and maintenance of the rural infrastructure, especially irrigation network, expansion of rural credit and microfinance, agricultural market development, organization of farmer communities and better management of agricultural land.",""],[1,"128","2","District-Level Agricultural Extension Expansion","the Royal Government will make further efforts to expand the system of technical and agricultural extension services by rolling them out to the district level and creating linkages with a community level volunteer network as well as with the agricultural services being provided within the framework of various development projects.",""],[1,"128","2","Multipurpose Farm Promotion Initiative","The Royal Government will encourage multi-purpose farms in order to increase productivity in animal husbandry and multi-crops farming through integrated farming.",""],[1,"128","4","Agriculture Sector Strategy Update and Sector-Wide Implementation Programme","the Ministry of Agriculture, Fisheries and Forestry (MAFF) will continue its work on updating the Agriculture Sector strategy and seeing support ot implement the strategy through a sector-wide programme.","Ministry of Agriculture, Fisheries and Forestry (MAFF)"],[1,"128","5","Agricultural Productivity, Diversification, and Agro-Industry Promotion","Continue to place priority on increasing agricultural productivity and diversification as well as promoting agro-industries.",""],[1,"129","1","Intensive Farming and Agricultural Productivity Enhancement","Continue to pay attention to increased production by shifting from extension of cultivated area to intensive farming on the existing land.",""],[1,"129","2","Expansion of Technical and Agricultural Extension Services","Expand the system of technical and agricultural extension services by rolling them out to the district level and creating linkages with a community level volunteer network as well as with the agricultural services being provided within the framework of various development projects.",""],[1,"129","4","Multi-Purpose Integrated Farming Promotion","Encourage multi-purpose farms in order to increase productivity in animal husbandry and multi-crops farming through integrated farming.",""]],"53":[[1,"134","2","Fishing Community Participation and Technical Training Support","The Royal Government of the Fourth Legislature will continue to attach priority to helping and encouraging fishing communities to participate in the preparation of plans and the management of natural resources by providing guidance and technical training in order to ensure sustainable management of fishery resources based on technical standards.",""],[1,"134","2","Fishing Lot Demarcation","To this end, the Royal Government will ensure the proper demarcation of the fishing lots.",""],[1,"134","3","Effective Fish Market Mechanism","the Royal Government will establish an effective fish market mechanism",""],[1,"134","5","Aquaculture Support Package for Fish Farmers","the Royal Government will provide a package of assistance to fish farmers, which will include technology, seed, credit and market.",""],[1,"134","5","Fisheries Law Enforcement Strengthening","The improvement in law enforcement through the existing mechanism continues to be the priority of the Royal Government in preservation of fisheries resources.",""],[1,"134","6","Sustainable Fisheries Management and Development","To implement RGC's priority policies for the Fourth Legislature, the Fisheries Administration will focus its efforts to strengthen the management, conservation, and development of sustainable fisheries resources to contribute to ensuring people's food security and to contribute to socio-economic development in order to enhance people's livelihoods and the nation's prosperity.",""],[1,"135","3","Sustainable Fisheries Resource Management","Ensure effective management and utilization of fisheries resources in a sustainable manner in order to enhance food security and food safety and to contribute to poverty alleviation.",""],[1,"135","4","Community Fisheries and Fish Refuge Development","Encourage the establishment and improvement of community fisheries and Community Fish Refuges in inland and coastal areas in order to enhance the management of sustainable fisheries resources by empowering local communities.",""],[1,"135","5","Responsible Aquaculture Development Initiative","Encourage the development of different kinds and scales of aquaculture, both inland and coastal to be a broad national movement, by implementing the 'Regional Code of Conduct for Responsible Aquaculture.'",""],[1,"135","6","Fish Processing and Packaging Development Initiative","Develop fish processing and packaging by encouraging large-scale investments and improving the fisheries infrastructure to increase competitiveness and market access.",""],[1,"135","8","Fisheries Conservation Awareness and Community Participation Programme","Increase awareness of people in fishing communities and general fishermen to the importance of conservation of fisheries resources and ensuring maximum participation from local communities with respect to fisheries management and conservation.",""],[1,"135","10","Fisheries Sector Human Resource Development","Promote human resource development within the fisheries sector to ensure quality service within fisheries in order to improve socioeconomic development.",""],[1,"135","11","Fisheries Research Promotion Programme","Encourage and promote fisheries research programs.",""],[1,"135","12","Fisheries Revenue Allocation and Reform Financing Procedure","Giving priority to using fisheries revenue through special financial procedures in order to achieve fisheries reforms, research conservation, development and surveillance.",""]],"54":[[1,"148","10","Electricity Supply Expansion and Energy Security Programme","In the Fourth Legislature, the Royal Government will attach priority to increase electricity supply capacity and reduce tariff to an appropriate level while strengthening institutional mechanism and management capability.",""],[1,"148","10","Low-Cost Power Generation Development","the Royal Government will encourage the construction of low cost electricity generating plants by using local energy sources such as hydro power, natural gas, and coal.",""],[1,"148","10","High-Tech and Non-Traditional Power Development","the Royal Government will explore possibilities of developing high-tech power plants including nuclear and non- traditional energy, and will pursue the import of electricity from neighbouring countries.",""],[1,"148","10","National Electricity Transmission Network Expansion","the Royal Government will encourage construction of electricity transmission lines covering all parts of the country to enable the supply of quality and low cost energy from all sources to meet the demand in cities, provinces, urban and rural areas; and will gradually integrate Cambodia's electricity energy system into the networks of the Greater Mekong Sub-region (GMS) countries and ASEAN.",""],[1,"149","1","Rural Electrification Expansion","the Royal Government will continue to attach priority to accelerate rural electrification, including the use of renewable energy.",""],[1,"149","6","Electricity Supply Capacity Expansion and Tariff Reduction","Increasing electricity supply capacity and reduce tariff to an appropriate level while strengthening institutional mechanisms and management capability.",""],[1,"149","11","Promotion of Local Energy Sources","Promote the use of local energy sources such as hydro power, natural gas, and coal.",""],[1,"149","12","Energy Source Diversification for Electricity Generation","Promote the diversification of energy sources for electricity generation.",""],[1,"149","14","Regional Energy Trade Cooperation","Promote regional energy trade through bi-and multi-lateral cooperation.",""],[1,"149","15","Reserve Generating Capacity Creation","Ensure energy security though the creation of reserve generating capacity.",""],[1,"150","2","Electricity Import from Vietnam for Phnom Penh Supply","Import 200 MW from Vietnam in 2009 to supply power to Phnom Penh.",""],[1,"150","3","Electricity Import from Vietnam for Kampong Cham","Import 20 MW from Vietnam in 2009 to supply power to Kampong Cham.",""],[1,"150","4","Electricity Import from Lao PDR to Supply Stung Treng","Import 20 MW from Lao PDR in 2009 to supply power to Stung Treng.",""],[1,"150","5","Kirirom Hydropower Station 3 Completion","Complete work on the Kirirom Hydropower Station 3 to provide an additional 18 MW in 2010.",""],[1,"150","6","Kamchay Hydropower Station Completion","Complete work on the Kamchay Hydropower Station to provide an additional 193 MW in 2010.",""],[1,"150","7","Imported Coal-Fired Electricity Plant Completion","Complete work on the Electricity plant powered by imported coal to provide an additional 200 MW in 2010.",""],[1,"150","8","Power Import from Thailand to Supply Banteay Meanchey","Import an additional 60 MW from Thailand in 2010 2009 to supply power to Banteay Meanchey.",""],[1,"150","9","Imported Coal-Fired Electricity Plant Completion","Complete work on the Electricity plant powered by imported coal to generate 100 MW in 2011 to serve coastal areas.",""],[1,"150","10","Stung Atai Hydropower Station Completion","Complete work on the Stung Atai Hydropower Station in 2012 to generate 120 MW.",""],[1,"150","17","Electricity Transmission Network Expansion","The Ministry of Industry, Mine and Energy will expand the electricity transmission network by carrying out the following projects:","Ministry of Industry, Mine and Energy"],[1,"150","18","Stung Treng-Lao PDR 115 kV Transmission Line Completion","115KV transmission line connecting Stung Treng-Lao PDR to be completed in 2009.",""],[1,"150","19","230KV Transmission Line Completion","ii. 230KV transmission line connecting Takeo-Kampot- a substation in Kampot provincial town to be completed in 2009.",""],[1,"150","20","230 kV Transmission Line to Sihanoukville","230KV transmission line connecting Kampot Provincial town-Sihanoukville- a substation in Sihanoukville to be completed in 2009.",""],[1,"150","21","230 kV Phnom Penh-Kampong Chhnang-Pursat-Battambang Transmission Line Completion","230KV transmission line connecting Phnom Penh-Kampong Chhnang-Pursat- Battambang to be completed in 2010.",""],[1,"150","22","230KV Transmission Line Completion Project","230KV transmission line connecting Stung Atai hydropower station-Osom substation and 230KV transmission line connecting Osom substation-Pursat substation to be completed in 2012.",""],[1,"150","23","230KV Transmission Line Completion","230KV transmission line connecting Phnom Penh-Kampong Cham provincial town-Skun substation to be completed in 2012.",""],[1,"150","24","115 kV Transmission Line Completion","115KV transmission line connecting Phnom Penh-Neakloeung-Prey Veng-Svay Rieng-Vietnam to be completed in 2012.",""]],"55":[[1,"48","14","Power Sector Efficiency and Rural Electrification","RGC's key physical infrastructure priorities include ... creation of an efficient power sector, rural electrification",""],[1,"48","14","Energy Sector and Electricity Network Development","This rectangle of the Rectangular Strategy addresses issues dealing with: (iii) development of the energy sector (including oil and gas) and electricity network",""],[1,"54","15","Energy Sector Development Plan","To guide the development of the energy sector, an Energy Sector Development Plan, 2005-2024 has been prepared.",""],[1,"54","15","Rural Electrification Master Plan","A Rural Electrification Master Plan focusing on the use of renewable energy has also been prepared and is being implemented.",""],[1,"55","4","Rural Electrification Fund","the Royal Government has established a Rural Electrification Funds to promote equity in access to electricity supply services and encourage private sector to participate in investing in rural power supply services in a sustainable manner, in particular to encourage the use of new technologies and renewable energy.",""],[1,"55","5","GMS Power Trade Plan Implementation","Cambodia has been participating in the implementation of GMS Power Trade Plan",""],[1,"55","5","ASEAN Power Grid Implementation","within the framework of ASEAN, Cambodia is participating in the implementation of ASEAN Power Grid",""],[1,"56","3","Hydroelectric Generation Capacity Expansion","such as for installing more hydro-electric generation capacity",""],[1,"56","3","National Grid Transmission Line Expansion","transmission lines for a national grid",""],[1,"56","3","Rural Electrification Programme","rural electrification",""]],"56":[[1,"55","10","Offshore Oil and Gas Exploration Programme","The Cambodian National Petroleum Authority (CNPA) has signed contracts with a number of companies from various countries to explore for oil and gas in six other blocks in Cambodian gulf waters.","Cambodian National Petroleum Authority (CNPA)"],[1,"55","10","Oil and Gas Development Infrastructure Investment","Once the deposits levels are estimated, further work and investments are needed for setting in place the development infrastructure before pumping could commence, currently expected in 2011.",""],[1,"55","10","Coordinated Advance Planning for Petroleum Resource Management","Coordinated advance planning should start now to carefully conserve and use this energy resource and potential revenues from it in an optimal manner to benefit Cambodia and its citizens in the immediate and long term.",""],[1,"55","11","Extractive Revenue Maximization and EITI Governance Review","Get maximum revenues to the state through multi-layered returns such as by way of royalties, profit sharing, taxes, etc.","MEF | RGC"],[1,"55","12","Sector Governance and Regulatory Oversight Mechanism","Set up mechanisms and bodies to guide this sector and monitor operations by ensuring strong regulatory oversight, transparency, and clear separation of policy, regulatory and operational aspects.",""],[1,"56","1","Associated Gas Utilization Planning","Consider and prepare plans for use of substantial associated gas which would otherwise go to waste by flaring.",""],[1,"56","2","Downstream Resource Processing and Industrial Use Units","Set up downstream units for processing and use of the resource for value-addition and for industrial use including fertiliser production.",""],[1,"56","3","Priority Projects and Feasibility Studies Preparation","Prepare and get ready a list of priority projects and feasibility studies for using the additional financial resources",""],[1,"61","8","Oil and Gas Exploration Programme","Exploration work for oil and gas reserves is now well underway",""],[1,"61","8","Bauxite Exploration Initiative","Exploration for bauxite has commenced in north-eastern provinces",""],[1,"61","8","Environmental and Revenue Regulation for Extractive Industries","Careful regulations and procedures need to be in place to ensure environmental sustainability, in-country value-added processing, and maximising revenues to the state.",""],[1,"92","5","Oil Sector and Energy Investment Promotion Policy","Adopt policies to foster investment in the oil sector and in energy resources more generally and to ensure that investment regimes are stable and predictable, encourage greater cooperation and synergies between national and international concerned agencies through well designed partnerships.",""]],"57":[[1,"149","2","Private Sector Energy Infrastructure Investment Promotion","The Royal Government will accord high priority to encourage the private sector to invest in energy infrastructure, including generation, transmission and distribution.",""],[1,"149","2","Environmental and Social Safeguards for Energy Projects","The Royal Government will make further efforts to mitigate adverse effects on environment and society in the implementation of energy projects while safeguarding economic efficiency of each project.",""],[1,"149","2","Electricity Sector Capacity Building and Institutional Reform","Attention will also be paid to capacity building and institutional reform in the Electricity Authority of Cambodia (EAC), Electricity Du Cambodge (EDC) and other relevant ministries and agencies to improve management efficiency and the quality of electricity supply.","Electricity Authority of Cambodia (EAC) | Electricity Du Cambodge (EDC)"],[1,"149","3","Oil and Gas Sector Policy and Regulatory Framework Development","the Royal Government will develop policy, legal and regulatory framework for the sector in order to ensure efficient management and resources utilization for economic development and improvement in livelihoods of the Cambodian people.",""],[1,"149","8","Energy Sector Policy, Legal and Regulatory Framework Development","Developing policy, legal and regulatory framework for energy sector in order to ensure efficient management and resources utilisation for economic development and improvement in livelihoods of the Cambodian people.",""],[1,"149","13","Private Sector Energy Infrastructure Investment Promotion","Encourage the private sector to invest in energy infrastructure, including generation, transmission and distribution.",""],[1,"149","17","Electricity Sector Capacity Building and Institutional Reform","Carry out capacity building and institutional reform in the Electricity Authority of Cambodia (EAC), Electricité du Cambodge (EDC) and other relevant ministries and agencies to improve management efficiency and the quality of electricity supply.","Electricity Authority of Cambodia (EAC) | Electricité du Cambodge (EDC)"]],"58":[[1,"20","7","Infrastructure and Energy Generation Investment","To further invest in infrastructure development, particularly energy generation to reduce energy costs to the private sector and to the community.",""]],"59":[[1,"176","28","Domestic Violence Prevention and Victim Protection Law Implementation","The government is implementing the Law on Prevention of Domestic Violence and Protection of the Victim",""],[1,"176","28","Human Trafficking Suppression Law Implementation","The government is implementing the Law on Suppression of Human Trafficking and",""],[1,"177","3","Domestic Violence Law Enforcement and Victim Protection","the Royal Government will effectively enforce the Law on Domestic Violence and Protection of Victims by providing effective and timely legal protection to victims, who are mostly women and children, in collaboration with all relevant institutions and development partners",""],[1,"178","5","National Program on Social Morality and Family Values","Foster harmony in the family and society and promote the status of women by implementing the National Program on Social Morality, the Value of Women and Khmer Family Values; increasing public awareness of, and taking action to prevent indecent acts and the spread of pornographic material.",""],[1,"178","7","Legal Protection and Prevention of Violence Against Women and Children","Promote legal protection from domestic violence, rape, sexual assault, human trafficking, sexual and labour exploitation by implementing the DV and Human Trafficking Law and the National Action Plan to Combat Violence against Women and the National Action Plan to Suppress Trafficking in Humans and Sexual Exploitation; developing database and information systems on all forms of violence against women and girls, human trafficking, sexual and labour exploitation; and raising public awareness and support for preventing violence against women and children.",""],[1,"178","8","Institutional Capacity Building for Legal Protection of Violence and Trafficking Victims","Increase the capacity of relevant institutions for effective legal protection for victims of violence, rape, human trafficking, and sexual and labour exploitation by capacity building and awareness raising of relevant authorities at all levels on laws and regulations related to prevention of violence against women and children, and human trafficking; supporting networking among officials of police, court and health institutions to respond to cases of violence against women and children and human trafficking; advocating for an increase in the number of women police, and prisons officers; capacity development of judicial police officers; facilitating the development",""],[1,"179","1","Implementation of Domestic Violence Law Regulations","implementation of all necessary regulations to implement the DV law, including administrative decisions and protection order to protect the victim",""],[1,"179","2","Victim Support Centres and Shelters Expansion","Improve access to and provision of social and health services for victims of violence, rape, human trafficking, and sexual and labour exploitation by promoting an increase in the number of centres and shelters;",""],[1,"179","2","Victim Care Regulations and Service Guidelines","preparing and revising regulations on care provision for victims, and guidelines for social services for victims at centres;",""],[1,"179","2","Staff Capacity Development for Victim Services","promoting capacity development of staff at the centres and staff providing consultation services",""],[1,"179","3","Anti-Trafficking Cooperation and Monitoring Action Plan","Strengthen international and regional cooperation to prevent trafficking in humans, labour exploitation, and sexual exploitation by implementing activities and monitoring the National Action Plan; continuing to implement international agreements and regional commitments and action plans such as the MOU of the Greater Mekong Sub regional committee; and monitoring and reporting on national and international commitments, including to the United Nations.",""]],"60":[[1,"40","9","Forestry Reform for Sustainable Forest Conservation and Management","Forestry reform - promote sustainable conservation and management of forests, ensure better management of natural protected areas.",""],[1,"45","9","Forest Law Enforcement and Forest Resource Management","The implementation of the Law on Forestry and regulations along with good collaboration between all concerned institutions, forest resources are now more strictly managed, resulting in increased prevention and suppression on illegal forest land grabbing.",""],[1,"45","9","Reforestation, Community Forestry, Boundary Demarcation, and Wildlife Conservation","Reforestation/tree plantings, community's forestry establishment, forest boundary demarcation, and wildlife research and conservation were actively carried out as planned.",""],[1,"45","9","Local Authority Instructions on Forest Protection","The Ministry of Interior plays an important role in issuing instructions to all level of local authorities to strengthen statistics, movement and resettlement of new incomers, and not to allocate forest areas for other purposes.","Ministry of Interior"],[1,"46","1","Implementation of State Forest Land Use Sub-Decree for Forest Plantations","implementation of sub-decree on rules on the use of state forest lands for forest plantation will contribute towards achieving Cambodian Millennium Development Goals that set a target of 60 percent forest cover in 2015.",""],[1,"135","14","Sustainable Forestry Management and Forest Protection Measures","Besides banning logging for the present, the Royal Government has established protected and biodiversity conservation areas, undertaken reforestation, formed forestry communities, taken up proper boundary demarcation and strict measures to prevent, reduce and eradicate illegal encroachments and occupation of forest land by private individuals.",""],[1,"135","15","Forest Communities Monitoring and Evaluation Program","Accordingly, the Royal Government of the Fourth legislature will continue to monitor and evaluate the effectiveness and efficiency of this program",""],[1,"136","1","Private Commercial Forest Plantation Development","the Royal Government encourages the private sector to establish commercial forest plantations in degraded forest land based on agreed technical standards.",""],[1,"136","2","Forest Concession Monitoring and Compliance Enforcement","The Royal Government will continue to monitor forest concessions to ensure that they comply with international standards by seeking external technical and financial assistance and by active and appropriate participation of civil society in monitoring.",""],[1,"136","2","Forestry Law Enforcement and Anti-Encroachment Measures","The Royal Government will continue to strictly enforce the Law on Forestry and take serious measures against forestry crimes, and will continue to educate people to be aware of obligations to protect forests and stop illegal forest encroachments.",""],[1,"136","5","Program Monitoring and Evaluation for Forest Community Development","Continue to monitor and evaluate the effectiveness and efficiency of this program in terms of the improvement of livelihoods of the rural people, the sustainability of forest resources, and the expansion of forest communities.",""],[1,"136","6","Private Sector Commercial Forest Plantation Promotion","Encourages the private sector to establish commercial forest plantations in degraded forest land based on agreed technical standards.",""],[1,"136","7","Forest Concessions Compliance Monitoring","Continue to monitor forest concessions to ensure that they comply with international standards by seeking external technical and financial assistance and by active and appropriate participation of civil society in monitoring.",""],[1,"136","8","Forestry Law Enforcement and Public Awareness Campaign","Continue to strictly enforce the Law on Forestry and take serious measures against forestry crimes, and will continue educate people to be aware of obligations to protect forests and stop illegal forest encroachments.",""]],"61":[[1,"136","11","Environmental Impact Assessment Requirement for Development Projects","will implement measures that will require the carrying out of Environmental Impact Assessments of proposed development projects before implementation",""],[1,"137","4","Genetic Access and Benefit-Sharing Draft Law","Preparing draft law on Genetic Access Benefit Sharing and Traditional Knowledge.",""],[1,"137","5","Chemical Substance Management Draft Law","Preparing draft law on Chemical Subsistence Management",""],[1,"137","6","Water Pollution Control Law Preparation","Preparing law on water polluted control",""],[1,"137","7","Solid Waste Management Law Preparation","Preparing law on solid waste management",""],[1,"137","8","Environmental Protection Law Review and Pilot Testing","· Reviewing and experiment law on environmental protection",""],[1,"137","9","Chemical Substance Classification and Signage Sub-Decree","Preparing sub-decree on classify and put sign for chemical subsistence",""],[1,"137","10","Sub-decree on Genetically Modified Organisms","Preparing sub-decree on life genetic modify organism",""],[1,"137","19","Environmental Impact Assessment Guideline Development","Preparing guidelines on prepare environmental impact assessment report",""],[1,"137","20","Environmental Impact Assessment for Development Projects","In the area of environmental impact assessment, the MOE will ensure sustainable use of natural resources and economic sustainability of the sector by conducting environmental impact assessments before development projects are implemented by:","MOE"],[1,"137","21","Environmental Impact Assessment Capacity Strengthening","Strengthening technical capacity on environmental impact assessment to national city and provincial level technical staff",""],[1,"137","22","Environmental Impact Assessment Legislation and Policy Revision","Preparing and edit legislation and policy relevance to environmental impact assessment",""],[1,"137","23","Environmental Management Plan Monitoring and Compliance Control","Strengthening monitoring control on implement environmental management plan that has informed in environmental impact assessment report and agreement environmental protection of project owner and development activities.",""],[1,"137","28","Solid Waste Management Implementation","Implement solid waste management in safety environment",""],[1,"137","30","Laboratory Quality and Competence Strengthening","Strengthen quality and competence laboratory",""],[1,"137","31","Technical Capacity and Public Awareness Strengthening","Strengthen technical capacity and enhance public awareness",""]],"62":[[1,"136","3","Reserved Forest Management and Eco-Tourism Development","the Royal Government will enhance management efficiency of the reserved forests and ensure their appropriate protection and development, including eco-tourism, for employment generation and additional income for the people.",""],[1,"136","3","Protected Areas Management","Moreover, attention will be given to the management of the protected areas.",""],[1,"136","9","Reserved Forest Management and Eco-Tourism Development","Enhance management efficiency of the reserved forests and ensure their appropriate protection and development, including eco-tourism, for employment generation and additional income for the people.",""],[1,"136","9","Protected Areas Management","Moreover, attention will be given to the management of the protected areas.",""],[1,"137","1","Protected Areas Management Strengthening","Strengthen management of protected areas in order to eliminate anarchy in Protected Areas, eliminate illegal exploitation of natural resources, control land clearing for use, and illegal cutting down of the forests.",""],[1,"137","11","Natural Resources Protected Foundation Sub-Decree","Preparing sub-decree on Natural resources protected foundation",""],[1,"137","12","Protected Areas Sub-Decree Preparation","Preparing sub-decree on determine protected areas",""],[1,"137","13","Sub-decree on Determination of Natural Protected Areas","Preparing e sub-decree on determine natural protected areas",""],[1,"137","15","National Park Sub-Decree for Phnom Kulen","Preparing sub-decree on determine national park Phnom Kulen",""],[1,"137","16","Marine National Park Sub-Decree Preparation","Preparing sub-decree on determine marine national park",""],[1,"137","17","Protected Area Sub-Decree Preparation","Preparing sub-decree on Natural resources protected area",""],[1,"137","18","Sub-decree on Establishing Natural Resources Protected Areas","Preparing sub-decree on establish Natural resources protected area of provincial and capital level",""],[1,"137","35","Protected Areas Mapping and Data Management Initiative","Prepare map, landmark define area and data management in natural protected areas",""],[1,"138","1","National Plant and Marine Park Establishment","Prepare establish National plant and marine park",""],[1,"138","2","Potential Area Definition and Community Living Conditions Study in Protected Areas","Define potential area and study community living condition in natural protected areas",""],[1,"138","3","Community Management Strengthening in Protected Areas","Strengthen community management in natural protected areas",""],[1,"138","4","Wetlands, Biosphere, and Coastal Zone Conservation Management","Strengthen management and conservation of Wetlands, multiple use land, biosphere reservation, and coastal zones",""]],"63":[[1,"142","16","National Oil Spill Readiness, Prevention, and Cooperation System","Draft a Sub-Decree on the Establishment of a National System for Readiness, Prevention, and Cooperation to Deal with Oil Spill;",""],[1,"142","19","National Oil Spill Risk Prevention Plan","Formulate a National Plan to Prevent Risks Caused by Spilled Oil;",""]],"64":[[1,"146","16","Private Sector Participation Promotion and Social Protection Regulations","Draft and enact regulations and build partnerships with private sector to promote private sector participation and to provide protection and subsidies to the poor.",""],[1,"146","17","Public Water Supply Authority Management Strengthening","Strengthen the management of public water supply authorities to improve the delivery of services, in particular to the poor.",""],[1,"146","19","Private Sector Participation Promotion and Social Protection Measures","Draft and enact regulations and build partnerships with private sector to promote private sector participation and to provide protection and subsidies to the poor, the MIME will:",""],[1,"147","1","Private Investment Guideline Manual for Drinking Water Supply","Prepare a guideline manual on procedures and principles for private investment in drinking water supply.",""],[1,"147","2","Drinking Water Production and Supply Prakas","Prepare Prakas on production and supply of drinking water.",""],[1,"147","3","Water Production Cost Policy Prakas","Prepare Prakas on policy for water production cost.",""],[1,"147","4","Review of Private Water Supply Company Tariffs","Examine the water production costs set by private water supply companies in all urban centres.",""],[1,"147","5","Regulatory Unit Capacity Strengthening for Drinking Water Department","Strengthen capacity of regulatory unit of Drinking Water Department.",""],[1,"147","6","Sub-national Consultation on Drinking Water Regulation Roles","Organize consultations with sub-national authorities in order to reach an agreement on the role and responsibility of each entity in the drafting and enactment of regulations for drinking water supply.",""],[1,"147","7","Sub-national Drinking Water Regulation Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen capacity of sub-national authorities in the drafting and enactment of regulations for drinking water supply.",""],[1,"147","8","Private Sector Investment Regulations for Drinking Water Supply","Enact regulations for the promotion of private sector investment in drinking water supply.",""],[1,"147","9","Private Service Provider Capacity Strengthening for Drinking Water Supply and Bookkeeping","Strengthen private service providers' technical capacity in drinking water supply and in bookkeeping.",""],[1,"147","10","SME Development Projects for Drinking Water Supply","Implement SME development projects for drinking water supply in Cambodia.",""],[1,"147","11","Urban Drinking Water and Sanitation Studies","Conduct studies on development programmes for drinking water supply and sanitation in urban centres.",""],[1,"147","12","Government-Private Sector Forum for Drinking Water Supply and Sanitation Partnership","Promote partnership with private sector within the framework of Government-Private Sector Forum on drinking water supply and sanitation.",""],[1,"147","13","Public Water Supply Authority Management Strengthening","Strengthen the management of public water supply authorities to improve the delivery of services, in particular to the poor, the MIME will:",""],[1,"147","14","Drinking Water Supply Authority Improvement Studies","Conduct studies on improving quality, business efficiency, and governance of drinking water supply authorities.",""],[1,"147","15","Monitoring of Public Drinking Water Supply Authorities","Monitor the status of progress in the operations of public drinking water supply authorities.",""],[1,"147","16","Review of Public Drinking Water Production Costs","Examine the drinking water production costs set by public drinking water supply authorities except for the autonomous ones.",""],[1,"147","17","Training and Capacity Building for Public Drinking Water Supply Authorities","Implement training and capacity building projects for public drinking water supply authorities in 8 municipalities.",""],[1,"147","18","Association of Public Drinking Water Supply Authorities","Foster the establishment of association of public drinking water supply authorities.",""]],"65":[[1,"48","14","Water Supply and Sanitation Improvement","RGC's key physical infrastructure priorities include ... improved water supply and sanitation",""],[1,"52","9","Sewage, Drainage, and Wastewater Filtration System Rehabilitation and Construction","The Ministry of Public Works and Transport is also responsible for the rehabilitation, construction and maintenance of the sewage/drainage and waste water filtration systems.","Ministry of Public Works and Transport"],[1,"52","9","Siem Reap Water Treatment Station Expansion","A water treatment station in Siem Reap is under construction with a plan to expand the work to include dredging of Steung Siem Reap.",""],[1,"52","9","Kampot Wastewater Filtration Station Feasibility Study","Plans for construction of a waste water filtration station in Kampot are currently being studied.",""],[1,"54","9","Subsidized Water Charges for Poor Households","17,590 poor households, many of which are female-headed households, have been receiving support through a policy of subsidised charges for water use based their income.","The Ministry of Industry, Mines and Energy (MIME)"],[1,"147","19","Drinking Water Supply and Sanitation Expansion Projects","Implement drinking water supply and sanitation expansion projects for poor communities in 5 municipalities.",""],[1,"147","20","Drinking Water Supply and Sanitation Expansion Projects for Poor Communities","Conduct studies on and developing drinking water supply and sanitation expansion projects for poor communities in 5 municipalities.",""],[1,"147","21","Drinking Water Supply Authority Rehabilitation Projects","Conduct studies on and develop rehabilitation projects for drinking water supply authorities of Kratie and Stung Treng Provinces.",""],[1,"147","22","Triangle Region Rehabilitation and Development Projects","Implement the rehabilitation and development projects in the Triangle Region in Rattanak Kiri and Mondul Kiri provinces under grants from Japanese Government.",""],[1,"147","23","Drinking Water Supply Expansion Project Studies and Development","Conduct studies on and developing drinking water supply expansion project in Siemreap Provincial Municipalities.",""],[1,"147","24","Drinking Water Supply Development Studies","Conduct studies on and developing drinking water supply in Prasat Sambo in Kampong Thom Province.",""],[1,"147","25","Drinking Water Supply Rehabilitation and Expansion Project","Implement the rehabilitation and expansion project for drinking water supply in Kampot Provincial Municipalities.",""],[1,"148","1","Drinking Water Supply System Rehabilitation and Expansion Project","Develop and implementing drinking water supply system rehabilitation and expansion project in 6 Municipalities.",""],[1,"148","2","Drinking Water Production Capacity Expansion Project","Develop and implement drinking water production capacity expansion project in provincial municipalities of Battambang and Kampong Cham.",""]],"66":[[1,"48","14","Water Resources and Irrigation System Management","This rectangle of the Rectangular Strategy addresses issues dealing with: (ii) water resources and irrigation system management",""],[1,"52","18","Irrigation Project Rehabilitation, Maintenance and Construction Programme","Rehabilitation, maintenance and construction of 141 irrigation projects which provide irrigated water to 267,224 hectares of agricultural land",""],[1,"53","10","River Water Level Staff Gate Installation","Set up 39 water level staff gates along the river at check points.",""],[1,"53","11","River Water Level Automatic Recorder Installation","Set up 13 water level automatic recorders at the check points along the rivers.",""],[1,"53","12","River Discharge Measurement Stations","Set up 4 discharge measurements at Siem Reap River in Siem Reap province, Sangke River, Battambang province, at Porsat River, Porsat province, and at Boribo river, Kampong Chhnang Province.",""],[1,"53","13","Meteorological Information Capacity Strengthening","To strengthen the capacity to provide up-to-date weather information, the Meteorology Department of the MRWAW has:","Meteorology Department of the MRWAW"],[1,"53","21","Preparation of Water Resources Management Law Sub-Decrees","sub-decrees to implement the Law have not yet been prepared. It is important to carry out this task",""],[1,"54","1","Water Law Implementation Mechanisms","to define mechanisms that will be used to implement the Law effectively especially, river basin management, water license, FWUC, and water quality protection.",""],[1,"54","3","Water Infrastructure Data and Information Development","There is a need to develop basic data and information on infrastructure which relate to water management and improvement to reduce the impact of floods and droughts.",""],[1,"54","3","Irrigation and Drainage Infrastructure Management Strengthening","There is a need to strengthen irrigation, drainage, and infrastructure management to:",""],[1,"54","4","Irrigation Infrastructure Rehabilitation and Construction Prioritization","Select priority locations for rehabilitation and construction within the irrigation infrastructure that have high potential for generating incomes in rural communities.",""],[1,"54","5","Commune Irrigation Infrastructure Management","Engage Commune Councils in managing commune irrigation infrastructure.",""],[1,"54","6","Integrated Water Resources Management for Agricultural Production","Take action to encourage water resources management to maximize its impact on increasing agricultural production in different ways.",""],[1,"54","7","Farmer Participation in Irrigation Utilities and Maintenance","Increase participation of farmers and farming communities in matters dealing with irrigation utilities and maintenance.",""]],"67":[[1,"148","3","Environmental Protection and Sanitation Strengthening","In the program area, Strengthen environmental protection and sanitation to preserve the ecosystem of unpolluted water and clean environment, in particular to the poor, the MIME will:","MIME"],[1,"148","4","Safe Water and Sanitation Awareness Campaign","Enhance the awareness of the need and benefits of safe water and sanitation by disseminating information to communities using all types of media.",""],[1,"148","5","Environmental Management Integration Plan for Sanitation","Coordinate the preparation of the plan for integrating environmental management into sanitation in 5 municipalities.",""],[1,"148","6","Environmental Management Integration in Sanitation Coordination","Coordinate the implementation of the plan for integrating environmental management into sanitation in 5 municipalities.",""],[1,"148","7","Institutional Framework Study Project for Environmental Management and Sanitation","Implement the study project on institutional framework relating to environmental management and sanitation.",""],[1,"148","8","Study Project on Financing Strategies for Environmental Sanitation and Safe Water","Implement the study project on financing strategies in environmental and sanitation issues and safe water.",""]],"68":[[1,"143","2","Irrigation Infrastructure Rehabilitation and Expansion","The Royal Government of the Fourth Legislature will continue to accord priority to the rehabilitation, construction, maintenance and efficient management of irrigation infrastructure, water reservoirs, canals, pipes, drainages, flood and sea protection levies, and water pumping stations to increase irrigated areas and boost agricultural production.",""],[1,"143","12","Irrigation System Rehabilitation and Construction","Rehabilitate and construct the existing irrigation system to meet the urgent needs of water for agriculture.",""],[1,"143","14","Reservoir, Lake, Pond, Intake Canal, and Drainage System Rehabilitation and Construction","Prioritize rehabilitation and construction of reservoirs, lakes, ponds, intake canals and drainage system to ensure the water supply for cultivation zone, aquaculture, daily use and animals.",""],[1,"143","15","Irrigation and Drainage System Rehabilitation and Construction","Prioritize the rehabilitation and construction of irrigation system and drainage system in the poorest areas.",""],[1,"144","9","Irrigated Agriculture Income Generation and Water Sector Investment","Generate income through irrigated agriculture and continual investments in water sector for cultivation.",""],[1,"146","8","Irrigation and Flood Control Infrastructure Rehabilitation and Management","Strengthen the process to prioritize the rehabilitation, construction, maintenance, and management of irrigation infrastructure, reservoir, calmatage structure, irrigation structures, drainage calmatage, calmatage canal, flood control, polder and pumping station to increase cultivated area and agricultural productivity.",""]],"69":[[1,"143","13","Broadcast Water Management Innovation Technology in Rain-Fed Agricultural Areas","Promote broadcasting of water management innovation technology in agricultural areas which depend on rain.",""],[1,"144","2","River Basin Development Study and Design","Promote study and design river basin development in short, medium and long term with the consideration of changing of water discharge, water current, and aquifers to ensure the use of water resources at present and in the future.",""],[1,"144","10","Flood Control and Water Drainage Development","Promote and encourage the study and construction of flood controls and water drainage with the aim of minimizing natural disasters caused by water.",""],[1,"144","11","Flood Mitigation and Community Awareness Measures","Undertake all actions to mitigate flood in all areas which provide high economic potential through providing education to communities, information to public and media.",""],[1,"144","12","Emergency Response for Water-Related Calamities","Urgently respond to the needs of people in areas affected by drought, flood and other calamities caused by water.",""],[1,"144","13","Flood Reduction Participation and Support Measures","Continue encouraging people and all institutions to participate in flood reduction actions such as: providing safety hills, materials, heavy equipment, machineries, education, and presenting new technology which is suitable for the real situation.",""],[1,"144","15","Emergency Water Pump Support for Rice Production","Be prepared to intervene water pump to rescue dry season rice and rainy season rice for people in all provinces in case of shortage of water, especially areas near water resources, not covered by irrigation system.",""],[1,"145","6","River Basin and Natural Lakes Conservation","Strengthen river basin conservation and natural lakes which could store water to help reduce flood and maintain ecology system.",""],[1,"145","9","Meteorological and Hydrological System Strengthening and Expansion","Strengthen and expand meteorological and hydrological system including data collecting and broadcasting.",""],[1,"145","10","Emergency Population Focus and Alert System","Focus and alert populations in effected areas during emergencies related to drought, flood and storm for short, medium and long term.",""],[1,"145","11","Meteorological and Hydrological Station and Rain Gate Installation","Improve and install meteorological and hydrological stations and rain gates, water staff gates at important locations and rivers including data collection and broadcast.",""],[1,"145","12","Hydrological Observation System Installation","Install hydrological observation system to provide accurate water level and water discharge data for flood forecasting, and hydrological data use for preparing project proposals on water resources, and water resources management.",""],[1,"145","13","Meteorological Observation System Installation","Install meteorological observation system to receive accurate weather data for weather forecasting, and weather data required for preparing project proposals and other purposes.",""],[1,"145","14","Weather Forecast Information and Public Education Programme","Provide public with weather forecast information, advice and educate to enhance understanding on how to prevent and minimize the impact of events caused by nature and climate change: storm, lightening storm, tsunami, and flood etc.",""],[1,"145","15","Irrigation and Water Resources Inventory and Mapping","Prepare inventory and geographical map of irrigation system, flood control, polders, river basins, inundated land and water resources management.",""],[1,"146","1","Water Resource Management Awareness and Training Programme","development and advise them to actively participate in preparing management planning, maintenance, conserving, and using water effectively in a sustainable manner to keep good eco-system, using all means such as organizing training programs, workshops, and adding these issues in the curriculum of programs offered by education institutions, and widely disseminate this information through bulletins, magazine, radio, TV and other medias.",""],[1,"146","13","Flood Mitigation and Flood Prevention Capacity Building","Mitigate flood effects and build capacity to prevent floods from rain and sea water.",""]],"70":[[1,"143","3","Clean Water Access and Water Use Rationalization Measures","The Royal Government will pay more attention to the rights of access of people to clean water supply to ensure food safety and better livelihoods in accordance with the Cambodia Millennium Development Goals (CMDGs) and will also preserve the ecosystem of unpolluted water and clean environment.",""],[1,"145","2","Water Resources Management Law Enforcement and Project Screening","Strengthen and encourage the implementation of Water Resources Management Law and other related provisions to monitor and prevent all rehabilitation and construction projects that might have adverse impact on water resources and eco-system.",""],[1,"145","4","River and Lake Water Level Maintenance","Maintain water discharge and minimum water level in river, and lake to ensure navigation and ecology system.",""],[1,"145","5","Regulation of Landfills, Excavations, and Water Invasion in Sensitive Areas","Prohibit and take urgent action on matters dealing with landfills, excavations or water invasion in rivers, lakes, ponds, and canals or regular inundated areas and the coastal areas without any permission which impact water resources, eco-system and environment.",""],[1,"146","9","Clean Water Rights and Water Resources Study","Pay attention to affirm the rights of citizen to get clean water to ensure food security in people's daily life to align with millennium development goals, and to ensure the ecology system and unpolluted water in the Mekong River Basin and to continue to study the use of water resources in rivers, lakes, ponds, canals and Tonle Sap River.",""]],"71":[[1,"183","1","Urban and Agglomeration Management Improvement","The Royal Government will strengthen urban and agglomeration management to make cities clean without litter, with full sanitary facilities, with fresh air, green park and gymnasium complexes; and organize cultural entertainment publications to support enhancement of quality of physical and moral human health.",""]],"72":[[1,"23","5","Armed Forces Reform","These are: (i) fighting corruption; (ii) legal and judicial reforms; (iii) public administration reforms in all aspects (including decentralisation and de-concentration); and (iv) reform of the armed forces.",""],[1,"30","4","Royal Cambodian Armed Forces Reform and Capacity Enhancement","the reform and further capacity enhancement of the armed forces are proceeding according to plan through demobilisation and establishment of more effective armed forces",""],[1,"30","4","Armed Forces Readiness Funding","RGC will ensure that the armed forces are always in readiness to protect the country's territorial integrity by allotting needed funds without reducing increasing share for development and social sectors.",""],[1,"31","1","Participation in UN Peacekeeping Missions","Although the capability and resources of the RCAF are limited, Cambodia will continue its efforts to participate with the UN in other humanitarian peacekeeping missions in the future.",""],[1,"31","1","Border Protection and National Security Strengthening","the RCAF has strengthened its capability to defend the border of the Kingdom of Cambodia and to ensure security for the entire nation.",""],[1,"31","1","Border Protection Force Capacity Enhancement","The capability of border protection forces has been further strengthened by the presence of armed forces at all strategically important points, strengthening the expertise in preventing infiltration by international terrorism and transnational crime, mobility, communications, information collection, and cooperation with other competent authorities.",""],[1,"118","4","Armed Forces Reform and Capacity Strengthening","The Royal Government has implemented on schedule the reform programs and strengthened the capacity of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces.",""],[1,"118","5","Armed Forces Professionalization and Modernization","Continued strengthening of the armed forces to be highly professional, capable of carrying on their designated missions by equipping them with technology and proper hardware",""],[1,"118","6","Armed Forces Cooperation and Capacity Strengthening","Continued improvement of cooperation among and between all categories of armed forces, and between the armed forces with other relevant ministries and agencies for the cause of peace, political stability, security, and national unity.",""],[1,"118","6","Armed Forces Rescue, Humanitarian, and Agricultural Capacity Building","The Royal Government will continue to promote the tradition of close relationship between the armed forces and people by strengthening the former's capacity in rescue and humanitarian operations, as well as in agricultural production.",""],[1,"118","6","International Cooperation on Peace and Transnational Crime Prevention","At the same time, the Royal Government will continue good cooperation with the international community in protecting and preserving peace and international security, in particular in preventing and cracking down on terrorism, and all kinds of transnational crimes, including drugs and human trafficking.",""]],"73":[[1,"156","4","Tourism Services Improvement and Investment Promotion","During the Fourth Legislature, the Ministry of Tourism (MOT) will focus on improving the quality and scope of tourism services in order to attract new private sector investments in the tourism sector.","Ministry of Tourism (MOT)"],[1,"156","5","Open Sky Policy Implementation","Continue to implementing the Open Sky Policy and promoting Cambodia - Kingdom of Wonder.",""],[1,"156","6","Tourism Marketing Research Council Sub-Decree","Formulate a Sub-decree to establish a Marketing Research Council for Tourism Promotion.",""],[1,"156","7","Domestic Tourist Travel Facilitation","Facilitate travel and transportation, and reduce unnecessary barriers that restrict tourist travel within the country.",""],[1,"156","8","Tour Package Cost Reduction and Creative Package Development","Work to reduce tour package costs and promote the development of creative tour packages.",""],[1,"156","9","Tourism Product and Destination Development Programme","Develop and upgrade tourism products, tourism events, and attractive destinations.",""],[1,"156","10","Domestic Tourism Promotion","Promote domestic tourism.",""],[1,"156","11","Clean City, Clean Resort, and Good Service Awareness Campaign","Promote the awareness campaign on Clean City, Clean Resort, and Good Service.",""],[1,"156","13","Tourism Sector Coordination for New Initiative Planning","Strengthen coordination with line ministries, relevant agencies, Tourism Associations and private sector in the planning of new initiatives to further develop the tourism sector.","line ministries | relevant agencies"],[1,"156","15","Tourism Sector Development Plan Preparation","Completing work on preparing the following plans for the development of the tourism sector:",""],[1,"156","23","Tourism Marketing and Promotion Campaign","Marketing study and to further promote tourism campaign, especially \"Cambodia - Kingdom of Wonder\", to raise awareness of Cambodia's potential tour programs at the regional and international arenas, to attract more visitor arrivals by planning and holding several tourism events, and developing tourist facilities of high quality.",""]],"74":[[1,"20","5","Tourism Infrastructure and Destination Development","To further improve tourism infrastructure and the development of more tourism destinations and attractive tour packages.",""],[1,"60","4","Open Sky Policy for Air Access to Tourist Destinations","RGC's \"Open Sky Policy\" to promote easy access to tourist destinations by air travel has been vigorously implemented.",""],[1,"60","5","Simplified Tourist Visa and Visa Exemption Arrangements","Tourist Visa requirements have been simplified for tourists from within the region.",""],[1,"60","6","Child Safe Tourism Monitoring and Enforcement","Anti Child sex tourism activities are being actively monitored and actions taken against the perpetrators by the Child Safe Tourism Commission of the MOT in cooperation with line-ministries, relevant agencies, national and international organizations.","Child Safe Tourism Commission of the MOT"],[1,"60","6","Child Safe Tourism Awareness Campaign","Tourism promotions materials are now produced, such as video clips, radio spots, stickers, leaflets, billboards, and through newspapers and magazines to raise awareness of and to ensure Child Safe Tourism.",""],[1,"61","1","Tourism Investment Expansion and Eco-Tourism Promotion","There is a need to broaden investments in areas surrounding the historical-cultural site (such as Chong Khneas, Kampong Phluk), around beaches and islands, as well as aggressively promoting eco-tourism around Tonlesap River.",""],[1,"61","3","Tourism Backward Linkages Development","It is important to establish strong backward linkages with local supplier and between tourism and agriculture sectors.",""],[1,"61","4","Tourism Environmental Monitoring and Mitigation Measures","There is need to monitor and take prompt action to mitigate the risks and adverse effects from tourism on environment especially in Siem Reap (e.g., excessive use of underground water resources which may lead to soil degradation and damage to ancient monuments) and Sihanoukville.",""],[1,"61","5","Cultural Heritage Protection and Promotion","The preservation and promotion of the rich Khmer cultural heritage and traditions are a high priority of the Royal Government.",""],[1,"61","5","Cultural Heritage Site Protection and Fine Arts Promotion","The Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts has been actively involved in ensuring that the cultural heritage sites are protected and in promoting activities covering various aspects of fine arts.","Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts"]],"75":[[1,"153","10","International Market Access Expansion through Trade Obligation Implementation","The Royal Government of the Fourth Legislature will make further efforts to expand international market access through concerted implementation of its obligations under the",""],[1,"154","1","Trade Facilitation Promotion","promote trade facilitation",""],[1,"155","20","Trade Sector Program Implementation Strengthening","Strengthen the implementation of the Trade Sector Program that is based on a sector-wide approach, focusing on trade facilitation and the private sector development.",""],[1,"155","21","Export Promotion for Agriculture Products and Garments","Continue to promote exports of agriculture products, garments and other products as part of its poverty reduction strategy.",""],[1,"155","23","National and International Trade Fair Promotion","Organize more national and international trade fairs.",""],[1,"155","24","Market Surveillance Strengthening","Strengthen the effectiveness of market surveillance in order to protect the health and well being of consumers.",""],[1,"155","25","Law Enforcement Strengthening","Strengthen law enforcement.",""]],"76":[[1,"59","3","Intellectual Property Rights Enforcement and Market Surveillance","The MOC has been enforcing the Laws on Intellectual Property Rights to prevent production and distribution of fake products.","MOC"],[1,"59","3","Border Product Safety Inspections","Camcontrol officers regularly do market surveillance and carryout inspections at border check points to prevent the importation and selling of unsafe products which could have negative affect to the health and well being of the consumers.","Camcontrol"]],"77":[[1,"41","9","Draft Declaration on Land Policy","The draft Declaration on Land Policy addresses issues relating to Land Administration (clarify and record ownership and other rights), Land Management (to ensure that land and natural resources are effectively managed) and Land Distribution (to allocate state land for public and private purposes in a transparent, decentralized and fair manner).",""],[1,"41","12","State Private Property Utilization and Land Concession Policy","State Private Property, is often idle that could be put to various uses or transferred, including grant of land concessions (for large plantation, commercial farming, mining and social concessions).",""],[1,"41","14","Land Titling and Land Reform Programme","The Royal Government recognizes that land reform is vital to enhance social stability, the development of an efficient land market, environmental sustainability, and for increasing agricultural productivity through the issuance of land titles to the citizens; in particular, to farmers who are cultivating land that they occupy.",""],[1,"41","14","Transparent and Equitable Land Tenure Security Reform","Issuing land titles to citizens is vital for improving the management of land use, especially the management of state- owned lands, to ensure security of land tenure in a transparent and equitable manner, and",""],[1,"42","2","Land Tenure Security and Land Registration Reform","The priority is on strengthening security of land tenure (both state land and private land) through land registration for systematic and sporadic land titling procedures in order to provide land titles to people as well as institutions entitled to tenure rights.",""],[1,"42","4","Indigenous Communal Land Titling and Registration","This next step is the setting up of the pole and full registration at the beginning of 2010, as well as continuing the implementation of Sub- decree 83 ANK.BK concerning the procedures of indigenous land titling; especially, those in Mondulkiri and Rattanakiri provinces.",""],[1,"43","2","Land Management Policy and Regulatory Framework Development","To further strengthen land management, the process of establishing policy framework and relevant regulatory frameworks such as land management policy, national housing policy, guidelines on legal procedures for resettlement, and law on land management, urbanization and construction are now being prepared through an inter- ministerial working group.",""],[1,"43","2","Urban and Provincial Land Use Mapping Support","To prepare Land Use Maps for urban areas, the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction is providing technical support to District/Khan, provincial and municipal authorities in order to collect and verify data on Urban and Provincial Land Use Planning from ten provinces/Municipality.","Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction"],[1,"43","2","Phnom Penh Strategic Development Plan and Provincial Planning","a Strategic Development Plan for Phnom Penh city has been finalized and work is now underway in three other provinces (Sihanouk, Kep and Kompong Cham province).",""],[1,"43","3","Social Land Concessions Program","RGC has been implementing a policy to distribute land to landless citizens through its social land concessions program.",""],[1,"43","11","Single Window Cadastral Service Delivery Reform","There is a need to promote the culture of land registration and to further strengthen the services delivery by the Cadastral System through a Single Window process that is transparent and accountable and delivers its services in a timely manner to build citizens confidence in the system.",""],[1,"43","11","Countrywide Systematic Land Registration Acceleration","Accelerate the countrywide land systematic land registration system, in particular in the economically potential areas through establishment of a special operation agency.",""],[1,"43","12","Transparent and Equitable Land Management Reform","Land management, land use and land distribution processes need to be made more transparent, equitable and effective.",""],[1,"43","12","State Land Management Strengthening","The management of state land needs to be strengthened using various tools, including land management planning for all levels to direct land development and monitoring, preventing Concentration of unused land in few hands, preventing clearance of state-owned lands, forestlands, and lands in",""],[1,"44","1","Social Land Concessions for Land Allocation and Relocation","Properly identifying lands to allocate for poor landless families, veterans, and for relocation of families displaced due to economic development projects of private companies, or through actions to recover state lands that were occupied illegally -- through RGC's social land concessions program;",""],[1,"44","1","Stricter Enforcement of Economic Land Concession Compliance","as well as taking more stringent enforcement measures against the concessionaires who do not properly comply with the terms and conditions of the agreements of economic land concessions.",""],[1,"44","2","Review and Enforcement of Large Economic Concessions","Undertake a review of already granted large economic concessions by strengthening the control mechanism for contract implementation; verify the size of authorized lands in order to take back land that are not being used in accordance with contracts or exceed the limits under the 2001 land law and to remove from the concessions lands of 'protected areas' and lands already earlier held by people, which had been inadvertently included in concessions, and restore such areas back to 'protected areas' or to the people who were using them, as the case may be.",""],[1,"44","3","Participatory and Transparent Social and Environmental Impact Assessment for Land Concessions","Strengthen the social and environmental impact assessment in a participatory and transparent manner in the areas considered to be land concessions.",""],[1,"44","4","State Land and Indigenous Community Land Registration","Pursue and ensure registration of state land according to procedures stipulated in the Sub-decree on the Management of State Land and the Registration of Indigenous-People Community lands where these people are living in community.",""],[1,"44","5","Enforcement of the Guiding Circular on Illegal Occupancy of State Land","Strictly implement the Guiding Circular on Illegal Occupancy of State Land in order to identify speculators and to take back illegally-occupied lands for social development and environment protection purposes.",""],[1,"44","6","Idle Land Taxation and Land Governance Reform","Pursue the taxation of idle lands; consider terminating concessions that are not complying with existing laws and regulations; set up a clear and well-functioning system of land information and land price valuation; and the preparation of strategic development plan for provinces and municipalities in particular for the economically potential areas in order to manage their development and to prevent concentration of lands for speculation.",""],[1,"44","7","Implementation of Social Land Concessions Distribution Plan","Pursue implementation of RGC's Guiding Circular on the Plan on Distribution of Social Land Concessions to 416 families in each province to reach the target of 10,000 families by 2010.",""],[1,"44","8","Collective Land Rights and Restitution Pilot Projects","Speed up the process to grant collective land rights and titles to indigenous minorities (estimated to be 17 groups) and to restore to them land wrongfully bought from them by some unscrupulous individuals; 2 pilot projects in Rattanakiri and 1 in Mondolkiri are being started to register lands held by such minorities.",""],[1,"44","9","Land Allocation for the Landless Poor","Provide land to the landless poor where-ever possible.",""],[1,"44","10","Public Awareness Campaign Against Speculative Land Grabbing","Through education and wide publicity, warn poor people from parting with their land, their main source of livelihood, to speculative land grabbers who pay a price seemingly high to the poor who may quickly use up this newly acquired \"wealth\" for consumption and are often left without any source of livelihood.",""],[1,"44","11","Land Conflicts Mobile Team","Speed up land dispute resolution process, in particular, the disputes of multi-parties by establishing Land Conflicts Mobile Team with a status of a special operational agency to clear the backlog in the districts.",""]],"78":[[1,"105","5","Rural Economy Development Strategy Coordination and Monitoring","CARD is also tasked to prepare comprehensive strategies covering all aspects of development of rural economies and to coordinate, monitor and evaluate the implementation of these strategies in a coordinated and time sequenced manner by implementing RGC institutions to achieve a sustainable development of the rural economies.",""],[1,"105","6","Rural Economic Development and Job Creation Strategy","RGC will aggressively pursue a strategy to ensure a broad- based development of rural economies to create new jobs and increase incomes to uplift the economic status of rural communities and to enable them to make a greater contribution to the national economy.",""],[1,"105","6","Pro-Poor Development Cooperation Grant Allocation","RGC will work with development cooperation partners to ensure that there is a greater net transfer of development cooperation grant resources targeted at poverty reduction to the vulnerable and the poor in rural communities, especially remote rural communities.",""],[1,"106","2","Inter-Ministerial Coordination for Development Programme Delivery","In key areas such as agriculture and rural development, and associated infrastructure development, irrigation and water resource management, and trade facilitation, I will be requiring much greater communication, coordination and cooperation between relevant ministries/institutions, especially their leaders and senior officials to ensure that development programmes are more speedily and effectively designed and implemented, and that the supporting resources provided by our development partners can be more speedily and effectively disbursed for implementation.",""],[1,"106","3","Broad-Based Rural Economy Development Strategy","Effective implementation of a strategy to ensure a broad-based development of rural economies to create new jobs and increase incomes to uplift the economic status of rural communities and to enable them to make a greater contribution to the national economy will require coordinated planning and implementation of programs by a number of RGC institutions.","RGC institutions"],[1,"106","3","Rural Agriculture Productivity and Diversification Programme","This broad-based development will be focused on enhancing the productivity and diversity of the agriculture sector, development of agro-industries, rehabilitation and construction of rural roads network to ensure that rural communities have access to market their products in the national and regional markets, and expansion of the education, technical and vocational training, and health services in the rural areas.",""],[1,"106","3","Rural Roads Rehabilitation and Construction Programme","This broad-based development will be focused on enhancing the productivity and diversity of the agriculture sector, development of agro-industries, rehabilitation and construction of rural roads network to ensure that rural communities have access to market their products in the national and regional markets, and expansion of the education, technical and vocational training, and health services in the rural areas.",""],[1,"106","3","Rural Education, TVET, and Health Service Expansion","This broad-based development will be focused on enhancing the productivity and diversity of the agriculture sector, development of agro-industries, rehabilitation and construction of rural roads network to ensure that rural communities have access to market their products in the national and regional markets, and expansion of the education, technical and vocational training, and health services in the rural areas.",""],[1,"106","3","CARD Rural Economy Strategy and Policy Development","As a high priority, the Council for Agriculture and Rural Development (CARD) has been tasked by RGC to develop strategies and policies to develop rural economies, and to coordinate, monitor and evaluate the implementation of planned strategies and policies by RGC implementing institutions.","Council for Agriculture and Rural Development (CARD) | RGC"],[1,"106","3","Inter-Ministerial Coordination Mechanism for Rural Development","Putting in place effective inter-ministerial coordination mechanisms that will ensure that development programs and projects are carried out in a coordinated and strategically sequenced manner by implementing RGC institutions to achieve a sustainable development of rural economies is a high priority of CARD.","CARD | RGC institutions"],[1,"107","4","Pro-Poor Rural Development Cooperation Grant Allocation","Ensuring that there is a greater net transfer of development cooperation grant resources targeted at poverty reduction to the vulnerable and the poor in rural communities, especially remote rural communities.",""],[1,"107","4","Participatory Delivery of Development Cooperation Grants","significantly increasing the proportion of development cooperation grant resources that are allocated and delivered to the vulnerable and the poor through program delivery methodologies that are based on an active participation of the poor in the utilization of these resources to improve their quality of life, incomes, and their contribution to the national economy.",""],[1,"107","4","Inter-Agency Development Resource Coordination","strengthening coordination in the planning, budgeting, and allocation of resources available for development from all sources by the four central agencies, MOP, MEF, CRDB/CDC, and SNEC.","MOP | MEF | CRDB/CDC | SNEC"],[1,"184","1","Targeted Resource Transfer to Vulnerable Rural Households","An important outcome, that is a high priority of RGC, is to achieve a significant increase in a net transfer of development resources to the targeted beneficiary populations, in particular the vulnerable and the poor households in rural communities; and a strengthened capacity of RGC institutions to deliver their programs and services efficiently.",""],[1,"186","1","Coordinated Support for Rural Economic Diversification and Institutional Capacity Strengthening","coordinated support to expand and diversify the economic base, in particular of the rural economies to alleviate poverty in rural areas, to mitigate the adverse effects of the global financial crisis and economic downturn on the vulnerable and the poor and the real economy, to support expansion and efficient delivery of social sectors services to achieve CMDG targets, and to strengthen the capacity of RGC institutions to deliver their programs and services efficiently.",""],[1,"186","2","Domestic Private Sector Financing Measures","RGC will implement measures to encourage financing of private sector economic activities from domestic financial sector to secure the private sector capital investment requirements.",""],[1,"186","5","Targeted Support for Rural Economic Development and Diversification","Resources required to provide targeted support for the development and diversification of rural economies to alleviate poverty in rural and remote areas, and to mitigate the adverse impact of the global financial crisis and economic downturn on the vulnerable and the poor.",""],[1,"186","8","Rural Economy Development and Diversification Support","It includes: resources required to provide targeted support for the development and diversification of rural economies to alleviate poverty in rural and remote areas, and emergency support to mitigate the adverse impact of the global financial crisis and economic downturn on the vulnerable and the poor (4,100.0 billion CR or 1 billion US$);",""],[1,"186","12","Targeted Support for Rural Economic Development and Diversification","Targeted support for the development and diversification of rural economies to alleviate poverty in rural and remote areas, and to mitigate the adverse impact of the global financial crisis and economic downturn on the vulnerable and the poor.",""]],"79":[[1,"184","3","Strengthening of Planning and Resource Allocation Processes","The Royal Government will further strengthen and refine the planning and resource allocation processes and the capacity of RGC institutions will be strengthened to ensure that the data required for development planning and public investment resources allocation purposes is readily available.",""],[1,"184","3","Three-Year Rolling Public Investment Program Preparation","The three-year rolling Public Investment Program (PIP) for 2011-2013 will be prepared based on a methodology that enables the harmonization of PIP, public investment expenditure, and development cooperation financing.",""],[1,"186","8","Public Sector Capital Investment Programme","The Royal Government has set a target of 23,538.1 billion CR (US$ 5,741 billion) for public sector investments to implement RGC's prioritized policies for the Fourth Legislature.",""],[1,"187","1","Public Sector Capital Expenditure Financing for Priority Investment Projects","Within the framework of the Medium-Term Expenditure Framework (MTEF), the Royal Government has allocated 3,245.2 billion CR (US$ 791.5 million) for public sector capital expenditures that will be leveraged to attract financing from traditional and non- traditional development cooperation partners and the private sector to implement RGC's priority investment projects during the Fourth Legislature.",""],[1,"188","7","Strengthening Public Investment, Resource Mobilization, and Budget Framework Linkages","Royal Government is now in the process of strengthening linkages between the processes that: (i) identify high priority public investment requirements, which include the five-year National Strategic Development Plans (NSDP) and the three-year rolling Public Investment Program (PIP); (ii) the mobilization of external resources from traditional and non-traditional development partners; and (iii) the preparation of the Budget Strategic Framework.",""],[1,"189","1","Public Investment Resource Envelope Preparation","the preparation of a public investment resource envelope that will serve as an operational and financing tool to implement policy priorities identified in the NSDP.",""],[1,"189","1","Three-Year Rolling Public Investment Programme Strengthening","The process of preparing the three-year rolling PIP will be strengthened to ensure that: (i) additional recurrent expenditure requirements of proposed projects that have implications for the Annual Budget are an integral part of information collected in the formulation of the PIP; and (ii) projects included in PIP are prioritized - RGC institutions will assign a sequenced priority ranking to projects for which they are seeking resources to implement over the planning period of PIP, taking into account the overall macroeconomic environment and an awareness of the scope to mobilize external resources based on recent trends.",""],[1,"189","2","Public Investment Program Funding Alignment and Resource Mobilization","RGC will ensure that only those programs and projects that are part of the PIP are included in a consideration for funding during the formulation of the Budget Strategic Framework.",""],[1,"189","3","Methodological Refinements for Policy-Investment Linkage","These methodological refinements will on the one hand ensure a closer linkage between Royal Government's policy priorities, the actions, programs and projects that line ministries and agencies plan to carry out to implement the prioritized policies, and the public investment resources required to implement the planned activities.",""],[1,"189","3","Medium-Term Public Investment Financing Linkage","On the other hand, this will forge a closer linkage between the public investment requirements identified through the planning process and the Royal Government's public investment budget and development cooperation resources that will provide a medium term financing outlook for the Royal Government in the implementation of the NSDP.",""],[1,"189","3","National Budget Comprehensiveness and Allocation Efficiency Reform","These, linked with and aimed at improved comprehensiveness of the national budget, which covers recurrent and capital budget, will also ensure enhanced allocation efficiency and effectiveness.",""]],"80":[[1,"131","8","National Housing Policy and Land Management Reform","Creating and enhancing the performance of National housing policy, Land management and Resettlement; legal framework and legal procedure suitable for managing land development in the urban and rural areas and land development for using in agricultural production and construction; and the proper limitation of building height in urban area.",""],[1,"132","1","Construction Regulations and Technical Standards Development","Speed up the regulations development, technical norms for advancing construction: in particular, the construction of high buildings using modern technology is increasing gradually.",""],[1,"132","1","Capacity Support for Skilled Officers in Construction Oversight","Provide enough facilities for the .skilful officers to be able to observe for the progress of technology and management effectively",""],[1,"133","1","Integrated Land Management Planning System","Make planning system for land management including master plan or national, divisional and provincial plan and sub-national land use plan (commune and town/district) with the involvement of all skilful and relevant people by accomplishing a consensus in the compliance with the nature of land and requirement for economic and social development",""],[1,"133","1","Urban Development Planning and Construction Control Measures","Meanwhile, it is necessary to encourage the process of making development plans for urban and inhabited areas, identification of used land area, limited high building areas, and disallowable area for construction, inspection of construction site with the inclusion, of legal procedure of non-developed land management.",""]],"81":[[1,"166","2","Gender Policy Implementation","The four sides or sub-components of this component of the Rectangular Strategy Phase II deal with: (iii) implementation of gender policy;",""],[1,"170","26","Gender Policy Development in Education, Youth and Sports","Complete building gender policies in education sector, youth and sport.",""],[1,"170","27","Gender Mainstreaming Strategic Plan Implementation","Continue to implement Gender Mainstreaming Strategic Plan 2006-2010.",""],[1,"170","29","Management and Staff Capacity Development through Increased Female Representation","Strengthening the management and staff capacity development through increasing number of female staff in management team.",""],[1,"176","28","Implementation of the Neary Rattanak II Strategic Plan","The Royal Government has succeeded in implementing the Strategic Plan \"Neary Rattanak II\".",""],[1,"177","2","Female Students Education Access Support Programme","The Royal Government of the Fourth Legislature will continue to implement its policy aiming at increasing education opportunity for female students through increased scholarships, additional training programs, providing accommodation and safe transportation, and increasing the number of female teachers.",""],[1,"177","2","Women's Leadership and Skills Development Initiative","The Royal Government continues to increase women's role and capacity in decision-making at all levels of governance and pays attention to skills training for women at all levels.",""],[1,"177","2","Women's Employment and Rights Protection Measures","The Royal Government will strive to increase the ratio of women at all government levels, by providing employment opportunities for women, using advocacy at the village and commune levels throughout the country, and by protecting the rights of working women.",""],[1,"177","4","Neary Rattanak III Strategic Plan","the Ministry of Women's Affairs in collaboration with the Cambodian National Council for Women has prepared a five year strategic plan, Neary Rattanak III (2009-2013), which focuses on five strategic areas, a gender mainstreaming program in national and sectoral policies, reform programmes and implementation of international conventions; as well as a cross-cutting area that deals with strategic management, capacity development and aid effectiveness.","Ministry of Women's Affairs | Cambodian National Council for Women"],[1,"178","1","Women’s Capacity and Skills Development Programs","programs on capacity and skills development and advocate for scholarships for women; advocate for and monitor mechanisms for providing decent jobs to women including disabled and indigenous women; and establish a consultation and information centre for women.",""],[1,"178","1","Scholarships for Women","advocate for scholarships for women;",""],[1,"178","1","Mechanisms for Decent Jobs for Women","advocate for and monitor mechanisms for providing decent jobs to women including disabled and indigenous women;",""],[1,"178","1","Women’s Consultation and Information Centre","establish a consultation and information centre for women.",""],[1,"179","10","Women’s Political Participation and Leadership Promotion","Increase the number of active women representatives in decision making in government institutions and at all sub national levels through lobbying of political parties and relevant institutions to increase the proportion of women standing for elections and putting their candidacy higher up in the list for senate, parliamentary and sub national councils; encourage political dialogue and develop strategies and advocacy for affirmative action and set quotas for women at all levels; raising public awareness of the importance of women's participation at the senior level as lower house representative, provincial, municipal, district and Khan board of governors and commune councillor; and capacity development for elected and appointed women by the public at national and sub national levels including female candidates standing for commune council elections 2012 and the next national elections.",""],[1,"179","11","Women's Participation in Public Sector Decision-Making","The promotion of women's participation in decision making in the public sector at all levels by pushing for the implementation of policies and procedures for promotion and recruitment of government officials in response to gender equality; cooperating",""],[1,"180","1","Gender-Responsive Curriculum Development and Female Leadership Capacity Building","with the Royal School of Administration in setting up gender responsive curriculum and increasing the number of female students - Cooperating with the women civil servant association and relevant players in improving the effectiveness of performance and rights protection, and the well being of women civil servants; capacity building and skills at Leadership and Management as well as other related skills for women leaders.",""],[1,"180","3","Gender Mainstreaming in National Policies and Statistical System","Gender mainstreaming in national policies and the statistical system by focusing mainly on gender mainstreaming in the process of developing, monitoring and evaluation of national policies and sectoral polices; strengthening and scaling up the mechanisms of gender mainstreaming at the national and sub national levels; capacity development on gender mainstreaming for relevant government institutions at the national and sub national levels; advocating and lobbying for integrating gender issues in the process of sectoral planning, budgeting and reporting; improving preparation and implementation of sector gender mainstreaming plans at the national and sub national level; and gender mainstreaming in the national statistical system.",""],[1,"180","4","Gender Mainstreaming Action Groups and Action Plans in Line Ministries","Gender mainstreaming in sectors by focusing specially on gender mainstreaming through the gender mainstreaming action groups and their respective gender mainstreaming action plans in the line ministries.",""],[1,"180","5","Gender Mainstreaming in Macro-Economic and Sector Policies","Economic and Finance sector, by gender mainstreaming in macro-economic policies and other policies and services for poverty reduction, agricultural and rural development, land and natural resource management and the protection of rights and welfare of female workers as well as women's economic welfare in the informal sector.",""],[1,"180","6","Gender Mainstreaming in Education Policy and Planning","Education sector, by mainstreaming gender in the national policy and plan on the Education for All to improve the effectiveness of the implementation of the policy and in response to gender equality considerations such as: increasing the number and capacity of female teachers; increasing the survival rate of girls in school especially from grade 9 onwards; and integrating gender equality issues in analysis into discussion of education policies including education for disabled children and indigenous and ethnic minority girls and women.",""],[1,"180","7","Gender Equality and Women's Rights Legal Reform","by advocating for the development and adoption of any necessary legislation, regulations or law amendments to promote gender equality and protect women's rights;",""],[1,"180","7","Legal Protection Access Research and Dialogue Initiative","carry out research and promote dialogue to also promote improved access to legal protection including disabled women and indigenous and ethnic minority women.",""],[1,"181","2","Gender Mainstreaming in Government Reform Programmes","Gender mainstreaming in government reform programs by analysing, advocating for, and monitoring the development and implementation of gender responsive national reform programmes, including legal and judicial reform, democratic development (D&D reform); public administration reform, and public financial management reform.",""],[1,"181","3","CEDAW and Women's Rights Convention Implementation Support","The implementation of the CEDAW and other relevant conventions and regional commitments relating to gender equality and women's rights by supporting dissemination and understanding of the conventions, and monitoring and reporting on their implementation; and for CEDAW, disseminating the concluding comments to the official report submitted by the State party.",""]],"82":[[1,"23","5","Public Administration Reform and Decentralisation","These are: (i) fighting corruption; (ii) legal and judicial reforms; (iii) public administration reforms in all aspects (including decentralisation and de-concentration); and (iv) reform of the armed forces.",""],[1,"27","1","National Program for Administrative Reform","Since 2000, the Council for Administrative Reform (CAR) has implemented a series of National Program for Administrative Reform to systematically and gradually transform the Administration and the Civil Service into effective providers of public services and trusted development partners.","Council for Administrative Reform (CAR)"],[1,"27","2","Third Governance Action Plan","The CAR together with ministries and institutions is preparing a third Governance Action Plan that will focus on how to improve services delivery and better coordinate reform efforts.","CAR | ministries and institutions"],[1,"27","4","National Programme for Administrative Reform","Through a rigorous implementation of its \"National Programme for Administrative Reform (NPAR)\", the Royal Government has been working hard to transform the Public Administration.",""],[1,"27","4","Civil Service Strengthening","it has become even more urgent to further strengthen the Civil Service.",""],[1,"27","8","Government-wide Performance and Accountability Instruments","Innovative instruments (Special Operating Agencies, Priority Mission Groups, Merit- Based Performance Incentives) are being deployed government-wide to enhance performance and accountability.",""],[1,"27","9","Performance Management and Accountability System","A Performance Management and Accountability System has been developed to support the implementation of P&A instruments.",""],[1,"28","5","Basic Salary Increase Implementation Mechanism","Mechanisms to implement the 20% annual increase in basic salary are in place.",""],[1,"28","6","Performance and Accountability Enhancement Schemes","Innovative schemes to enhance performance and accountability are being deployed (SOAs, PMGs, MBPIs).",""],[1,"28","7","Performance Management and Accountability System","The Performance Management and Accountability System is being implemented to better mobilize human resources and identify priority capacity development needs.",""],[1,"28","8","Public Services Delivery Improvement Policy Implementation","The Policy on Improving Public Services delivery has been approved and is being implemented.",""],[1,"28","9","Public Services Compendium Completion and Dissemination","A Compendium on Public Services is being completed and disseminated to improve access to public services and enhance transparency.",""],[1,"28","13","National Program for Administrative Reform","The Royal Government intends to continue to vigorously pursue the implementation of the National Program for Administrative Reform (NPAR) to transform the Administration and the Civil Service into effective providers of public services and trusted development partners.",""],[1,"28","14","Public Sector Reform Policy Framework Completion","Complete the policy framework (Capacity Development, HRD, HRM, compensation and redeployment) to guide reform activities.",""],[1,"28","15","Public Service Quality and Delivery Improvement","Improve the quality and delivery of public services.",""],[1,"28","16","Civil Service Service-Oriented Culture Reform","Change the attitude and behaviour of civil servants from administrators to service providers.",""],[1,"28","17","Ministerial Focal Point Network for NPAR Implementation","Deploy a network of ministerial focal points to facilitate the implementation of NPAR and the policy framework.",""],[1,"28","18","Human and Institutional Capacity Development for RGC Policy Implementation","Further develop human and institutional capacity to implement RGC policies and to sustain results.",""],[1,"28","19","Performance and Accountability Improvement Using Innovative Instruments","Improve performance and accountability using innovative instruments in a controlled manner and carefully manage associated risks.",""],[1,"28","20","Merit-Based Human Resource Management Reform","Manage human resources based on principles of performance, merit and fairness.",""],[1,"28","21","Civil Service Compensation and Career Development Reform","Motivate civil servants with adequate compensation and promising career perspectives.",""],[1,"28","22","CAR Secretariat and Institutional Capacity Development for Reform Management","Develop the capacity of the CAR Secretariat, ministries and institutions to plan, manage and monitor the reform.",""],[1,"56","3","Civil Service Reform and Salary Improvement","civil service reform and improvements in salary levels",""]],"83":[[1,"114","1","Public Service Delivery Through Information Technology","public service provision through information technology are also offered.",""],[1,"116","8","ICT Implementation Improvement","Improvement of ICT implementation.",""],[1,"116","13","ICT-Based Human Resource Management Development","Ongoing development of human resource management through ICT.",""],[1,"116","14","ICT-Enabled Payroll Management","Ongoing payroll management through effective ICT.",""],[1,"116","18","Cadre Classification System and New Payroll Implementation","Ongoing implementation of classification system by cadre and of the new payroll.",""],[1,"116","19","ICT-Enabled Retirement Policy Implementation","Ongoing implementation of the retirement policy using ICT.",""]],"84":[[1,"23","5","Anti-Corruption Reform","These are: (i) fighting corruption; (ii) legal and judicial reforms; (iii) public administration reforms in all aspects (including decentralisation and de-concentration); and (iv) reform of the armed forces.",""],[1,"24","1","Anti-Corruption Complaint Handling and Enforcement Unit","The Anti-Corruption Unit in the Council of Ministers is responsible for receiving complaints from the public about incidences of corruption and taking disciplinary actions against the perpetrators of corruption.",""],[1,"24","1","Public Anti-Corruption Information Dissemination","It is also responsible for widely disseminating information on RGC's policies on preventing and combating corruption.",""],[1,"24","1","Anti-Corruption Legal and Regulatory Coordination","It also coordinates the preparation of any laws, rules and regulations required to implement RGC's policies on preventing and combating corruption.",""],[1,"24","1","Public Sector Inspection and Irregularity Investigation Program","The Ministry of National Assembly-Senate Relations and Inspection (MONASRI) through its Inspection Program monitors the management practices of public sector institutions and investigates any irregularities.","Ministry of National Assembly-Senate Relations and Inspection (MONASRI)"],[1,"24","1","Law Enforcement Monitoring and Public Complaint Investigation","It also monitors law enforcement in line ministries and public institutions and investigates complaints received from the public.","Ministry of National Assembly-Senate Relations and Inspection (MONASRI)"],[1,"24","2","Transparency in Competitive Bidding Processes","In public management more transparency is being ensured in competitive bidding processes.",""],[1,"24","2","Public Anti-Corruption Information and Education Campaigns","Campaigns have been launched to provide information to and educate the public and disseminate knowledge on all aspects of corruption, including causes, effects and consequences.",""],[1,"24","4","Anti-Corruption Law Drafting and Review Process","The Ministry of Justice that is responsible for the drafting of all laws has been updating the drafts of the Anti-Corruption Law as work on related laws has progressed.","Ministry of Justice"],[1,"24","4","Existing Anti-Corruption Legal and Institutional Framework","In the meantime, the already existing legal framework and institutional mechanisms will continue to be employed to prevent and combat corruption.",""]],"85":[[1,"72","6","100% Condom Use Program","The 100% Condom Use Program for HIV prevention covers 24 provinces with outreach and peer education program reaching more than 90% of entertainment workers in 2008.",""],[1,"72","6","STD Case Management and Integrated STI Clinic Services","STD case management is being provided at 32 specialized STI clinics in 24 provinces for high-risk population and syndrome approach of STD integrated into 222 health centers for the general population.",""],[1,"73","2","Home and Community-Based HIV Care Expansion","Home and community based care for people living with HIV have been scaled up to 657 Health Centers in 20 provinces.",""],[1,"73","2","Opportunistic Infection and Antiretroviral Treatment Service Expansion","Opportunistic Infection Treatment/Anti-Retroviral Treatment (OIT/ART) services have been expanded to 51 sites in 39 Referral Hospitals/Operational Districts in 20 provinces.",""],[1,"73","3","National HIV/AIDS Coordination and Monitoring Mechanism","The National HIV/AIDS Authority (NAA) is responsible for coordinating and monitoring the national, multi-sectoral response to HIV/AIDS.",""],[1,"73","3","Five-Year National HIV/AIDS Strategic Plan","It has been implementing a five-year comprehensive and multi-sectoral national strategic plan (2006-2010) that was developed in collaboration with all government agencies, national and international NGOS, other civil society organizations, the private sector and development partners10.",""],[1,"74","4","Costed Strategic Plan Development and Review for Line Ministries and High-Risk Populations","The development or review of costed strategic plans for several line ministries including MoH (NCHADS and NCMCH), MoWA, MoND, MoEYS and MoLVT and for specific high risk populations such as drug users and injecting drug users (DU/IDU), MSM and entertainment workers (brothel based and non-brothel based).","MoH (NCHADS and NCMCH) | MoWA | MoND | MoEYS | MoLVT"],[1,"74","5","Linked Response Initiative","the integration of HIV, reproductive health, TB and ANC through the \"Linked Response\" initiative was accelerated",""],[1,"74","19","National Multi-Sectoral HIV Response Coordination and Monitoring","NAA's mandate is to lead, coordinate and monitor the national, multi-sectoral response to HIV.",""],[1,"74","20","Single HIV/AIDS Action Framework","One single agreed HIV/AIDS Action Framework that provides the basis for coordinating the work of all partners;",""],[1,"74","20","National AIDS Coordinating Authority","One national AIDS coordinating authority, with a broad based multi-sectoral mandate;",""],[1,"74","20","Comprehensive HIV/AIDS Monitoring and Evaluation System","One single comprehensive multi-sectoral HIV/AIDS M&E System.",""],[1,"75","7","Standard Operating Procedure for HIV Prevention among Entertainment Establishment Staff","To address this issue a new Standard Operating Procedure (SOP) was developed targeting HIV prevention specifically at this high risk group.",""],[1,"75","10","PMTCT Linked Response Strengthening","PMTCT has been strengthened especially through the Linked Response",""],[1,"175","22","National HIV/AIDS Prevention, Care and Support Programme","The National HIV/AIDS Authority (NAA) will continue to implement programs and projects to further reduce the number of new HIV infections by taking to scale targeted prevention interventions; increase coverage and quality of care, treatment and support for people living with and affected by AIDS; and alleviate the socioeconomic and",""],[1,"176","2","Prevention Intervention Expansion for High-Risk Groups","Increase coverage of effective prevention interventions and develop additional interventions especially for high risk groups.",""],[1,"176","3","Comprehensive Care and Support Coverage Expansion","Maintain treatment coverage and increase coverage of effective interventions for comprehensive care and support and develop additional interventions.",""],[1,"176","5","Multi-sectoral HIV and AIDS Coordination and Leadership Strengthening","Strengthen multi-sectoral coordination and leadership by government and non- government sectors for implementation of the national response to HIV and AIDS, especially at sub-national levels.",""],[1,"176","6","Supportive Legal and Public Policy Environment for HIV and AIDS Response","Strengthen a supportive legal and public policy environment for the national response to HIV and AIDS.",""],[1,"176","7","Monitoring, Evaluation, and Research for Policy Information","Increase the availability and use of information for policy makers and programme planners through monitoring, evaluation and research.",""],[1,"176","8","HIV and AIDS Resource Mobilization and Allocation Improvement","Improve mobilization and allocation of resources for the national response to HIV and AIDS.",""]],"86":[[1,"59","4","Better Factories Program","the MOC has been implementing the \"Better Factories\" program to ensure that better working conditions in the sector meet international standards, as well as providing training to workers and unions on Labor Law and fashion design.","MOC"],[1,"63","2","Labour Law Enforcement and Workplace Inspection Programme","the Ministry has continued its focus on strengthening the enforcement of the Labour Laws and regulations, disseminating information about these laws, conducting inspections of working conditions, hygiene and occupational safety, child labour and foreign employees at business establishments across the country","Ministry"],[1,"63","2","Labour Dispute Resolution and Labour Association Promotion","It has facilitated resolution of labour disputes and promoted the formation of labour associations in accordance with the provisions of the Labour Law",""],[1,"63","2","Trade Union and Labour Court Legislation Drafting","The Ministry is now working on drafting the Law on Trade Union and the Law on Labour Court","Ministry"],[1,"63","2","Tripartite Labour Law Working Group","A tripartite working group - composed of representatives of workers, employers and relevant development partners - has been established to guide this work",""],[1,"64","3","National Social Security Fund Compliance Enforcement","The rules and regulations governing the National Social Security Fund need to be enforced by the Ministry to ensure that contributions on behalf of workers are paid by employers on time.",""],[1,"64","3","Ministry Enforcement Capacity Strengthening","The Ministry's capacity to enforce the rules and regulations also needs to be strengthened.",""],[1,"157","8","Trade Union Freedom Promotion","The freedom of trade union has been promoted.",""],[1,"157","8","Labour Inspection and Conflict Resolution Mechanism","Work inspection and conflict resolution mechanism has been tightened to monitor labour law enforcement and ensure decent working conditions.",""],[1,"157","9","Labour Standards and Labour Law Enforcement","effective implementation of labour standards, norms, the Labour Law and international conventions;",""],[1,"157","9","Better Factory Project Continuation","continuation of the \"better factory\" project;",""],[1,"157","9","Labour Dispute Resolution Mechanism Strengthening","strengthening existing mechanisms of labour dispute resolution such as Arbitration Council, and, demonstration and strike resolution committees at all levels.",""],[1,"157","10","Volunteer Arbitrator Training for Local Conflict Resolution","The Royal Government will train volunteer arbitrators among local authorities aiming for peaceful conflict resolution.",""],[1,"157","10","Labour Inspection and Labour Law Enforcement Strengthening","efforts will be made to ensure: sustainability of job creation and labour law enforcement through training, improved labour inspection at factories/enterprises to raise awareness about labour conditions including hygiene, health and safety; prevention of child labour; the adherence to the norms for foreign employees; freedom of union as prescribed in the Labour Law; and, progress towards adoption of a Law on Trade Unions and the legal framework on the Labour Court through comprehensive consultation with all related stakeholders.",""],[1,"158","8","Labour Standards Enforcement Strengthening","Strengthening the enforcement of labour standards, norms, provisions of the Labour Law and international conventions.",""],[1,"158","9","Better Factories Program","Continuing the implementation of the \"better factories\" program.",""],[1,"158","10","Occupational Safety and Health Inspection Enforcement","Strengthening the enforcement of the occupational safety and health standards by carrying out regular inspections of business establishments in both formal and informal sectors.",""],[1,"158","11","Occupational Safety and Health Awareness and Requirements Enhancement","Enhancing the awareness of and requirements for occupational safety and health by working with employer and employee organizations, in particular with regards to under 15 year old and under 18 year old children.",""],[1,"158","13","Child Labour Law Enforcement and Inspection Programme","Strengthening enforcement of laws and regulations dealing with child labour by carrying out regular inspections of industrial establishments and other enterprises to eliminate the exploitation of child labour.",""],[1,"158","14","Workplace Worker-Management Conflict Resolution Measures","Implement measures to reduce worker-management conflicts in work places.","Ministry of Commerce"]],"87":[[1,"60","2","Fiscal Stimulus Package","The Royal Government is implementing a fiscal stimulus package to support the growth of the real economy as well as measure to mitigate the adverse impact of these external developments on the vulnerable and the poor.",""],[1,"90","3","Prudent Fiscal and Monetary Policy Framework","The Royal Government will continue to pursue prudent fiscal and monetary policies, with a focus on broadening the fiscal base to generate additional revenues, in order to consolidate macroeconomic and financial stability.",""],[1,"91","1","Macroeconomic Policy Support for Demand","to continue to follow macroeconomic policies to support demand;",""],[1,"91","3","Fiscal Deficit Consolidation and Stimulus Exit Strategy","on the fiscal side, the deficits in the medium-term will be consolidated in order to bring public finances back to a sustainable path.",""],[1,"91","5","Domestic Revenue Mobilization and Public Financial Management Reform","Mobilizing domestic revenues, ensuring effective allocation of budget resources among competing priorities and promoting healthy public financial practices in general.",""],[1,"91","6","Exchange Rate Stabilization through Fiscal and Monetary Policy Coordination","This fiscal policy instrument will continue to be used along with appropriate monetary policy interventions to maintain a stabile exchange rate.",""],[1,"91","7","Inflation Monitoring and Agricultural Price Stabilization Measures","In addition to maintaining a stable exchange rate, the Royal Government will closely monitor factors that may cause inflationary pressures in domestic markets, in particular agriculture products.",""],[1,"91","8","Sound Debt Management Policy","Pursuing sound debt management.",""],[1,"91","8","Prudent Macroeconomic and Fiscal Management Policy","The Royal Government will pursue prudent policies to ensure a sound macroeconomic and fiscal management of the economy.",""],[1,"92","1","Prudent Fiscal Policy and Fiscal Stability Measures","The Royal Government will follow a prudent fiscal policy and will ensure that budget deficit decline as economy recuperates, at the same time putting in place measures to consolidate the recovery.",""],[1,"92","2","Public Expenditure Rationalization and Wage Bill Control","Rationalizing less productive spending and protect budget allocation to priority sectors.",""],[1,"92","3","Revenue Mobilization and Tax Reform Measures","Increasing revenue collection through broadening the tax base and strengthening administrative compliance.",""],[1,"92","4","National Budget Review and Expenditure Reallocation","The Ministry of Economy and Finance will review the current national budget by rationalizing current spending (compulsory versus non-compulsory expenditures) and reallocating them into funds used for direct support of growth or for specific government's allocations for social safety net as well as spending needed to mitigate unexpected impacts resulting from the global financial and economic crisis.","Ministry of Economy and Finance"],[1,"101","8","Economic Stimulus Package to Support Demand","measures to promote demand through the stimulus package",""]],"88":[[1,"32","4","Juvenile Delinquency Prevention and Suppression Action Plan","Through the National Police General Commissariat (NPGC), the MOI has cooperated with the Ministry of Justice in drafting the RGC-MOI circulars, and preparing an action plan to prevent and suppress the activities of \"juvenile delinquency\".","Ministry of Justice"],[1,"32","4","Strategic Plan to Combat Drug Trafficking and Exploitation","The MOI, through this subsidiary body, has also prepared a strategic plan on combating drug trafficking, the exploitation of labor and sex exploitation of women and children and on strengthening management mechanisms for the implementation of this plan at the central as well as in provincial, municipal and district/Khan levels.",""],[1,"32","4","Traffic Offence Fine Collection and Transfer Mechanism","It is implementing the MOI-MEF Inter-ministerial Prakas on the Collection, Distribution and the Transfer of the fines paid by traffic offenders to national budget.","MOI | MEF"],[1,"32","4","National Police Capacity Strengthening","The MOI has strengthened the capacity of the National Police Force including the National Border Police to be more professionally capable of defending the sovereignty and ensuring security and order within the nation.",""]],"89":[[1,"169","1","Youth HIV-AIDS Awareness and Youth Activities Strengthening Program","The focus of this program is on enhancing youth awareness of HIV-AIDS and strengthening youth activities; and strengthening capacity and youth activities.",""],[1,"170","16","Finalization of the National Youth Policy","Finalization of National Youth Policy of Cambodia.",""],[1,"170","18","Youth and Children Councils Expansion Programme","Strengthening and expansion of youth and children council at school/institution over the country.",""],[1,"170","19","Youth Staff Capacity Strengthening","xix. Strengthen youth staff's capacity.",""],[1,"170","21","Physical Education and Sport Policy and Regulatory Framework","Formulate policy/regulation for development of physical education and sport.",""]],"90":[[1,"122","2","Financial Sector Development Strategy Implementation","The Royal Government will further strengthen the financial sector through effective implementation of the \"Financial Sector Development Strategy 2006-2015\"",""]],"91":[[1,"44","12","Landmine and ERW Clearance Programme","The Cambodian Mine Action and Victim Assistance Authority (CMAA) has been implementing a landmine and ERW clearance programme since 1992 and its performance has improved steadily.",""],[1,"130","5","Mine and UXO Clearance Programme","During the fourth legislature, the clearance of mines and UXOs will remain government priority, especially in remote areas, areas with landless farmers and areas with high potential for agricultural and infrastructure development.",""],[1,"130","5","Equitable Distribution of Cleared Land to Landless Farmers","Moreover, the clearance of mines and UXOs should be linked to the principles of equitable distribution of cleared land to landless farmers.",""],[1,"133","6","Landmines and Explosive Remnants of War Clearance Programme","The Cambodian Mine Action and Victim Assistance Authority (CMAA) has been implementing a landmines and Explosive Remnants of War (ERW) clearance program since 1992.","Cambodian Mine Action and Victim Assistance Authority (CMAA)"],[1,"133","6","National Mine Action Strategy","CMAA is formulating a programme-based National Mine Action Strategy to strengthen its alignment with Cambodia's development priorities and to ensure that clearance enables cultivation, infrastructure, and the provision of safe land to landless households, as well as building national capacity.","Cambodian Mine Action and Victim Assistance Authority (CMAA)"],[1,"133","6","Baseline Survey for Remaining Mine Contamination","CMAA has also launched a 'baseline survey' that will result in a much firmer estimate of the remaining contamination.","Cambodian Mine Action and Victim Assistance Authority (CMAA)"],[1,"133","7","Mine Action Financing Support","Sustained financial support will continue to be required to achieve the mine action objectives of the NSDP, and increased support will be needed to reach the APMBC obligation to clear all known mined areas within 10 years.",""]],"92":[[1,"119","6","Prison Management Improvement and Renovation Programme","The MOI will continue to improve the management of prisons in accordance with that of international standards, renovating dilapidated prisons by equipping them with materials and equipments in proportion to the increased number of prisoners, and proceeding to build","MOI"],[1,"120","1","Prison Construction and Rehabilitation Center Development","new prisons in the provinces of Kratier, Kompong Cham, Baatambang, Pursat, Mondulkiry, Stung Treng, Kompong Thom, Prey Veng, and Rattanakkiry, and building four re-education centers similar to the agricultural prison in Pursat Province.","MOI"],[1,"120","1","Prison Rehabilitation and Inmate Welfare Programme","MOI will put emphasis on re- education and rehabilitation of culprits/prisoners by caring for their health and living conditions in accordance with the ministry policy on prison reform and the procedures on the management of industrial and agricultural prisons with attention being paid to educating the inmates on consciousness, merit and equity to become good citizen with skills to embark on a new life in the community.","MOI"],[1,"120","1","Prison Guard Status Legal Reform","The MOI will prepare a draft of Royal Decree on the status of prison guards, and continue to cooperate with the provincial/municipal authorities and NGOS to strengthen law enforcement and respect of human rights in prisons.","MOI"]],"93":[[1,"94","8","Payment and Settlement System Development","Developing a gross domestic payment and settlement system, monetary and inter- bank markets, including short-term government bonds.",""],[1,"94","9","Fiscal Incentives Framework for Payroll and Riel Payments","Implementing a fiscal incentives framework, including government payroll and other Riel expenses, via bank accounts and the payment system.",""],[1,"94","9","Transfer of Inter-Bank Credit Information System to the Private Sector","It will examine options to transfer inter-bank credit information system to the private sector.",""],[1,"94","10","Expansion of Payment and Credit Information Systems","Widening the payment and credit information systems to include licensed microfinance institutions.",""],[1,"94","11","Payment System Risk Collateral Facility","Providing collateral against risks related to the payment system by using short-term government bonds.",""],[1,"96","3","Credit Information Exchange System Development","Developing a credit information exchange system: to improve the credit information sharing system and establish a framework for a credit information system with a larger scope.",""],[1,"96","5","National Payment System Development","Developing a national payment system: by continuing to develop its safety, effectiveness and capability by automating the check clearing system and initiating the development of electronic payments (e-payments) at the national level to support the inter-bank market.",""],[1,"96","6","Information Technology Management System for NBC","The NBC will develop and implement an information technology management system that is needed to carry out its critical functions and to increase staff efficiency and productivity.",""]],"94":[[1,"56","11","Government Administrative Information System and E-Government Implementation","RGC will continue to implement the Government Administrative Information System and E-Government.",""]],"95":[[1,"7","3","Village Development Committees","Set up Village Development Committees",""],[1,"37","7","Civil Society Participation in Planning and Decision-Making","Active efforts continue to involve and associate all sections of the civil society in all appropriate aspects of RGC's planning and decision-making processes for taking Cambodia forward.",""],[1,"48","8","Village Development Committee Legal Framework","Royal Decree on Village Development Committee (VDC) and Sub-Decree on Procedures for the Establishment and Functioning of the VDC, which has been submitted to Council of Ministers for endorsement.",""]],"96":[[1,"18","3","Stakeholder Partnership and Cooperative Financing Coordination Mechanism","Partnership with all stakeholders especially official development partners, private sector and civil society has been strengthened by putting in place a range of effective mechanisms, allowing for mobilizing and coordinating cooperative financing and investments.",""],[1,"38","5","Government-Development Partner Coordination and Joint Monitoring Mechanism","A high level GDCC (Government-Development Partner Coordination Committee) meets thrice yearly to discuss common issues and pursues Joint Monitoring Indicators (JMIs) on the progress of various aspects of NSDP.",""],[1,"38","6","Technical Working Groups for Sectoral Coordination and Monitoring","Technical Working Groups (TWGs) function to better coordinate and monitor progress at the sectoral level.",""],[1,"38","7","EDP Assistance Data Collection Streamlining and ODA Database Maintenance","The procedures and processes of collection of data of EDP assistance have been streamlined and the ODA data base maintained at CRDB/CDC gets continuously updated.",""],[1,"38","9","Accra Agenda for Action Implementation","RGC is committed to implement the \"Accra Agenda for Action\" to increase efficacy of development assistance4.",""],[1,"39","4","Poverty Reduction and Growth Operations","further progress in this direction has commenced through Poverty Reduction and Growth Operations (PRGO) jointly supported by many EDPs.",""],[1,"39","4","Joint Monitoring Indicators for External Development Partners","There needs to be equal emphasis to create JMIs for EDPs to meet in terms of accountability, alignment and harmonisation.",""],[1,"39","4","Enhanced Alignment and Coordination of External Development Resources","The immediate need is for more efforts by EDPs to better align their resources to meet NSDP priorities and to increasingly utilise the opportunities in TWGs to inform RGC about their work and better coordinate among themselves.",""]],"97":[[1,"20","8","Wealth Creation and Livelihood Support","Continue to promote and support wealth creation and improving the people's livelihood according to the correct principles and procedures as stipulated in the Cambodia's Constitution.",""],[1,"47","8","Credit Provision for Rural Households and Small Businesses","The decentralisation and deconcentration of public services delivery, support for participatory decentralised-based programmes, and the provision of credit to households and small businesses are some of the examples of Royal Government's efforts in this sector.",""]],"98":[[1,"31","4","Promotion of Family and Religious Values","the Ministry of Religion and Cult has continued to make important contributions to promote family and religious values.","Ministry of Religion and Cult"],[1,"31","5","Strengthening Free and Fair Elections","RGC will make every endeavor",""]],"99":[[1,"33","3","Regional Economic Integration and Multilateral Cooperation","RGC institutions, in particular the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, have worked hard to strengthen relations with countries in the region by actively participating in the work of the GMS and ACMECS; and through multilateral development cooperation agreements.","Ministry of Foreign Affairs"]],"100":[[1,"40","18","Introduction and Propagation of High-Yielding Livestock Species","Introduction and propagation of high yielding species and expanded veterinary services is priority of MAFF.","MAFF"],[1,"40","18","Expansion of Veterinary Services","Introduction and propagation of high yielding species and expanded veterinary services is priority of MAFF.","MAFF"],[1,"40","18","Agricultural Sanitary and Phytosanitary Law Reform","To promote agricultural production, the MAFF has prepared laws and regulations that include: the Law on Sanitary and Phyto-sanitary, the Law on Production and Animal health, Law on Agricultural Pesticide Management, and Law on Agricultural Land.","MAFF"],[1,"41","2","Agricultural Inputs and Soil Resource Regulation Framework","Develop appropriate legal and regulatory tools and competency in law enforcement to monitor and regulate agricultural inputs and soil resources and soil fertility management.",""]],"101":[[1,"46","15","Environmental and Social Impact Assessment Recommendations for Projects","The MOE in collaboration with other ministries and concerned parties has provided recommendations on environmental-social impact assessment for 15 projects in the agricultural, industrial, energy, tourism and infrastructure sectors.","MOE | other ministries"],[1,"46","15","Environmental Protection Agreements with Project Owners","The Ministry of Environment also signed agreements with 61 project's owners on environmental protection.","Ministry of Environment"],[1,"47","2","Monthly Water Quality Monitoring for Biodiversity Conservation","To monitor water quality for biodiversity conservation, every month the Ministry takes water samples along Tonle Sap river (Prek Kdam), up Mekong river (Chroi Changva), down Mekong river (Kien Svay) and Tonle Bassac (Ta Khmav Svay Rolom) as well as water samples from sewage at Boeng Trobek, Stung Chrav.","the Ministry"],[1,"47","3","Natural Protected Areas Master Plan","The MOE has prepared a master plan of natural protected areas covering 18 areas.","MOE"],[1,"47","3","Biodiversity Research and Data Collection","The Ministry is also carrying out research and collecting data on plant species, medicine plants and animals.","The Ministry"],[1,"47","5","Climate Change Response Reporting","The MOE is also working on addressing the climate change issues.","MOE"],[1,"47","6","Environmental Education and Public Awareness Dissemination","The MOE is engaged in providing educational information and discussions on environment issues as well as disseminating this information to the public.","MOE"],[1,"47","7","Mekong River Commission Monitoring and Dialogue","Constant watch and dialogue will be maintained through the Mekong River Commission.",""]],"102":[[1,"58","10","Trade Facilitation through Risk Management Implementation","the Ministry has actively implemented the Sub- Decree on Trade Facilitation through Risk Management which was adopted in March, 2006.","Ministry"]],"103":[[1,"61","9","Private Sector Investment Promotion for Manufacturing Expansion and Diversification","RGC will continue to actively promote private sector investments for expansion and diversification of manufacturing and industrial production to take advantage of the country's natural endowments.",""],[1,"62","2","Business Facilitation and SME Support Package","The planned work ahead will focus on three main aspects, viz., (1) legal framework and adjustment - limitation of procedures of inspection and product justification for import and export without sacrificing essential quality aspects, preparation and adoption of a sub- decree on business facilitation through risk management, and widening registration through internet; (2) financing, creation of a financial leasing company, company classification by credit points, and strengthening governance and financial reporting; and, (3) supportive actions for SMEs - creation of a new business development service, prevention of all kinds of smuggling, subsidies for SMEs for export, and adding SMEs into a global value chain.",""],[1,"62","2","One Village, One Product Movement","Adoption and acceleration of the \"one village, one product\" movement is among many other measures to be pursued.",""],[1,"96","2","Financial Leasing Law for SME Leasing Credit","Promoting the Development of leasing businesses: by encouraging leasing credit activity as an alternative source to small and medium enterprises through establishing a financial leasing law which emphasizes the rights and obligations of contract parties.",""]],"104":[[1,"65","1","Cambodia National Council of Children Coordination Function","The Cambodia National Council of Children (CNCC) has strengthened its activities as a coordinating institution to promote improved cooperation among relevant institutions for children's interests.",""],[1,"65","1","Community-Based Child Protection Network Program","The community- based child protection network program has also increased and reinforced its activities.",""],[1,"65","2","Youth Delinquency and Substance Abuse Rehabilitation Services","The Youth Rehabilitation Department of the MoSAVY has been providing education programs on delinquency and impact of substance abuse to children and young teenagers across the country.","MoSAVY"],[1,"65","2","Residential Rehabilitation and Reintegration Services for Youth Offenders","Children and young teenagers committing offences and abusing addictive substances have been admitted to centers that provide health services, moral education, general knowledge and vocational training to enable them to be reintegrated into their communities.",""],[1,"65","2","Protection Services for Children in Prisons","Attention has also been given to protection for children in prisons.",""],[1,"65","2","Disability Rehabilitation Services Expansion","Rehabilitation services for the disabled are being continuously strengthened and expanded.",""],[1,"65","2","Vocational Training and Employment Support for Persons with Disabilities","Many disabled people have received vocational training in centers and are being employed to earn a living.",""],[1,"65","2","Disability Sports, Arts, and Cultural Promotion","Progress is being made to promote sports, art and cultural movements of the disabled.",""]],"105":[[1,"86","2","Measures to Mitigate Global Economic Shocks for Vulnerable and Poor Households","RGC will take whatever measures are necessary to mitigate the adverse effects of the global developments on the vulnerable and poor, in particular those living in rural areas.",""],[1,"90","2","Targeted Safety Nets for Vulnerable Households","The RGC is therefore taking urgent measures to put in place safety nets through subsidies and targeted labour intensive work programs, like food for work program, to protect the most vulnerable and the poor from the negative impact of external developments on the Cambodian economy.",""],[1,"90","4","Fiscal Stimulus and Social Safety Net Support","the Royal Government has taken immediate steps that have included: a sizeable fiscal stimulus and a sharper focus on support for social safe net programs delivered by ministries and agencies to mitigate the adverse effects of the crisis on the vulnerable and poor segments of the population.",""],[1,"101","8","Targeted Measures to Protect Vulnerable and Poor Households","The implementation of RGC's targeted measures to protect the vulnerable and the poor from the adverse impact of the downturn in the economy",""],[1,"104","8","Expanded Social Protection and Safety Net Response","The short-term actions have focussed on broadening the scope of social protection and safety net programs that are being implemented by various RGC institutions to mitigate the adverse effect of the global crisis on the vulnerable and the poor; implementing fiscal measures to incentivise producers",""],[1,"105","3","Fiscal Stimulus and Social Safety Net Support Package","the RGC is implementing a sizeable fiscal stimulus package and a sharper focus on support for social safe net programs delivered by ministries and agencies to mitigate the adverse effects of the crisis on the vulnerable and poor segments of the population.","ministries and agencies"],[1,"105","5","Social Protection and Safety Net Coordination Strengthening","RGC will continue to strengthen coordination and scope of social protection and safety net programs:",""],[1,"105","5","Emergency Financial Support for Crisis-Affected Communities","In the short-term, RGC strongly encourages all development partners, the private sector, external development cooperation partners, NGOs, civil society organizations, and citizens who are able to provide financial support to communities that are adversely effected by the current crisis.",""]],"106":[[1,"91","7","Agricultural Processing Investment and Trade Facilitation for Price Stability","Fiscal measures combined with other policy instruments, such as increased investment in processing facilities and ensuring fair competition among traders and middlemen by improving road conditions and enhancing trade facilitation will be used to stabilize agricultural prices.",""]],"107":[[1,"107","2","Public Sector Capacity Development Strategy","The development and implementation of a comprehensive capacity development strategy covering all public sector institutions in close collaboration with these institutions is a high priority of the Council for Administrative Reform (CAR).",""],[1,"107","2","Institutional Mandate and Staffing Review","CAR will examine issues related to: mandate of each institution and identify if there are any overlaps in the mandate of institutions; the functional organization of each institution to deliver mandated functions and the minimum staffing levels and skills required to carry out these functions.",""],[1,"107","3","Climate Change Impact Assessment and Disaster Management Capacity Strengthening","Strengthening RGC institutions capacity to identify the implications of climate change, developing a strategy to deal with the anticipated impact of the climate change, and strengthening disaster management capabilities.",""]],"108":[[1,"107","6","Rule of Law and Democratic Governance Measures","Ensuring sustainability of peace, political stability, security and social order through specific measures aiming at promoting the rule of law, respect for human rights and dignity, liberal multi-party democracy in order to create a favorable security and political environment for long-term sustainable development.",""],[1,"108","6","Governance Reform Programme","In the Fourth Legislature, the continued governance reforms by the Royal Government will place importance on the enhanced effectiveness in implementation of policy and delivery and management of public goods, especially a better public services delivery in order to respond to the aspirations of the people.",""],[1,"108","6","Anti-Corruption Reform","The four sides or sub- components of this component of the Rectangular Strategy deal with: (i) fighting corruption;",""],[1,"108","6","Legal and Judicial Reform Programme","The four sides or sub- components of this component of the Rectangular Strategy deal with: (ii) legal and judicial reforms;",""],[1,"108","6","Public Administration Reform Programme","The four sides or sub- components of this component of the Rectangular Strategy deal with: (iii) public administration reforms;",""],[1,"108","6","Cambodian Armed Forces Reform","The four sides or sub- components of this component of the Rectangular Strategy deal with: (iv) reforms of the Cambodian Armed Forces.",""],[1,"108","7","Anti-Corruption Law Development and Adoption","The Royal Government is strongly committed to develop and adopt the anti-corruption law that is consistent with other fundamental laws to ensure coherence and consistency among different laws and their effective implementation, as soon as possible, in close consultation with all concerned parties.",""],[1,"108","7","Fundamental Laws Development and Adoption Agenda","The development and adoption of all fundamental laws has been and will continue to be a high priority of the Royal Government.",""],[1,"108","8","Anti-Corruption Legal and Strategic Measures","While work on the preparation of these laws is underway, the Royal Government will continue to pursue strict strategic measures to eliminate the root causes of corruption through the following interrelated actions:",""],[1,"108","9","Anti-Corruption Awareness and Public Participation Campaign","The Royal Government will continue to raise awareness about all aspects of corruption, including its causes, impacts and consequences to encourage public participation in preventing and fighting corruption.",""],[1,"109","1","Public Service Ethics and Professionalism Measures","measures will be pursued to encourage all levels of government officials to adhere to dignity, morality, professionalism and responsibility in fulfilling their duties.",""],[1,"109","2","Public Integrity and Conflict-of-Interest Reform","The Royal Government will focus on improving its effectiveness in avoiding conflict between the public and private interests by adhering to the principle of incompatibility between functions, especially incompatibility between political and public servant positions; and between political or public servant positions and private activities.",""],[1,"109","2","Reduction of Abuse of Public Office","The Royal Government will also reduce and eliminate the use of public positions, influence and power which blur or bias the decision-making process.",""],[1,"109","3","Freedom of Information for Corruption Reporting","the Government will continue to further promote and protect the freedom to seek to obtain and to disseminate information on corrupt cases in the media.",""],[1,"109","4","Private Sector Integrity and Fair Competition Framework","The Royal Government will continue to develop and pursue implementation of policies, legal and regulatory framework and procedures to protect the integrity of the private sector in order to prevent collusion and to ensure fair competition between private companies/enterprises by ensuring proper behaviour, honourable conduct and dignity in all business transactions.",""],[1,"109","5","Law Enforcement Strengthening Measures","The Royal Government will take strict legal measures against culprits in order to eliminate the culture of impunity, reduce corruption, and increase public confidence.",""],[1,"109","7","Corruption Regulations Education and Dissemination Initiative","Strengthen and speed up the work of education, dissemination of corruption-related regulations",""],[1,"109","10","Anti-Corruption Unit Interwoven Strategy Implementation","To achieve the above objectives, the Anti-Corruption Unit will implement the following interwoven strategies during the Fourth Legislature.",""],[1,"109","11","Anti-Corruption Public Awareness Campaign","Continue to raise awareness about all aspects of corruption, including its causes, impacts and consequences to encourage public participation in preventing and fighting corruption.",""],[1,"109","12","Public Service Ethics and Professionalism Measures","Concrete measures will be pursued to encourage all levels of government officials to adhere to dignity, morality, professionalism and responsibility in fulfilling their duties.",""],[1,"109","14","Public-Private Interest Conflict Prevention Measures","Strengthen the effective implementation of principles in order to avoid conflict between the public and private interests.",""],[1,"110","1","Anti-Corruption Law Implementation and Inspection Capacity Strengthening","Continue to build and strengthen the institutional capacity, including inspection tasks for management and enforce the effective implementation of the Anti-Corruption Law.",""],[1,"110","3","Freedom to Seek and Disseminate Information on Corruption Cases","Continue to further promote and protect the freedom to seek to obtain and to disseminate information on corrupt cases in the media.",""],[1,"110","4","National and International Anti-Corruption Seminars","Continue and expand the organizing of national and international seminars on corruption.",""],[1,"110","5","International Anti-Corruption Cooperation and Partnership","Continue international cooperation and partnership in order to prevent and combat corruption.",""],[1,"110","7","Private Sector Integrity and Fair Competition Framework","Continue to develop and pursue implementation of policies, legal and regulatory framework and procedures to protect the integrity of the private sector in order to prevent collusion and to ensure fair competition between private companies/enterprises by ensuring proper behaviour, honourable conduct and dignity in all business transactions.",""],[1,"110","8","Public-Private Contract Safeguards","Safeguard the balance between the rights and interests in the contracts made between the public and private sector.",""],[1,"110","9","Anti-Corruption Enforcement Measures","Continue to take strict and severe legal actions against corrupt people in order to reduce corruption and to build confidence among people.",""],[1,"110","10","Anti-Corruption Priority Programs","The Ministry of National Assembly-Senate Relations and Inspection (MONASRI) will continue to focus on fighting corruption through its five key priority programs, in particular its inspection program.","The Ministry of National Assembly-Senate Relations and Inspection (MONASRI)"],[1,"110","12","Law Dissemination and Public Legal Awareness Programme","Strengthening law dissemination sector for raising public awareness of the laws, their rights and responsibilities to maintain stability, social order, and rule of law to reduce social poverty and crimes.","MONASRI"],[1,"110","13","Inspection Sector Strengthening and Complaints Handling Mechanism","Strengthening inspection sector and complaints handling in order to fight against corruption, abuses of power and misconducts, ensuring the enforcement of laws and the reduction of corruption, abuse of the law, and misconduct.",""],[1,"111","1","Public Inspection and Complaint Handling Program","for its inspection program: (1). to conduct inspection on the inventory management of the state properties, state income-expense generations and foreign aids, and general management within the line ministries and public institutions; (2). to monitor the law enforcement in the field of agriculture, public works, education, health care, land management, urbanization, and construction, commerce, industry and social affairs; and (3). to receive and handle public complaints.",""],[1,"111","2","Institutional Capacity Strengthening and Human Resources Development","Strengthening institutions and human resources development in order to increase its institutional capacity at the headquarters, and provincial and municipal department to: (1) to continue drafting the laws on inspection, procedure on inspection, and policy on access to information; (2) to conduct training courses on: training of trainer on law dissemination, investigation skill, forensic accounting, human resource management skill, general administration skill, protocol skill, and planning skill; (3) establish Priority Mission Group Projects, and (4) to construct office buildings for municipal and provincial departments.",""],[1,"111","3","Anti-Corruption Law Legislative Approval Support","The Ministry of Justice will continue to provide the support needed to have the draft Anti-Corruption Law, which wer endorsed by the Council of Minister on 11 December 2009, approved by the Legislature.","Ministry of Justice"]],"109":[[1,"118","7","Strategic Plan for the National Police Forces","Pursuit of the development of strategic plan for the National Police Forces aimed at enhancing their effective, commanding roles to fulfil all assigned functions by ensuring management of human, financial and other resources.",""],[1,"118","7","Law on the National Police Forces","The Royal Government will also accelerate the development of the Law on the National Police Forces which will become a guiding framework, enshrining their rights, obligations, duties and responsibilities.",""],[1,"119","2","Security and Rule of Law Strengthening Initiative","the Royal Government will do its utmost to strengthen security and substantially reduce crimes, promote the \"Rule of Law\", enhance the respect for human rights and dignity in all aspects and open up equitable opportunities to Cambodians from all walks of life.",""],[1,"119","3","Promotion of Family and Traditional Religious Values","the Ministry of Religion and Cult will continue to actively promote the role of family and adherence to the traditional religious values of the Kingdom.","Ministry of Religion and Cult"],[1,"119","3","Institutional Capacity Strengthening for Civil and Policing Services","the MOI will focus on strengthening the institutional capacity of national and sub-national institutions with its mandate to efficiently deal with newly emerging situations and to improve the delivery of public services falling within its civil and policing mandates.","Ministry of Interior (MOI)"],[1,"119","3","MOI Organizational and Regulatory Reform","The MOI will formulate a new sub-decree on the organization and functions of the MOI, and amend internal regulations to ensure that its staff on civil and police payroll perform their duties with discipline, neutrality, follow the code of ethics and good order.","Ministry of Interior (MOI)"],[1,"119","4","District-Level One-Window Service Pilot Program","the MOI has been implementing a pilot program of \"One window service\" at the district level in two provinces: Siem Reap and Battambang.","MOI"],[1,"119","4","District Ombudsman Complaint-Handling Mechanism","Under this program the MOI has appointed \"district ombudsman\" who receive complaints from citizens, communities, civil society organizations, and district officials.","MOI"]],"110":[[1,"122","3","Public Financial Management Reform Deepening","The Royal Government will continue to deepen the implementation of the \"Public Financial Management Reform\", especially the second platform of this program in order to enhance the efficiency of the national budget, which is a key tool of the country's development policy.",""],[1,"122","3","State-Owned Asset Management Strengthening","The Royal Government will continue to strengthen the strict management of state-owned assets in accordance with the existing laws and regulations, and to ensure effective collection of revenues from all kinds of state- owned assets.",""],[1,"122","3","Public Administrative Financial Management Accountability Measures","The Royal Government will ensure the efficiency, transparency and accountability in financial management of the public administrative establishments.",""],[1,"122","3","Public Enterprise Management Capacity and Oversight Reform","the Royal Government will place priority on enhancing the efficient management of public enterprises by strengthening the management capacity of the tutelage ministries responsible for technical as well as financial matters, and by adopting business plans, operational guidelines and performance benchmarking and by strengthening control and audit.","tutelage ministries"],[1,"122","3","Public Enterprise Capital Market Readiness Improvement","Attention would also be given to improving the management of public enterprises to enable them to reach the standards needed to mobilize financing from the capital markets.",""],[1,"122","3","Government Contract and Concession Review Oversight","Moreover, the Royal Government will continue to strengthen the role of the Ministry of Economy and Finance in the review and the approval of all government contracts and concession agreements in accordance with the laws and regulations in force.","Ministry of Economy and Finance"],[1,"122","4","Transparent and Accountable Resource Revenue Management","The Royal Government is committed to efficient, transparent, and accountable management of the revenues from mineral, oil and gas exploitation.",""]],"111":[[1,"128","2","Smallholder and Large-Scale Farm Partnership Promotion","The Royal Government will foster partnership between small land holders and large-scale agricultural farms or corporations, and between economic and social land concessionaires, especially those involved in agro- industries such as rubber plantation in accordance with the Strategic Plan for the Development of Rubber, Cashew, and Sugarcane.",""],[1,"128","3","Agricultural Investment Promotion and Market Linkage Mechanism","the Royal Government will create an enabling environment to attract private investors, domestic and foreign, and welcomes the contribution from NGOs to ensure the transfer of know-how and new technology to farmers in regard to crop farming and animal rearing.",""],[1,"128","3","Agricultural Market Integration and Standards Compliance Mechanism","It will further strive toward linking farmers to the regional and global agricultural markets by creating necessary institutional mechanism and through efforts to make the quality of agricultural products conform to international standards.",""],[1,"129","3","Partnerships Between Smallholders and Large-Scale Agricultural Enterprises","Foster partnership between small land holders and large-scale agricultural farms or corporations, and between economic and social land concessionaires, especially those involved in agro-industries such as rubber plantation in accordance with the Strategic Plan for the Development of Rubber, Cashew, and Sugarcane.",""],[1,"129","5","Private Investment Attraction and NGO Technology Transfer Support","Create an enabling environment to attract private investors, domestic and foreign, and welcomes the contribution from NGOs to ensure the transfer of know-how and new technology to farmers in regard to crop farming and animal rearing.",""],[1,"129","6","Private Investment and NGO Support for Agricultural Modernization","Promote and create an enabling environment to attract private investors, domestic and foreign, and welcome the contribution from NGOs to ensure the transfer of know-how and new technology to farmers in regard to crop farming and animal rearing",""],[1,"129","6","Agricultural Market Linkage and Standards Compliance Mechanism","further strive toward linking farmers to the regional and global agricultural markets by creating necessary institutional mechanism and through efforts to make the quality of agricultural products conform to international standards",""],[1,"133","5","Partnerships Between Smallholders and Agricultural Corporations","Continue partnership between the owners of small farming land and plantation and other agricultural production corporation and between economic land concession and social land concession to create job opportunity and market for local people.",""]],"112":[[1,"131","3","Transparent and Equitable Land Distribution and Use Reform","Conduct land distribution and use for private and public with transparency, equity, social stability, food security, and the investment opportunity in accordance with land variety and natural advantage and in response to citizens' requirements in general; and in particular, the requirements of poor people, disabled veterans, families of sacrificed soldiers, and families of armed forces in duties in the front line of the battle field;",""],[1,"131","3","Social Land Concession Programme","through social land concession program, registration for collective lands of indigenous community resettlement program, review of economic land concession with the area disallowed by the land law and not following the agreements and/or without conducting social and environmental impact assessment or without suitable utilization and development plans, through the implementation of Instruction 06 SNN focusing on illegal holding of state-owned lands to take back unused, purchased lands and state lands suffered from illegal deforestation.",""],[1,"131","3","Collective Land Registration for Indigenous Community Resettlement","through social land concession program, registration for collective lands of indigenous community resettlement program, review of economic land concession with the area disallowed by the land law and not following the agreements and/or without conducting social and environmental impact assessment or without suitable utilization and development plans, through the implementation of Instruction 06 SNN focusing on illegal holding of state-owned lands to take back unused, purchased lands and state lands suffered from illegal deforestation.",""],[1,"131","3","Review of Economic Land Concessions","review of economic land concession with the area disallowed by the land law and not following the agreements and/or without conducting social and environmental impact assessment or without suitable utilization and development plans, through the implementation of Instruction 06 SNN focusing on illegal holding of state-owned lands to take back unused, purchased lands and state lands suffered from illegal deforestation.",""],[1,"131","3","Implementation of Instruction 06 SNN on Illegal State Land Holdings","through the implementation of Instruction 06 SNN focusing on illegal holding of state-owned lands to take back unused, purchased lands and state lands suffered from illegal deforestation.",""],[1,"133","2","Land Distribution Planning and State Land Enforcement Framework","Establish and implement the strategy and framework of land distribution plan for middle and long term for land distribution and use targeting social and economic purpose in compliance with national, divisional, city/provincial, town/district, and communal plans with transparency and efficiency to avoid negative impact to society and environment, to prevent land purchase without using, to confiscate illegal- grabbed state lands on the basis of reinforcing efficiency in performing the existing policy and legal framework; above all, instruction circular numbering 06 about state land unlawful grab as well as the strengthen of duty on unused lands.",""],[1,"133","3","Social Concession Land Distribution Programme","Conduct land distribution for social concession purpose to 10,000 families in 2013 to contribute to social issue solution and national defence.",""],[1,"133","4","Review and Regulate Economic Land Concessions","Precisely examine the performance of the existing economic concession agreements as well as economic land concession with the area disallowed by land law and new economic land concession to be granted, basing on sub-decree on economic land concession and permanent legal framework with thorough social and environmental impact assessment, and transparently participated by all related people; especially, at the local grassroots level.",""],[1,"137","14","Sub-decree on Land Provision for Local Communities and Minor Ethnic Groups","Preparing sub-decree on provide land to increase productivity for local community and minor ethnic",""]],"113":[[1,"134","4","National Resource Conservation and Eco-Tourism Linkage Initiative","The Royal Government will further strengthen national resource conservation, especially promoting the linkage of conservation to eco-tourism.",""],[1,"134","4","Illegal Encroachment and Illegal Fishing Enforcement Measures","The Royal Government will continue to take serious action against illegal encroachment of flooded forests, use of illegal fishing gears, and all anarchic activities preventing the conservation efforts, by encouraging participation from relevant local and competent authorities.",""],[1,"135","7","Illegal Fishing Enforcement and Inundated Forest Protection Regulations","Enact and disseminate of law and regulations for enforcement and cracking down on all illegal fishing activities and preserving the inundate forest.",""],[1,"135","9","Community Fish Refuge and Fish Release Programme","Protect the important natural habitats and biodiversity by establishing Community Fish Refuges and releasing fish in fishing lots and major important water bodies in every commune all over the country.",""]],"114":[[1,"136","3","Climate Change Resource Mobilization and Financing","The Royal Government will mobilize resources, support, and financing to participate in global efforts to address challenges of climate change.",""],[1,"136","9","Climate Change Resource Mobilization and Financing","The Royal Government will mobilize resources, support, and financing to participate in global efforts to address challenges of climate change.",""],[1,"137","34","Climate Change Financing and Resource Mobilization","Secure resources, suport and financing to solve climate change problems.",""],[1,"138","6","Climate Change Education and Awareness Campaign","Educate and propagate on climate change",""],[1,"138","7","Completion of the Second National Climate Change Convention Report","Prepare to finish Second National Report on climate change convention",""],[1,"138","8","Greenhouse Inventory Decentralization and Database Management","Decentralise green house inventory and prepare data base management",""],[1,"138","9","Clean Development Mechanism Promotion","Continue define seeking and pushing implement mechanic clean development",""],[1,"138","10","Greenhouse Gas Emission Project Implementation","Accelerate implementation of green house gas emision project",""],[1,"138","11","National Climate Change Adaptation Programme Implementation","Accelerate implementation of programme activities on National climate change adapation",""],[1,"138","12","National Climate Change Action Plan","Prepare a National action plan to respond to climate change",""],[1,"138","13","National Climate Change Fund","Push for the creation of a National climate change fund",""]],"115":[[1,"138","14","Environmental Education and Information Provision","To provide environmental education and environmental information, the MOE will:","MOE"],[1,"138","15","Environmental Education Coordination and Cooperation","Coordinate and cooporate on environmental education for eternity development",""],[1,"138","16","Environmental Education for Sustainable Development Human Resource Development","Stregnthen human resource development efforts for work on environmental education for sustainable development",""],[1,"138","17","Environmental Awareness and Information Exchange Programme","Enhance environmental awareness programme and exchange information",""]],"116":[[1,"141","11","Single Stop and Single Window Inspector Implementation","Fostering the implementation of single stop and Single Window inspector within the scope of GMS with Viet Nam and Thailand.",""]],"117":[[1,"143","4","Irrigation System Management Strengthening","The Royal Government will enhance efficient management of the irrigation system by strengthening the institutional capacity of concerned ministries and agencies.",""],[1,"143","4","Decentralized Irrigation Management and Water User Participation","It will further increase people's participation in the decentralized management and use of the irrigation systems in order to address water issues for cultivation, facilitation of navigation and promotion of aquaculture, and will strengthen the capacity of water user communities.",""],[1,"143","4","Private Sector Participation in Irrigation and Clean Water Supply","Along with use of resources from development partners and its own resources, the Royal Government will encourage private sector participation in the development and the management of irrigation systems and clean water supply.",""],[1,"143","16","MOWRAM Staff and Management Capacity Strengthening for Irrigation and Drainage","Strengthen capacity of staff and management of MOWRAM to implement irrigation and drainage theory and innovation skills.","MOWRAM"],[1,"144","1","Stakeholder Participation in Irrigation and Drainage Project Development","Involve farmers, stakeholders, and private sector to participate in all stages of projects preparation, projects improvement, and irrigation and drainage system development.",""],[1,"144","4","Integrated Water Resources Management Approach","Implementing multi-approaches on water resources management and development thoroughly considering water sources which are linked to other sectors of environment.",""],[1,"144","5","River Basin Development and Management Plan Preparation and Implementation","Increase the awareness and encourage preparation and implementation of river basin development and management plan with the cooperation of concerned ministries, stakeholders and benefit receivers.",""],[1,"144","6","Stakeholder Participation in Irrigation and Drainage Management","Encouraging the participation of Farmer Water Users Community, benefit receivers, and private sector at all stages of development and management of irrigation and drainage system.",""],[1,"144","7","Farmer Water Users Community Capacity Building for Irrigation Management","Improve Farmer Water Users Community (FWUC) capacity on how to manage, maintain, and operate irrigation system through Participatory Irrigation Management and Development.",""],[1,"144","8","Participatory Irrigation Management and Development","Encourage investments from international development cooperation partners and the private sector to support the development, maintenance, and management of the irrigation system through Participatory Irrigation Management and Development.",""],[1,"144","17","Water Resources Management Law Sub-Decrees","Prepare sub-decrees to implement the Water Resources Management Law adopted in June 2007, e.g:",""],[1,"145","7","Farmer Water Users Communities Strengthening and Expansion","Continue strengthening and expanding the Farmer Water Users Communities to participate in water management and distribution to maintain the irrigation system in an effective and sustainable manner.",""],[1,"145","8","Sub-decree on Irrigation System and Reservoir Geographic Mapping","Preparing sub-decree to define geographical map of irrigation system, and reservoir to avoid invasion.",""],[1,"145","17","Administrative Process Strengthening and On-the-Job Training for MOWRAM Officials","Strengthen the administrative processes and provide on-the-job training to MOWRAM officials to meet national and international standard.","MOWRAM"],[1,"145","18","Water Awareness Capacity Strengthening","Continue strengthening capacity of central officials, sub-national level, and FWUC to be aware of the significance of water to daily livelihood and economic",""],[1,"146","2","Gender Network in Provincial Departments","Create gender network in all provincial departments of the MWRAM.","MWRAM"],[1,"146","4","Gender Group Participation in Ministry Projects","Ensure the participation of gender group in all projects of ministry.",""],[1,"146","10","Irrigation Management Capacity Building","Increase irrigation management effectiveness by building capacity.",""],[1,"146","11","Irrigation System Participation and Ownership Mechanism","Ensure the participation of related institutions and the ownership of people in using and managing irrigation system",""]],"118":[[1,"156","12","Tourist Safety and Security Coordination","Work with law enforcement agencies to strengthen safety and security of tourists.",""],[1,"157","2","Khmer Heritage Preservation and Promotion Programme","The Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts will continue to ensure the preservation of the ancient temples and the national museum, and actively promote Khmer arts including traditional Khmer dances, songs and other artistic endeavours; as well as promoting the revival, production and marketing of Khmer handicrafts as an important contribution to support the growth of the tourism sector.","Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts"],[1,"157","4","Temple Repair and Access Infrastructure Improvement","The repair and maintenance of ancient temples, as well as improvements to roads and bridges for easy access to the temples.",""],[1,"157","5","National Museum Repair, Maintenance, and Exhibit Restoration","The repair and maintenance of the national museum as well as the preservation and restoration of museum exhibits.",""],[1,"157","6","Provincial Offices and Tribal Centre Construction","Construction of offices in provinces and a Tribal Centre in North East.",""],[1,"157","7","Cultural Exhibition and Traditional Dance Halls Construction","Construction of a hall to exhibit cultural products and a hall for traditional Khmer dance performances.",""]],"119":[[1,"157","9","Overseas Job Placement Facilitation","facilitating workers finding jobs abroad;",""],[1,"157","9","Labour Market Statistics and Qualification Standards System","development of a labour market statistical system and national qualification standards;",""],[1,"157","9","Labour Market Awareness Campaigns","conducting wide public awareness campaigns on labour market demands in order to assist labour mobility;",""],[1,"158","2","Job Creation and Overseas Employment Support Programme","Strengthen and expand its programs and services to support job creation in both the formal and informal sectors, as well as, strengthen the management of services of its overseas employment program, including the employment permit system (EPS), to enhance protection of workers seeking employment outside the country.",""],[1,"158","3","Studies for National Employment and Manpower Policy Preparation","Carry out studies to support the preparation of national policies on employment and manpower management.",""],[1,"158","4","Labour Market Information and Analysis System","Develop, regularly update, and widely disseminate labour market information and analysis to policy makers and the public.",""],[1,"158","5","Employment Placement Services Expansion","Strengthen and expand employment placement services for job seekers.",""],[1,"158","6","Business Establishment Information System","Develop and regularly update information on business establishments.",""]],"120":[[1,"159","11","Public Service Institutional Capacity Strengthening and Service Delivery Improvement","Strengthen institutional capacity and improve the quality and efficiency of public service delivery.",""],[1,"160","1","Factory and Handicraft Workshop Regulatory Enforcement Strengthening","Strengthen quality and efficiency of enforcement of laws and regulations governing the operation of factories and handicraft workshops.",""],[1,"160","2","Private Sector and Development Partner Partnership Strengthening","Strengthen partnerships with private sector and development partners.",""],[1,"160","8","Information Management and Sharing System Improvement","Improving information management and sharing system and strengthening capacity on information technology.",""],[1,"160","9","Staff Capacity Building for the General Department of Industry","Strengthening capacity of the staff of General Department of Industry through various trainings.",""],[1,"160","10","Industrial Legal and Regulatory Review and Improvement","Reviewing and improving the existing legal procedures and regulations for industry sector aiming at strengthening quality and efficiency of enforcement of laws and regulations governing the operation of factories and handicraft workshops.",""],[1,"160","12","Industry Laboratory Centre Institutional Strengthening and Capacity Enhancement","Institutional strengthening and enhancing capacity of Industry Laboratory Centre of Cambodia for conducting analyses and researches and improving product quality.",""],[1,"160","13","Review and Restructure Departmental Roles and Responsibilities","Reviewing and restructuring the allocation of roles and responsibility of all departments and units under",""],[1,"160","15","Law Enforcement Regulatory Strengthening","Examining the needs for and issuing regulations, guidelines, and procedures necessary for strengthening of law enforcement.",""],[1,"160","16","Legal and Regulatory Dissemination Campaigns","Conducting dissemination campaigns of laws and regulations.",""],[1,"160","17","Factory Concession Contract Management Strengthening","Strengthening the management of factory concession contracts.",""],[1,"160","18","Factory and Handicraft Workshop Directory","Creating directory of factories and handicraft workshops.",""],[1,"160","19","Industrial Enterprise and Handicraft Workshop Inspection and Monitoring","Strengthening the inspection and monitoring pursuant to law on industrial enterprises and handicraft workshops.",""],[1,"160","20","Industry Sector Regulation Implementation Bulletins","Publishing the bulletins on the implementation of industry sector regulations.",""],[1,"160","22","Government-Private Sector Forum Partnership Strengthening","Strengthening partnership with private sector within the framework of the Government-Private Sector Forum.",""],[1,"160","23","SME Sub-Committee Capacity Strengthening","Strengthening the capacity of SME sub-committee to efficiently exercise its role.",""],[1,"160","24","Development Partner Orientation for Manufacturing Sector","Facilitating and providing orientation to development partners in manufacturing sector.",""],[1,"161","2","Priority Industry Investment Regulatory Reform","Issuing laws and regulations necessary for promoting the investment in prioritized industries.",""]],"121":[[1,"165","12","Strengthen Social Affairs Administration for Social Service Delivery","Strengthen the effectiveness and quality of the social affairs administration in provision of social services",""],[1,"165","13","Civil Service Management and Public Administration Reform","Struggle to strengthen good governance and the increase of effectiveness of internal rules at work and promote the management of civil servants according to the co- statutes of civil servants and the principles of public administrative reforms",""],[1,"165","14","Civil Servant Capacity-Building and National Institute of Social Affairs","Increase the enhancement civil servants' capacity through training courses and the establishment of a national institute of social affairs; enhance women's capacity at work and support their decision",""],[1,"165","15","Social Affairs Sector Statistical System","Establish a statistical system for the social affairs sector based on the six priorities set by the ministry",""],[1,"165","16","Information Technology Utilization and Work Activity Information Dissemination","Promote the utilization of information technology (IT) and disseminate information about the achievement of work activities",""],[1,"165","17","Decentralization and Deconcentration Policy Reform","Continue the implementation of decentralization and deconcentration policy reforms through step-by-step transfers of some of the ministry's functions to national lower levels and through the inclusion of social work into development plans at all levels",""],[1,"165","18","Public Financial Management Reform Programme Implementation","Strengthen the implementation of reform programs of public financial management",""],[1,"165","19","Partnerships for Social Services to Vulnerable Groups","Strengthen partnerships with NGOs, national and international humanitarian organizations and other generous people to seek technical, material and financial support for the provision of social services to victims and vulnerable groups in society; strengthen and expand bilateral and multilateral international cooperation and call for the support and participation from development partners in the social affairs sector.",""]],"122":[[1,"167","3","Informal Education Expansion Programme","The Royal Government will continue to expand informal education through literacy and vocational programs, establishment of community learning centres and implementation of equity programs.",""],[1,"168","1","Functional Literacy Expansion","poor students, enhancing teaching and management capacity, strengthening teachers' morality, improving schools' environment (supply of clean water and latrines), and expanding functional literacy.",""],[1,"170","10","Equivalency Program Dissemination and Implementation","Widely disseminate equivalency program and effectively implement.",""],[1,"170","11","Literacy, Life Skills, and Equivalency Program Expansion","Improve and expand Literacy program, life skill and equivalency program.",""]],"123":[[1,"177","3","Small and Medium Credit Support for Women and Communities","the Royal Government continues to provide small and medium credits to women and communities for their livelihoods",""],[1,"177","11","Women's Employment and Entrepreneurship Support Mechanisms","Support and advocate for expansion of opportunities and employment creation for women, including the informal sector by Supporting needs assessments; facilitating partnerships to set up support mechanisms for women entrepreneurs; develop",""],[1,"178","2","Women's Enterprise Development and Support Services","Strengthen business development services to support and develop micro, small and medium enterprises for women by developing and transforming the traditional Women in Development Centres (WIDs) into integrated Women's Development Centres (WDCs) that provide vocational training responding to market needs, along with enterprise consultation and development services, and livelihood skills development for women; designing pilot projects in communities to increase employment opportunities for women, and setting up women's associations and entrepreneur networks; and support access to information on micro finance and credit services for women entrepreneurs.",""]],"124":[[1,"186","8","Institutional Capacity Strengthening for Service Delivery","It includes: resources required to strengthen the capacity of RGC institutions to deliver their programs and services efficiently.",""],[1,"186","14","Institutional Capacity Strengthening for Service Delivery","Support to strengthen the capacity of RGC institutions to deliver their programs and services efficiently.",""],[1,"188","3","Institutional Capacity Strengthening for Service Delivery","RGC also urges development cooperation partners to speedily reallocate resources away from less priority areas now receiving funds, make a serious effort to significantly reduce various forms of \"free standing technical assistance\" and work towards achieving a greater \"net real transfer\" of development resources to the targeted vulnerable and poor beneficiaries, and to strengthen capacity of RGC institutions to deliver their programs and services efficiently to achieve CMDGs targets.",""]],"125":[[1,"194","1","Systematic Measures to Mitigate the Global Financial Crisis Impact","The Royal Government is taking systematic and sequenced measures to mitigate the negative impact of the International Financial Cataclysm and the economic downturn in the advanced economies on Cambodia's financial and economic system, and to protect the hard earned achievements.",""]]}});